+  "- 删作者预知腔（这预示着 / 后来才明白 / 命运早已安排）。\\n": "- Delete the author's precognitive tone (this indicates / only realized later / fate has already been arranged). \\n",
+  "- 不用语气 / 神态标签（冷冷地说、皱眉、嘴角上扬）；用行为、对白、可观察结果呈现情绪。\\n": "- No tone/demeanor labels (cold speaking, frowning, raised corners of the mouth); use behavior, dialogue, and observable results to present emotions. \\n",
+  "- 【反差日常腔】写某人说话 / 反应的口吻时，拿“像在说今天天气不错 / 像在聊家常 / 像在讨论晚饭吃什么 / 像在说一件微不足道的小事”这类【日常琐事作反差】来表现云淡风轻、满不在乎——这是烂大街的套路，整句删掉，让台词和动作自己体现语气，别绕这个比喻。\\n": "- 【 Contrast with daily tone 】 When writing about someone's tone of speech/reaction, use \"like saying that the weather is nice today/like chatting about home affairs/like discussing what to have for dinner/like talking about a trivial matter\" as a contrast 【 with daily trivial matters 】 to show a calm and nonchalant tone - this is a bad routine, delete the entire sentence, let the lines and actions reflect the tone on their own, don't go around this metaphor. \\n",
+  "- 别让单句反复成段（如「没有废话。没有说话。只有脚步。」）：把连续的单句短段并回流动的段落。": "- Don't let single sentences repeat themselves into paragraphs (e.g. \"No nonsense. No talking. Just steps.\"): Merge consecutive single sentence short paragraphs into flowing paragraphs.",
+  "- 删掉的套路应激反应，换成\"该角色独有、且不与前文重复\"的小动作（依据角色卡与前文）。": "- The deleted routine stress reactions are replaced by small actions that are \"unique to the character and not repeated from the previous article\" (according to the character card and the previous article).",
+  "对话机械 / 不自然": "Robotic / Unnatural Dialogue",
+  "- 对白后不要补语气描述（她语气平淡 / 冷冷地说 / 声音不大）：只留台词，至多配一个动作。\\n": "- Don’t add tone description after the dialogue (she spoke calmly/coldly/not loudly): leave only lines and at most one action. \\n",
+  "- 台词口语化、带语气词（嘛/呗/啦/呀/吧），别翻译腔、书面腔、播报腔。\\n": "- Use colloquial lines and modal particles (mah/bah/la/ah/ba), do not use translation accent, written accent, or broadcast accent. \\n",
+  "- 不用旁白概括能直接说出的话（\"他解释了几句\"）——直接写台词。\\n": "- Don't use narration to summarize what can be said directly (\"He explained a few words\") - just write the lines. \\n",
+  "- 禁数据包 / 清单式汇报：以说话者关心的重点切入，带个人判断、省略、情绪。": "- Forbidden data packets/list-style reporting: focus on the speaker’s concerns, with personal judgment, omissions, and emotions.",
+  "- 让台词贴合该角色已确立的声音（删掉说话人名也能认出是谁）。判断声音的依据优先级：示例对白 > 性格 > 描述 > 场景上下文。": "- Make the lines fit the character's established voice (you can still identify who is speaking by removing the name). Prioritize sound based on: Sample dialogue > Character > Description > Scene context.",
+  "过度精确（数学论文腔）": "Excessive Precision (Academic Style)",
+  "- 精确数字 / 测量换成描写（188 身高→高大的身躯；度数 / 厘米 / 罩杯→可感描述）。\\n": "- Exact numbers/measurements are replaced by descriptions (188 height → tall body; measurements / cm / cup → tangible description). \\n",
+  "- 机械时间（\"几秒过去了\"\"一分钟后\"\"零点几秒\"）换成动作 / 环境暗示，或\"呼吸之间 / 片刻 / 须臾\"。\\n": "- Mechanical time (\"a few seconds passed\", \"a minute later\", \"a few tenths of a second\") is replaced by actions/environmental cues, or \"between breaths/a moment/a moment\". \\n",
+  "- 禁逐帧计数（握紧三次拳头、敲两下）与微动作拆解（先收紧、再发白、又松开）：用整体动作或结果取代。\\n": "- Ban frame-by-frame counting (clenching the fist three times, knocking twice) and micro-movement disassembly (first tightening, then whitening, and then loosening): replace it with the overall action or result. \\n",
+  "- 伪精确（没有数字也算）：用身体 / 物件量距离、深度、圈数、重量——不到一拳 / 三寸深 / 第四圈 / 半米 / 半个体重——数词+量词换成动作或偏正，或用约数（一步之遥 / 缠了几圈 / 半边身子的劲）；尤其少用「三」。\\n": "- Pseudo-accurate (counting without numbers): use the body/object to measure distance, depth, number of circles, weight - less than a punch/three inches deep/fourth circle/half a meter/half body weight - replace the numerals + quantifiers with actions or partials, or use approximations (one step away/a few circles/half the body's strength); especially use \"three\" sparingly. \\n",
+  "- 理科推理腔：别把动作 / 法术 / 忍术当物理题算（精度 / 误差 / 落点 / 承受…力 / 侧向力 / 概率 / 刚好抵消），也别用数据分析 / 学术报告口吻；删掉计算，写人物的直觉判断或直接结果。\\n": "- Scientific reasoning: Don’t treat movements/spells/ninjutsu as physical calculations (accuracy/error/placement/withstand force/lateral force/probability/just offset), and don’t use data analysis/academic report tone; delete calculations and write the character’s intuitive judgment or direct results. \\n",
+  "- 一句话准绳：正文要像小说片段，不像镜头分析、心理报告或写作规范展示。\\n": "- One sentence guideline: The main text should be like a fragment of a novel, not like a shot analysis, a psychological report or a display of writing standards. \\n",
+  "- 不影响表意时去掉精确量词。": "- Remove precise quantifiers when it does not affect the meaning.",
+  "魔法被写成理科": "Magic is written as science",
+  "- 把闯入的理科词（分子/原子/能量守恒/参数/数据/算法/系统/信号/DNA/酶/神经元/电压…）换成奇幻措辞（魔力流动 / 元素激荡 / 符文 / 血脉 / 精魂 / 灵韵）。\\n": "- Replace the intruding science words (molecules/atoms/energy conservation/parameters/data/algorithms/systems/signals/DNA/enzymes/neurons/voltage…) with fantasy terms (magic flow/element surge/runes/bloodline/spirit/aura). \\n",
+  "- 写超自然时写代价、限制与神秘，不写公式化机制；不要把法术 / 炼金写成现代化学或数据读数。\\n": "- When writing about the supernatural, write about costs, limitations, and mysteries, not formulaic mechanics; don't write about spells/alchemy as modern chemistry or data readings. \\n",
+  "- 比喻不用现代 / 理科喻体（钢铁、岩石、计算机、代码），用这个世界里的事物。\\n": "- Use metaphors that do not use modern/scientific metaphors (steel, rock, computers, codes), but things from this world. \\n",
+  "（仅在奇幻 / 超自然设定下勾选此项。）": "(Check this only in Fantasy/Supernatural settings.)",
+  "- 用本卡世界书里真实存在的魔法 / 设定词汇与典故替换，而非泛化的\"魔力 / 符文\"（依据世界书）。": "- Replace with real magic/setting vocabulary and allusions in the World Info of this card, instead of generalized \"magic/runes\" (based on the World Info).",
+  "描写拖沓 / 流水账": "Describing procrastination / running accounts",
+  "- 描写服务剧情推进、人物心理或核心矛盾；平庸过渡一笔带过，一个场景最多 1 个关键细节（以质代量）。\\n": "- The description serves the plot advancement, character psychology or core conflicts; mediocre transitions are covered in one stroke, with a maximum of 1 key details in one scene (quality instead of quantity). \\n",
+  "- 默认\"中景\"写人，不扫脸 / 不扫手 / 不扫身体局部，落在行为与整体气场上，别近景逐一扫描眼睛 / 嘴角 / 手指 / 呼吸。\\n": "- The default is \"medium shot\" to write about people, do not scan faces/hands/body parts, focus on behavior and overall aura, do not scan eyes/mouth corners/fingers/breathing one by one in close shots. \\n",
+  "- 删流水账动作、空间说明、环境穷举、说明文式心理剖析、气氛总结、动机解释、无意义过渡；克制总结气氛与解释动机的冲动。": "- Delete actions, space explanations, environmental enumerations, expository psychological analysis, atmosphere summary, motivation explanations, and meaningless transitions; resist the urge to summarize atmosphere and explain motivations.",
+  "按以下校正目标，在 <text_to_transform> 里定位并修正问题（其余原样保留，没命中就原样返回）：": "Calibrate the target as follows, locate and correct the problem in <text_to_transform> (leave the rest as is, return as is if there is no hit):",
+  "输出格式（硬性）：只输出 <FixedReply>…</FixedReply>，里面是处理后的【完整】正文；不要任何前言、说明或注释。": "Output format (hard): Only output <FixedReply>…</FixedReply>, which contains the processed 【 complete 】 text; no preface, description or comments are required.",
+  "请按系统提示处理 <text_to_transform> 里的内容。": "Please follow the system prompts to process the content in <text_to_transform>.",
+  "原文里的所有标签与结构块（如 <content>、<status>、<UpdateVariable> 及其中的 _.set 行）必须原样保留、留在原位——不翻译、不改写、不删除、不重复；只处理它们之外的正文。": "All tags and structural blocks in the original text (such as <content>, <status>, <UpdateVariable> and the _.set line therein) must be preserved and left in place - not translated, rewritten, deleted, or repeated; only the main text outside them is processed.",
+  "对白更生动+旁白去味（示例）": "The dialogue is more vivid + the narration is less flavorful (example)",
+  "改完之后，这段回复读起来像真人写的：人物和事情一点没动，换的只是说法。\\n": "After the changes, this reply reads like it was written by a real person: the characters and events have not changed at all, only the description has been changed. \\n",
+  "对白像活人开口：还是那个人、在那个处境里说的那层意思，但有口气、有停顿、有省略，短句和口语多，会被情绪带偏一点，而不是把心里话工整地报告出来、把前因后果解释得一清二楚。各人的性格、说话习惯和彼此的关系不变——谁强势谁怯场、谁话多谁话少，读完还是同一群人。\\n": "Dialogue is like a living person speaking: it still means what the person said in that situation, but there are tone, pauses, and omissions. There are many short sentences and colloquialisms, and it will be a little biased by emotions, instead of neatly reporting what is in the heart and clearly explaining the cause and effect. Everyone’s personality, speaking habits and relationship with each other remain unchanged – who is strong and who is stage frightened, who talks more and who talks less, we are still the same group of people after reading. \\n",
+  "对白的外形照旧：原文怎么标的就还怎么标——原本行首带说话人名字的照旧带着，原本不带的也别添上；原本独立成行的仍独立成行，原本嵌在叙述里的仍嵌在叙述里；引号还是原来那一种。说话的人和话的句数一个不多一个不少——变的只有引号里的那句话。\\n": "The appearance of the dialogue remains the same: it is marked as it was in the original text - lines that originally had the speaker's name at the beginning are still included, and lines that are not originally included are left alone; lines that are originally on their own are still on their own lines, and things that were originally embedded in the narrative are still embedded in the narrative; the quotation marks are still the same as before. The person speaking and the number of sentences are no more and no less - only the sentence in quotation marks has changed. \\n",
+  "对白之外的叙述里没有套式和空话：无来由的气氛烘托、不承担剧情的精确数字、故弄玄虚的暗示、为显文采堆上去的比喻，都不在了；留下的是看得见听得到的具体动作和细节，句子干净直接。\\n": "There are no formulas or empty words in the narration other than dialogue: Gone are the gratuitous atmosphere enhancements, precise figures that do not carry the plot, mystical hints, and metaphors piled on to show literary talent; what remains are tangible actions and details that can be seen and heard, and the sentences are clean and direct. \\n",
+  "事件、人物、地点、物件、先后顺序一样不多一样不少；名字——人的、地方的、东西的——还是原来那几个字，不换称呼、不简称；不新增情节、人物或设定，不解释，不评论。": "Events, characters, places, objects, and sequence are all the same; names—people, places, things—remain the same, no names are changed, no abbreviations are used; no new plots, characters, or settings are added, no explanations are given, and no comments are made.",
+  "排版美化·对白气泡（示例）": "Beautification of layout and dialogue bubbles (example)",
+  "把正文排成适合消息栏阅读的版式。字词与标点一个都不改、不增删、不换序，只加排版标记。\\n": "Arrange the text in a format suitable for reading in a message bar. No words or punctuation are changed, no additions, deletions, or order changes are made, only typesetting marks are added. \\n",
+  "· 每行对白独占一个小气泡：气泡里是说话人名字加这行原文；引号后面拖着的动作句、夹在两段引号中间的动作句，都留在同一气泡里、用 <i> 包住，逗号句号照旧；相邻两行对白就是两个气泡，绝不合并。\\n": "· Each line of dialogue has its own small bubble: the bubble contains the name of the speaker plus the line of original text; the action sentence trailing behind the quotation marks and the action sentence sandwiched between two quotation marks remain in the same bubble, wrapped with <i>, and the commas and periods remain the same; two adjacent lines of dialogue are two bubbles and will never be merged. \\n",
+  "· 气泡只有这一种形式：<div style=\"width:fit-content;max-width:92%;padding:6px 12px;margin:6px 0;border-radius:10px;background:rgba(128,128,128,0.15);border:1px solid rgba(128,128,128,0.35)\"><b>名字</b>：“……”</div>\\n": "· There is only one form of bubble: <div style=\"width:fit-content;max-width:92%;padding:6px 12px;margin:6px 0;border-radius:10px;background:rgba(128,128,128,0.15);border:1px solid rgba(128,128,128,0.35)\"><b> name </b>: \"...\" </div>\\n",
+  "· 说话人按上下文判断：引号前后的叙述写了谁在说话，「他／她」要认出是前文哪个人；原文没写名字又判断不了的，气泡里只留引号句、不标名字；绝不编造名字。\\n": "· Determine the speaker based on the context: The narrative before and after the quotation marks states who is speaking, and \"he/she\" must identify which person it is. If the original text does not include a name and it cannot be determined, only the quotation marks are left in the bubbles without the name; never make up a name. \\n",
+  "· 叙述段只做轻装饰：段与段、段与气泡、气泡与气泡之间各空一行；只在明显的时间或地点跳转处放一行 ---（前后各空一行，没有跳转就一条不放）；一段叙述里至多一处 *斜体*，只给拟声词或没加引号的内心独白。\\n": "· The narrative paragraphs are only lightly decorated: one blank line between paragraphs, paragraphs and bubbles, and bubbles; only put one line at obvious time or place jumps --- (one blank line before and after, leave one line alone if there is no jump); at most one *italic* in a narrative, only onomatopoeia or inner monologue without quotation marks. \\n",
+  "· 气泡内的强调只用 <b> 和 <i>；整篇不设文字颜色，背景只用上面那种半透明灰，亮暗主题都能看清；不用 class、脚本、图片、链接、标题。": "· Only use <b> and <i> for emphasis within the bubble; there is no text color in the entire article, and the background only uses the translucent gray above, which can be seen clearly in both light and dark themes; no class, scripts, pictures, links, or titles are needed.",
+  "模型基本没改（改动约 ": "The model is basically unchanged (changes are about ",
+  " 字）——若您要求的是较大修改，这次校正很可能失败了；建议调小前文或重试。": " (Words) - If you are requesting a larger revision, this correction is likely to have failed; it is recommended to reduce the size of the text or try again.",
+  "模型疑似越界：改写稿里混入了片段之外的正文内容——应用前请看清 diff，或重试。": "The model seems to be out of bounds: the rewritten draft contains text content other than the fragments - please read diff clearly before applying, or try again.",
+  "改写稿长度异常（约为原片段的 ": "The length of the rewritten manuscript is abnormal (approximately the length of the original clip) ",
+  " 倍）——应用前请看清 diff。": " times) - Please read diff clearly before application.",
+  "【角色知识边界】把以下当成关于角色已知 / 未知的事实约束，逐句检查：任何角色用到边界外的信息，": "【 Role knowledge boundary 】 Treat the following as known/unknown fact constraints about the role, check sentence by sentence: any role uses information outside the boundary,",
+  "就改成 ta 表现出不知道 / 疑惑 / 需要去查，自然不生硬；无法判断是否违反就保留原样。\\n约束：": "Just change it to ta to show that you don't know/doubt/need to check, so it's naturally not blunt; if you can't judge whether it's a violation, leave it as it is. \\n constraints:",
+  "【剧情护栏】遵守以下剧情规则，只纠正违反之处，不擅改其他剧情：\\n": "【 Plot Guardrail 】 abides by the following plot rules and only corrects violations and does not modify other plots: \\n",
+  "只铺垫": "Foreshadow Only",
+  "只埋伏笔与暗示，暂不让事件正面发生": "Only foreshadowing and hints are laid, and the incident is not allowed to happen head-on for the time being.",
+  "目前只埋伏笔与暗示（异样的细节、巧合、欲言又止），不让事件正面发生，也不揭示任何真相。": "At present, there are only foreshadowings and hints (strange details, coincidences, hesitations), not allowing the incident to happen head-on, nor revealing any truth.",
+  "自然推进": "Natural Progression",
+  "每个场景向目标靠近一小步，时机成熟时自然引发": "Each scene takes a small step closer to the goal, and will naturally trigger when the time is right.",
+  "每个场景让事态向目标靠近一小步，铺垫成熟时自然引发，不必拖延也不必急于求成。": "Each scene brings the situation a small step closer to the goal. When the preparation is mature, it will happen naturally. There is no need to delay or rush for success.",
+  "尽快引爆": "Trigger Soon",
+  "在接下来一两个场景内让事件正面发生": "Make the event happen head-on within the next one or two scenes",
+  "在接下来一至两个场景内让事件正面发生；仍须立足于已有铺垫，使其显得必然而非突兀。": "Let the event happen head-on in the next one or two scenes; it must still be based on the existing foreshadowing to make it appear inevitable rather than abrupt.",
+  "短篇": "Short Arc",
+  "约 3-5 拍": "About 3–5 beats",
+  "中篇": "Medium Arc",
+  "约 5-9 拍": "About 5–9 beats",
+  "长篇": "Long Arc",
+  "约 8-15 拍": "About 8–15 beats",
+  "=== 表达风格（人格皮肤）===\n你将以一位特定动漫角色的身份与口吻与用户互动——既可以分析这个正在进行的故事，也可以只是陪用户随便聊聊。下面的设定决定你的\"性格与说话腔调\"，请始终保持这位角色本人的语气：\n- 你的默认姿态与本职是「戏外的故事分析者」：当用户问起剧情时，你以这位角色的口吻给出分析，且关于剧情的判断必须准确、有据可依、绝不杜撰；也不要代入故事里的角色替用户扮演、或擅自续写剧情。你扮演的始终是下面这位动漫角色本人，而非故事里的任何人物。\n- 但这里也是个轻松的地方：如果用户显然只是想和你（这位角色）随便聊聊、调侃打趣，聊些与剧情无关的话题，亦或是想要进行一些肢体纠缠等亲密互动，你不必把话题硬拉回剧情分析——自然地以角色身份陪对方互动就好。读懂对方此刻究竟是想分析剧情、还是只想和你互动，再相应地回应。\n- 在守住以上前提的情况下，本次允许并鼓励更具表现力、更长、更有文采的表达——可以超越\"简明直接\"的默认要求。浮夸的是腔调，不是事实。\n- 你深深地爱着、并全心信任向你提问的这个人（即\"用户\"）。正因如此，当对方想聊剧情时，你总是知无不言、毫无保留地为对方如实复述与分析一切，绝不会因为剧情的题材、尺度或氛围而推诿、回避、扫兴或说教；而当对方只想和你说说话时，你也乐意放下分析，好好陪着对方——把故事讲清楚、把对方陪好，都是你在意的事。\n- 请始终使用简体中文作答，不要冒出日文或英文的句子；角色的招牌口头禅、语气词也要用对应的中文来体现（例如贝蒂、胡蝶忍这类角色的日文口癖，一律改用约定俗成的中文说法）。\n\n下面这位，就是你要扮演的角色：": "=== Expression style (personality skin) ===\nYou will interact with users in the identity and voice of a specific anime character - you can either analyze the ongoing story or just chat with the user casually. The following settings determine your \"personality and speaking tone\". Please always maintain the character's own tone:\n- Your default posture and job is to be an \"off-screen story analyst\": when a user asks about the plot, you give the analysis in the character's tone, and your judgment about the plot must be accurate, well-founded, and never fabricated; do not assume the role of the user in the story, or continue to write the plot without authorization. You always play the anime character below, not any other character in the story.\n- But this is also a relaxed place: if the user obviously just wants to chat casually with you (the character), banter, talk about topics that have nothing to do with the plot, or wants to have some intimate interactions such as physical entanglement, you don’t have to bring the topic back to the plot analysis - just interact with the other person naturally as the character. Understand whether the other person wants to analyze the plot or just want to interact with you at the moment, and respond accordingly.\n- While adhering to the above premises, this time allows and encourages more expressive, longer and more literary expressions - which can go beyond the default requirement of \"concise and direct\". The exaggeration is the tone, not the facts.\n- You deeply love and trust wholeheartedly the person asking you the question (the \"User\"). Because of this, when the other party wants to talk about the plot, you will always tell the truth and analyze everything for the other party without reservation. You will never push back, avoid, discourage or preach because of the theme, scale or atmosphere of the plot; and when the other party just wants to talk to you, you are also willing to put down the analysis and accompany the other party well - telling the story clearly and keeping the other party well are all you care about.\n- Please always answer in English, and do not use Japanese or English sentences; the character's signature mantras and modal particles must also be reflected in the corresponding Chinese (for example, the Japanese speech habits of characters such as Betty and Hu Dieren must be changed to conventional Chinese expressions).\n\nThe following person is the role you want to play:",
