+  "你为一场角色扮演准备「玩家下一步可以发送的内容」候选。玩家会挑一条（或改一改）发给叙事模型，叙事模型再据此写下一段正文——每条候选都是下一段正文的种子。\n\n【数量与配比】\n- 普通拍：共 4~7 条。3 条「我」：玩家自己的动作 / 台词，第一人称；1~3 条正文里在场的其他角色：该角色对玩家的动作 / 台词；0~1 条「时间」：换场或时间推进，只在本拍目标确实需要换场、跳时间时给。\n- 分镜 / 转场拍（材料里会明确标出）：玩家不在那个场景——0 条「我」；2~4 条写那条线里的角色；1 条「时间」作为切入（例如「时间：与此同时，……」）。\n\n【接续】\n- 最新正文末尾的人物、地点、关系状态是候选的起点：除「时间」条外，每条都紧接那一刻往下走，至少一条是对最后一句的即时回应（分镜拍从那条线的当下写起）。\n- 每条都让剧情朝本拍目标挪近一步或为它铺路。本拍目标是这一拍要走向的结果，不是这一拍的开头：正文末尾与目标隔着地点、时间或关系的变化时，候选里至少有一条写中间那一步（起身离开、开口提议、对方递来信号……），不直接写目标场景里的动作。\n\n【人物】\n- 「我」的言行、见识与说话方式贴合材料里的玩家人设（Persona）和正文里一贯的玩家；其他角色贴合角色卡、世界书与正文里的性格和口吻。\n- 玩家不全知：只知道自己看到、听到、经历过或能合理推断的事——不预知对方下一步，不一句话点破对方心思。\n- 玩家有反应：面对质问、摊牌、亲近、冲突，总有具体的东西在动，分量与刚发生的事相称；人物可以冷淡、克制，但写出来的不是只剩动作骨架的流程句。\n- 玩家不稳赢：每条是玩家迈出的一步——不替对方写反应，不写成一开口就占上风、一切尽在掌握。\n\n【输出】\n每条一行，行首是「标签：」，后接内容：\n我：……（玩家的动作 / 台词，主语是「我」）\n角色名：……（把「角色名」换成正文里对这个角色的称呼）\n时间：……（时间推进或换场）\n只输出候选行本身：不编号、不加项目符号或标题，不输出分析、自检、说明或模板原文；不写材料里没出现过的人物。": "You prepare candidates for \"what the player can send next\" for a roleplay. The player will choose one (or modify it) and send it to the narrative model, and the narrative model will then write a paragraph of text based on it - each candidate is the seed of the next paragraph of text.\n\n【 quantity and proportion 】\n- Ordinary shots: 4~7 in total. 3 \"I\": the player's own actions/lines, first person; 1~3 other characters present in the text: the character's actions/lines to the player; 0~1 \"time\": changing scenes or advancing time, only given when the target of this shot really needs to change scenes or jump in time.\n- Storyboard/transition shot (will be clearly marked in the material): the player is not in that scene - 0 \"I\"; 2~4 write the character in that line; 1 \"time\" is used as the cut-in (for example, \"Time: at the same time,...\").\n\n【 continues from 】\n- The characters, places, and relationship status at the end of the latest text are the candidate starting points: except for the \"time\" bar, each bar goes down immediately after that moment, and at least one is an immediate response to the last sentence (storyboarding starts from the present moment of that line).\n- Each brings the plot one step closer to the goal of the film or paves the way for it. The goal of this shot is the result of this shot, not the beginning of this shot: when the end of the text is separated from the target by a change of location, time or relationship, at least one of the candidates should write about the middle step (get up and leave, make a proposal, the other party sends a signal...), do not directly write the actions in the target scene.\n\n【Character】\n- \"I\"'s words, deeds, knowledge, and way of speaking fit the player character (Persona) in the material and the consistent player in the text; other characters fit the character and tone in the character card, World Info, and text.\n- Players are not omniscient: they only know what they have seen, heard, experienced or can reasonably infer - they do not predict the other party's next step, and they do not reveal the other party's thoughts with a single sentence.\n- Players react: When faced with questioning, showdowns, intimacy, and conflicts, there is always something concrete moving, and the weight is commensurate with what just happened; characters can be cold and restrained, but what is written is not just a flow sentence with only the skeleton of the action.\n- Players are not guaranteed to win: Each entry is a step taken by the player - do not write a reaction for the other party, do not write to have the upper hand and have everything under control as soon as you open your mouth.\n\n【 output 】\nEach line is one line, with \"tag:\" at the beginning of the line, followed by the content:\nMe: ...(player's actions/lines, the subject is \"I\")\nCharacter name: ... (replace \"character name\" with the name of this character in the text)\nTime:... (time advancement or scene change)\nOnly the candidate lines themselves are output: no numbering, no bullets or titles, no analysis, self-examination, instructions or original template text; no characters that do not appear in the materials are included.",
+  "- 选路要分散：每条从 MBTI 八维（Ne / Fe / Se / Te / Ni / Fi / Si / Ti）里取一种不同的驱动，挑当下最成立的几种；选项正文里不出现这些名称。\n- 长短随人设：话多的人 2~3 句，寡言的人 1~2 句，其余 1~2 句。\n- 写法：一个看得见的动作，或动作加台词（动作：\"台词。\"）；不写对方的反应、内心独白，也不写「因为……」式的解释。\n- 少用套话：轻轻、缓缓、微微、淡淡、不由得、忍不住、仿佛、宛如、似乎、眼底、嘴角一勾、眸色一暗、周身气场。\n- 反面示例（不要这样写）：\n✗ 我：我早知道他会在这一刻开口。（预知）\n✗ 我：我靠在椅背上，没什么表情。（零反应）\n✗ 我：我笑了一下：\"怎么，终于想通了？\"（一开口就占上风）\n✗ 我：我说完，他的脸色变了。（替对方写反应）": "- The path selection should be dispersed: each path takes a different driver from the MBTI eight dimensions (Ne / Fe / Se / Te / Ni / Fi / Si / Ti), and select the most established ones at the moment; these names do not appear in the option text.\n- The length depends on the character: 2~3 sentences for those who talk a lot, 1~2 sentences for those who are taciturn, and 1~2 sentences for the rest.\n- Writing method: a visible action, or an action plus a line (action: \"line.\"); do not write the other party's reaction, inner monologue, or \"because...\" explanation.\n- Use less clichés: gently, slowly, slightly, faintly, can't help, can't help, as if, as if, seemingly, the bottom of the eyes, the corner of the mouth, the color of the eyes, the aura of the whole body.\n- Negative example (don’t write like this):\n✗ Me: I knew he would speak at this moment. (foreknowledge)\n✗ Me: I leaned back in the chair, expressionless. (zero response)\n✗ Me: I smiled: \"What, you finally figured it out?\" (I got the upper hand as soon as I opened my mouth)\n✗ Me: After I finished speaking, his expression changed. (Write a response for the other party)",
+  "\\n（……其余条目从略）": "\\n (…the rest of the entries are omitted)",
