+  "# 故事神谕（Story Oracle）—— SillyTavern 扩展\r\n\r\n一个可拖动的侧边面板：连接你自定义的 **OpenAI 兼容** 端点，针对*正在进行中*的剧情向 LLM 提问。\r\n问答在它**独立的窗口、独立的历史**里进行——**完全不碰你的主聊天**，随时可清空。\r\n\r\n**它能帮你做六件事**（顶部图标切换，互斥）：\r\n\r\n- 💬 **普通聊天** —— 问剧情：「她为什么这么做」「现在好感度多少」。\r\n- 🩺 **诊断** —— 修 MVU 状态变量（数值 / 状态栏对不上时）。\r\n- 📖 **世界书** —— 聊世界书，或让它**直接帮你改**世界书。\r\n- 🧭 **剧情参谋** —— 一起构思剧情走向，并可**悄悄引导**主聊天（含多拍长线「弧线」与预写「序列」）。\r\n- ✨ **校正** —— 一键修掉最新回复的「AI 味」（手动指定，或自动每条）。\r\n- 🎭 **角色工坊** —— 聊几句就把一个角色从零打磨成完整设定，写进你的人设或世界书 NPC 条目。\r\n\r\n> **v1.89.0（🩺 诊断看得懂「有变量规则的卡」了）**：有些角色卡给变量定了严格的规则（常见的是挂了 mvu_zod 的卡：某个值必须是数字、只能从几个选项里选、某个文件夹不许新增项……）。以前诊断照写不误，卡再悄悄拒掉，你看到的就是「诊断了半天什么都没变」。这版起：① **写入之前先按这张卡的规则预演一遍**——补丁卡上「将修复应用到状态」按钮上方会直接写明「这份修复里有 N 处这张卡不会接受」、每处为什么（比如「主角 › 体力：必须是数字」），应用时只写能过的部分；② 模型写错了的话，诊断会**自动带着原因让它重写一次**（多花一次调用；在「诊断设置」里取消勾选「被拒时让模型自动重写一次」即可关掉）；③ 新增 **「🩺 检查存档」**：存档里要是已经存着一个不合规的值，这张卡之后的**每一次**变量更新都会失败（连讲故事的模型自己写的也一样）——检查会用大白话指出是哪一格、现在是什么、卡要求什么，并有按钮直接在 🎛 变量编辑器里打开那一格。第一次在某个聊天里进诊断、以及一次修复什么都没改动时，它会自动查一次。读取规则靠的是酒馆助手内部的数据；万一哪天酒馆助手更新后读不到，诊断会安静地按以前的方式工作，不会报错。另修一个 bug：打开一个只有开场白的聊天（新建或重新打开），不会再触发自动校正 / 自动诊断 / 修改器了——以前每打开一次就会在开场白上跑一轮（修改器的「每回合 +X」会每开一次加一次）。\r\n\r\n> **v1.88.0（🎛 变量编辑器可以删东西了 + 挑选预设块「重新挑选」不再像没保存）**：① **🎛 变量编辑器**里，页签内的每个文件夹、字段、列表右边多了一个 **🗑**——比如背包 / 储物里不要了的物品条目，点 🗑 标记删除（整行划线变淡，按钮变成 **↩**，点 ↩ 就取消），再按「**应用**」才真正删掉；删错了在诊断侧聊那条「🎛 手动编辑」记录上点「**撤销**」就能整份换回。页签本身（最顶层的大类）不能删，列表里的单项照旧用 ➖。提醒一句：带严格变量结构（schema）的卡，删掉卡片规定「必须有」的字段后，下一条回复可能会被卡自己加回来——那是卡的行为。② **挑选预设块**：点 [重新挑选] 打开时，现在显示的是**你上次保存的勾选和顺序**（以前永远显示默认勾选，看起来像没保存——其实保存一直有效，只是没显示出来；更糟的是再点一次保存会把默认勾选盖回去）。想按预设现在的内容从头挑，点「重置默认」。\r\n\r\n> **v1.87.0 新增（🧭 下一拍建议 —— 序列引导时，帮你想好下一句可以发什么）**：社区插件「下一拍建议」并入了神谕本体（原作者 **棉花娃娃**，感谢授权）。在剧情参谋的「**参谋设置**」里勾上 **下一拍建议**，之后只要**序列引导**在进行中，主聊天最新一条回复下方就会出现一张小卡：点「**生成建议**」，神谕会读当前这一拍的引导、角色卡与你的人设、相关的世界书条目和刚写完的正文，给出 4~7 条你接下来可以发的话（3 条「我」、1~3 条在场角色、0~1 条时间推进；分镜 / 转场拍则不给「我」），**点一条就填进输入框**——输入框里已经有字时接在后面另起一行，**不会覆盖、也不会替你发送**。默认只在你点按钮时才生成；想每条回复自动生成可在「更多设置」里打开（每条回复多花一次 API 调用）。单步方案 / 弧线下不出现。之前装了独立版插件的朋友请把它停用，否则每条回复下会有两张卡。\r\n\r\n> **v1.86.0 新增（🌐 模板广场 —— 下载别人分享的自定义模板，也能分享你自己的）**：校正模式「自定义」面板的模板行多了两颗按钮：**🌐 广场** 打开一个公共模板库，按标签 / 关键字找、点「预览」看全文、点「下载」就存进你的模板下拉并选中；作者更新了会显示「有新版本」，可以覆盖本地那份或另存一份。**📤 分享** 把你当前这份模板填好名字、说明、标签后交给作者审核，审核通过才会出现在广场里（分享出去的模板是公开的，任何人都能下载使用）。下载来的模板就是一段普通文字，和你亲手写的一样，只在你选中它时才会用上。**（目前广场暂停开放、一键投稿已取消；📤 分享改为复制分享文本发到 Discord，见下方「🌐 模板广场」段。）**\r\n\r\n> **v1.85.3 改进（⚡ 长对话记录打开 / 切换更快）**：有朋友反映「打开神谕非常卡」。查下来，神谕窗口里的对话记录越长，载入聊天、切换聊天、切模式时就越卡——以前每画一条旧消息都要让浏览器把整页重新排一遍版。现在整批画完只排一次：200 轮的记录，重画从约 8.5 秒降到约 0.4 秒（电脑实测，手机上差距更大）。另外，旧消息不再在每次开窗时一起重播淡入动画，只有新到的消息才有。功能和外观都没变，无需任何设置。（记录特别长的话，开窗本身仍会慢一些；进一步的优化还在评估。）\r\n\r\n> **v1.85.2 修复（🧭 剧情参谋引导里点名的人物/地点，世界书不认得）**：有朋友反映剧情参谋悄悄引导主聊天时，引导里提到的 NPC、地点这些关键词，居然不会点亮世界书里按关键词触发的「绿灯」条目——模型看不到那条设定，只能自己瞎编一个。原因是这条引导以前注册时没有告诉酒馆「把我也扫进世界书关键词检测」。现在**剧情参谋里提到的人物/地点关键词会触发世界书绿灯条目**了（单拍方案、弧线拍、序列拍都一样，弧线的盲盒模式也一样）；落拍感应那条提示语句照旧不参与关键词扫描，它的措辞太通用，扫进去反而容易误触发别的条目。\r\n\r\n> **v1.85.1 修复（⏎ 手机上神谕输入框换不了行）**：有朋友反映手机上在神谕的输入框里一按回车就发出去了，想分段都没办法（手机键盘没有 Shift+Enter）。现在神谕的输入框**跟随酒馆自己的「用户设置 → 按 Enter 发送」**，和酒馆主输入框一个样：默认「自动（PC）」下电脑 Enter 发送、手机 Enter 换行（点发送按钮发出）；改成「已启用」手机上也 Enter 直接发送，「已禁用」则到哪都只用按钮发。用中文输入法按回车选词 / 上屏也不会误发。\r\n\r\n> **v1.84.1 修复（✨ 校正结果卡里摊出一整份 HTML 源码）**：有朋友反映用「创世回廊」这类卡做整篇校正时，神谕窗口里的**校正稿卡片**是一大片 `<!DOCTYPE html>…` 源码、正文埋在里头（✂️ 选段校正却一直正常）。原因是这类卡的「美化」不是状态栏那种内联小部件，而是**一整份网页**——主聊天里由酒馆助手把它渲成内嵌页面，神谕窗口没有那套渲染器，只能把源码原样摊开。现在神谕认出这种**整份网页型**美化时，校正稿卡片会**改用纯文本排版显示正文**；美化本身一点没少——点 **[应用]** 之后回主聊天照样是美化好的样子。状态栏、天气头、思维链折叠这类内联美化不受影响，照旧在卡片里渲染。\r\n\r\n> **v1.82.0 修复（🎭 角色工坊 · 世界书条目默认只喂启用的 + 条目体积读数）**：有朋友反映工坊「突然开始读整本世界书」——提示词暴涨、请求被服务商以 400 打回。查明是工坊的**选条目器没动过手时会把那本书的每一条条目都投喂出去**，连你在世界书里**已经禁用**的条目（旧版设定、废案、备用规则）也一起发。现在**没勾过的书只喂它当前启用的条目**，禁用条目在列表里也显示成**未勾选**——所见即所得；确实想喂某条禁用的（比如一条停用的「角色生成规则」），手动勾上它就照发，「全选」也仍是连禁用一起发。顺带把世界书模式早就有的**体积读数**搬了过来：条目列表的汇总行现在会写「约 X token」，超过 10 万标红提醒（**只提示、绝不拦截发送**）。\r\n\r\n> **v1.79.0 新增（✂️ 选段校正 · 手机「点选」模式）**：手机上划选老是多选 / 少选 / 光标乱跑、还跟别的划词弹窗打架——现在选段卡在**触屏设备上默认改成「点选」**：全文按句子铺开，**轻点一句就选中这句**（琥珀色），再点别处就换一句；想选好几句，先按 **「扩选」** 再点另一头，中间整段全选上；要精确到字，按 **「微调」**，下面会停靠一块这一句的**大字格**（「开头」「结尾」各选一个字，还有「‹ 一字 / 一字 ›」微推、「完成 / 取消微调」；微调期间下方的钉段和「想怎么改」输入框会暂时收起，按「完成」或「取消」就回来，写好的字不会丢）。选中后照旧 **📌 钉住这段**、写要求、开始校正——点选模式下钉住的段和「想怎么改」输入框都**固定在正文下方的操作条里**，不用翻到文末去找；机制一个字没变（还是按字符偏移只发你选的那几段，其余原样不动；状态栏等结构块在点选里也是普通文字，想选就选，和拖选一样）。整个卡在点选模式下**不会产生系统划选**，所以放大镜、「拷贝」气泡、划词扩展都不会冒出来；手指滑动就是滚动，**惯性滚动中按停的那一下不算点选**。卡片右上角有 **「点选｜拖选」** 开关，随时切回老的划选方式（切换不丢已钉的段和写好的要求）；这个选择只记在**当前浏览器**里（不随账号同步到别的设备）。桌面浏览器默认仍是「拖选」，行为和以前一模一样。另有两处对两种模式都生效的小变化：① 已经钉了段、又选着一段**没钉住**就点「开始校正」，会提醒你**先钉住或清除**（以前这段会被悄悄丢掉）——为此拖选模式的 📌 旁也多了一颗「清除」；② 遇到点不准的情况，可在浏览器控制台执行 `localStorage['so.fixsel.debug']='1'` 后重开卡片，卡底会多一个「调试日志」框，长按全选复制给作者即可。\r\n\r\n> **v1.77.5 改进（🧭 参谋专属设置归位）**：「剧情引导注入深度」和「落拍感应」这两项只跟剧情参谋有关，以前却混在主设置面板的「上下文与世界书」组里，不好找。现在它们搬进了参谋模式自己的「**参谋设置**」折叠组（切到 🧭 参谋模式即可看到，与「套用我的补全预设」同一处）；原来填的值原样沿用，不用重设。注入深度那行顺带多了一句提醒：**模型不听引导时把深度调低，最低可到 0**——数字越小，引导指令离最新一条消息越近、越容易被模型照做。\r\n\r\n> **v1.77.4 修复（🔔 落拍感应 · 与「明月秋青 Myriad Stars」这类预设并用时思维链美化消失）**：有朋友反映开着序列引导时，AI 回复里那段折叠好的思考块没了，整份思维链连同 `</thinking>` 一起摊在正文里；单拍引导却没事。查明是两件事撞上了：那份预设把最后一条「秋青子吃掉了原生思维链」当成**玩家消息**尾置在整个提示词最末（它的作用就是让模型接着 `<thinking>` 往下写，酒馆再把这段折叠起来），而神谕 1.75 起的贴合注入会把落拍协议贴在**最后一条玩家消息的末尾**——正好贴在那句提示后面，提示就不算「最后一句」了，模型改走原生思考，酒馆的折叠也就不认这段文字。现在神谕看到最后一条玩家消息以 `<|…|>` 记号、开口标签（如 `<thinking>`）或一行光秃秃的「说话人:」收尾时，会把协议放到那条消息的**开头**，让预设的提示仍是最后一句；其余一切情形发出去的内容与以前逐字节相同。顺带说明：这种「思考块不折叠」在**模型同时回传原生思考**的线路上是酒馆自身的限制（两种思考一起到时它只留一种），神谕这版只保证不再由自己触发它。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.77.3 修复（🩺 诊断 · 「一个值都没变」时的原因说得更准了）**：有朋友反映每一轮自动诊断都留下同一句——「补丁运行了，但没有任何值发生变化」，底下跟着「① 酒馆助手版本偏旧 ② 这张卡开了 schema 校验（mvu_zod），类型不符的写入会被**整批一起**拒绝」。回去核对变量引擎的源码，这段话有两处不对：**mvu_zod 是逐条检查、逐条丢弃**（不合规的那一条被丢掉，其余照常写进去），而且那句笼统的「环境问题」把**本来能说清楚的失败**也一起甩了出去。这版做两件事：① **照卡片自己的结构定义来判**——变量引擎默认**不允许**往没标成「可扩展」的对象 / 列表里新增项，也**做不了**对文字字段的加减；这两类现在会被逐条点名（「这一层是卡片没标成可扩展的对象 / 列表」「这一项现在的值不是数字也不是日期」）并各给一句照做得了的下一步，不再混进那段笼统提示。② **真说不出原因时，指一条查得到答案的路**——变量引擎自己就会弹提示写明是哪条指令、为什么被拒，只是那个开关**默认是关的**：酒馆助手 →「MVU 变量框架」面板 → 通知 → 勾上「变量初始化/更新出错时通知」，再跑一次就看得到（挂了 mvu_zod 的卡显示的是 `[MVU zod] …`；F12 控制台里也有）。另外提醒一句：挂 mvu_zod 的卡上如果**存档里已经存着一个不合规的值**，之后每一条更新都会被拒——包括讲故事那个模型自己写的——那种情况得先在 🎛 变量编辑器里把那个值改回合规。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.77.2 修复（🩺 自动诊断 · MVU 选「额外模型解析」但不勾「启用自动请求」时没有状态栏）**：有朋友反映「自动诊断开着、MVU 原本的额外解析不开自动请求，状态栏就显示不出来」。查明是 MVU 在这种配置下对新收到的 AI 回复**什么都不做**——既不把上一楼的变量抄过来、也不加状态栏那行占位符；神谕按楼去读，读到的是一份**空状态**，推导出的更新一条都落不了地，于是也就没有补占位符。现在自动诊断会先替 MVU 把这一步做了：这一楼没有变量而更早的楼有，就把最近那楼的状态**抄过来**、把这条回复自己带的更新（如果有）跑一遍、补上占位符，然后照常诊断——状态栏就像官方更新那样出现。**给 MVU 留了三秒半宽限**（它自己有时会慢一拍再处理），它自己处理了就不插手；「随AI输出」或开着自动请求的用户完全不受影响。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.77.1 修复（🧩 与「柚月の记忆」（yuzuki-Memory）插件并用时神谕失忆）**：有朋友反映装着柚月记忆时，诊断模式「不修变量」——问它「状态栏错误」，它却像个客服一样反问你用的是苹果还是安卓。原因在柚月那边：它会拦下浏览器发出的**每一个**模型请求做整理，只要哪条消息里出现它自己的记忆标题（比如「【当前世界状态参考 - 角色档案】」「【前情提要】」），就把那**整条消息**删掉——而神谕把规则、变量状态和剧情记录整段装在一条消息里，剧情里的 AI 回复抄过一次那种标题，神谕的整份提示词就没了，模型只剩你那一句话。神谕现在检测到柚月在场时，会在发出去的副本里给那几个标题悄悄插一个**不可见字符**把它拆开，柚月就不认了；模型看到的文字一样，你的聊天记录、世界书、变量一个字不改。没装柚月的用户完全不受影响（发出去的内容和以前逐字节相同）。普通聊天、世界书、参谋、校正、工坊全都同样受益——它们此前在同样的条件下也会静悄悄失忆。神谕每次发送前还会拿柚月**自己的**清理函数把发出去的副本复核一遍：它日后改了标题也认得出来，会自动换更宽的拆法救下那条消息，并在浏览器控制台提醒一次。\r\n\r\n> **v1.77.0 新增（📋 校正模式第三档「自定义」—— 用你自己的模板处理每条新回复）**：校正模式的下拉多了一档「**自定义**」——写一份你自己的模板（比如「把正文完整翻译成日文」），每条新回复就照它处理一遍，结果照旧作为**新 swipe** 落地、原文留在左边随时划回来；一个聊天里**要么跑校正、要么跑模板，二选一**，不会叠加。模板里**只写你要它做的事**，输出格式与结构块的保留标记由神谕自动附上。「**沿用校正的正文识别**」默认开着（只处理剧情正文，状态栏、变量块原样保留），关掉就把**整条**回复交给模板、输出原样替换；这一档还有自己的保留区 / 丢弃区和最少字数。也可以不开自动，随时点「**用模板处理最新回复**」跑一次。\r\n\r\n> **v1.77.0 新增（✂️ 选段校正的两颗按钮各有一个开关）**：【校正设置 → 手动】里现在是**上下两行勾选**——上面那行（1.44 起，默认**关**）决定要不要在**聊天输入框上方**多放一颗「✂️ 选段校正」快捷按钮；下面那行（默认**开**，行为和以前一样）决定要不要在**最新一条 AI 回复的右上角**放那颗 ✂️——嫌回复上的小剪刀碍眼就取消它，输入框上方那颗不受影响，取消后按钮**立刻**消失、不用刷新页面。\r\n\r\n> **v1.76.0 新增（🎭 角色工坊 · 用户角色（Persona）回来了）**：工坊的「打造目标」下拉重新有了三项：**NPC 世界书条目**（照旧）、**用户角色·抢话**（AI 也会替你的角色行动、说话）、**用户角色·不抢话**（AI 只回应你，绝不替你行动）——后两项把访谈里聊出来的、你自己扮演的角色写成一份给 AI「读」的说明书，可以**完善当前 Persona 的描述**，也可以**另存为一个新 Persona**，写入照旧一键可撤销；两种用户角色各有自己的小节勾选、自己的访谈房间。这版还顺手治了一个老毛病：以前「目标动机」偶尔会凭空安一条材料里没有的野心、再配一句对不上的依据；现在每一行都**先照抄材料里的原句、再写它撑得住的所求**，抄不出原句的行干脆不写——**整个锻造仍然只有一次模型调用**，不多花一分钱。⚠ 下架期间打造目标被统一改成了 NPC，不会自动切回来——想写用户角色请在下拉里重新选一次。\r\n\r\n> **v1.74.2 修复（🧭 落拍感应 · 提示不再一闪而过）**：以前「这一拍可能已落地」的提示只活一条回复——你没来得及点【完成】就继续聊，下一条回复一到提示就没了。现在提示会**一直亮着**，直到你点【完成】处理它、或把当初触发它的那条回复 swipe 掉为止。\r\n\r\n> **v1.74.1 改进（🧭 落拍感应 · 提醒更醒目）**：检测到「这一拍可能已落地」时，【完成】按钮现在会**缓慢闪烁**（v1.73.0 那圈呼吸光太含蓄，容易错过）；如果你把引导条收成了屏角的**指南针小圆钮**，指南针也会同步缓慢闪烁——展开就能看到熟悉的提示和证据句。要不要换拍照旧由你点头，绝不自动推进；系统开了「减少动态效果」的朋友不受打扰（不闪）。顺带修复：从序列切到单步方案 / 弧线时，上一条序列的落拍提示可能残留在引导条上。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.74.0 新增（🩺 自动诊断 · 失败自动重试）**：自动诊断偶尔会有一轮白跑——模型什么都没回（拒答 / 截断）、回了一堆但格式坏得没法用、或者请求本身就没发出去（网络 / 中转抽风）。以前这种回合就只能让它过去，等下一条回复才有下一次机会。现在诊断设置里新增「**🔁 失败自动重试**」勾选（默认关）：开启后这一轮没跑成会**自动再试**，次数自己填（默认 2 次），还可以分别勾选**哪些失败情形**需要重试——**空白回复**（模型没返回内容）、**格式错误**（没能读懂 / 拒收模型给的更新）、**调用失败**（网络错误 / 超时等），三项独立组合。每次重试都会**重新读取当前状态**再发一次请求（不是把旧请求原样重发），进行中的提示会写明第几次重试、点一下照旧可中断；失败的那几轮在诊断记录里也各留一条、末尾标注「将自动重试」。**永不重试**的情形：诊断成功、核验通过无需改动、以及各种安全跳过（你切了聊天 / 状态刚被别人改过 / 你手动点了中断）——这些重试也没意义或不安全。⚠ 每次重试都是一次真实的模型调用，会照常花钱；用中转不太稳的朋友建议只勾「空白回复」和「调用失败」。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.73.0 新增（🧭 序列引导 · 落拍感应——这一拍演完了，神谕自己看得出来）**：用序列引导时，以前每一拍演没演完全靠你自己记得、自己点【完成】。现在序列进行期间，神谕会让讲故事的模型在每条回复末尾**隐形**汇报一行「这一拍进行到哪了」（这行字你在聊天里完全看不到，只给神谕读）；当模型报告「这一拍已经在正文里发生了」、且它引用的那句原文**真的能在回复里找到**时，方案条上会亮出提示「**这一拍可能已落地——完成？**」（悬停可看证据句）、【完成】按钮开始呼吸——**换不换拍仍然由你点头**：不理它就一直原样，**绝不自动推进**。整个检测**零模型调用**（搭的是本来就要发生的那次回复的便车），换拍照旧不花一分钱。设置里新增「**落拍感应（自动提示当前拍可能已完成）**」勾选（默认开；关掉后与 v1.72.0 行为完全一致）。⚠ 两点须知：① 模型偶尔会忘了汇报（尤其序列刚开始、上下文里还没有先例的第一拍）——那就是没提示而已，照旧手动点【完成】；② 个别卡片自带的正则若把这行隐形汇报吃掉，感应会失灵但**不影响任何其它功能**。卸载扩展后若想清掉它注册的显示正则，到「扩展 → 正则」删掉「故事神谕 · 落拍感应隐藏行」即可。\r\n\r\n> **v1.72.0 新增（🧭 序列引导 —— 把聊出来的一整段长线剧情排成「拍列表」，一次采用、逐拍推进）**：以前和参谋聊完一整段长线（比如「魔法学校第一学年」里想经历的十件事），要么拆成十个单步方案一个一个采用，要么开一条弧线、每换一拍都花一次模型调用现编。现在参谋会把这类讨论直接排成**一条有序的拍列表**：每一拍都有自己的目标、起始迹象和契合点，**全部摊开给你看**，点【开始序列引导】一次采用。之后**同一时间只有当前这一拍在引导主聊天**，你觉得这拍演完了就点【完成】换下一拍——**换拍不调模型、不花一分钱**（内容早就写好了）。方案条上会显示「第 X / Y 拍」和一张**拍列表**：✓ 已完成 / ▶ 进行中 / ○ 待播 / ⤫ 已跳过，点任意一行看它的完整内容；**待播的拍可以直接 ✏️ 改注入内容，也可以【跳过】**。想大改（重排、增删、换个方向）就点【💬 找参谋改改】——**当前这一拍照常引导着，什么都不会被拆掉**，窗口自动打开、回到参谋房接着聊；聊好后参谋会把**剩余的拍**重新列一遍，采用它就只替换从当前拍往后的部分，**已经玩过的历史一拍都不动**。整条不想要了点【放弃】（会先问一次）。⚠ 一条聊天同一时间只能有一个引导构件：采用序列会替换掉正在跑的单步方案 / 弧线，反过来也一样（丢东西之前都会先问你）。\r\n\r\n> **v1.71.1 修复（🩺 自动诊断 · 两个用户实报）**：① **诊断写入后，消息上的正则 / 美化不再被刷掉**。以前自动诊断一写入（或刷新状态栏），正则、卡内美化的界面会变回素文本，要刷新浏览器或点 MVU 的「重新处理变量」才能回来——根因是我们重渲染后只广播了一种刷新事件，而美化生态普遍监听的是**另一种**（酒馆助手自己每回合发的那种）；现在两种都发。② **「没能读懂模型的回复」的记录能看完整回复了**。记录里的回复摘要只显示开头 3 行；被截过（末尾 …）时，记录上会多一枚「**查看完整回复**」按钮，点开就地展开模型回复原文，再点收起。按钮在**本次会话内**有效，重载后记录只剩摘要（与「撤销」按钮同一规则——完整原文不写进存档，免得反复失败把聊天档撑大）。另外：摘要**没有**被截时，标签现在写「模型回复全文（模型只返回了这些）」——以前一律写「模型回复开头」，有用户误以为是记录把回复截断了；其实那种情况多半是模型 / 中转真的只返回了那么一点（常见于思维链吃光了回复 token）。\r\n\r\n> **v1.71.0 新增（🧭 弧线的注入指令也能 ✏️ 手动编辑了）**：有朋友反映：弧线引导走到下一拍时，对这一拍的细节不太满意，却**找不到改的地方**——「换个思路」重掷出来的还是差一点。现在弧线（透明与盲盒都行）的方案条上也有 **✏️**：点开就是**当前这一拍**实际注入主聊天的那段幕后指令，想补的细节、想禁的写法直接写进去，【保存】立刻生效、刷新不丢；【恢复默认】随时找回自动生成的版本。走到下一拍会现编一段新指令——看不顺眼照样点 ✏️ 再改。规则与单步方案的编辑完全一致（「节奏：」行保持原样时强度档照常可切）。**盲盒玩家注意**：点 ✏️ 会直接看到幕后指令（含剧透），想保住盲盒体验就别点它；编辑只改注入的文字，给你看的任务和「✓ 目标已达成」的判定都不受影响。\r\n\r\n> **v1.69.0 修复（🩺 自动诊断 · 更新没生效时会重新算一遍）**：讲故事的那个模型偶尔会把变量更新区块**写坏**——少一个 `</JSONPatch>` 闭合标签、标签里多打了一个空格、几条指令里混进一条格式不对的、整块都是引擎不支持的「改名」指令、或者路径统统多写了一层。这几种情况下，**变量引擎一条都没执行**：你的数值和状态栏就停在原地，看起来像「卡住了」。而自动诊断以前只会问「这条回复里**有没有**更新区块」——看见有，就当它**已经生效**，只做核验；它甚至会明确告诉诊断模型「这些变化都已经算进去了，别再重算」。于是诊断模型每回合都老实回答「没什么要改的」，那个由讲故事的模型亲手造成的冻结**永远修不好**（2026 年 8 月一位用户的存档就是这么冻了一整段剧情）。现在自动诊断问的是另一个问题：「变量引擎这一回合**到底执行了没有**」。三种结果三种做法——真执行了就照旧只核验（**绝不重算，同一笔算两次的老毛病一点没放松**）；正文里根本没有更新区块，照旧据剧情推导补上；**区块在、但一条都没执行**，就据剧情**重新推导**这一回合的全部更新，并明确告诉诊断模型「那个区块没有生效」。这一支**绝不往消息正文里再塞一个更新区块**（那一楼里已经躺着一个坏的了，再加一个会把多数卡片的状态栏整个吞掉），只把变量写进去并刷新状态栏。**顺带修好**：如果卡片甩出来的是**不带任何外层包装**的 `<JSONPatch>` 区块（注意没有下划线），神谕以前认不出来、于是把这一回合的变化**又推导了一遍**——花掉的钱扣两次、好感度加两次（和 v1.40.2 修过的是同一类毛病，只是形态更隐蔽）；现在认得了。\r\n\r\n> **v1.68.0 新增 / 修复（🩺 诊断 · 改名搬家真的能落地了 + 少写一个标签也救得回来）**：这版是拿 **768 次真实测试**（6 张真卡 × 4 种模型 × 8 类改动指令）跑出来的错误清单一条条修的，四件事：① **「改名 / 搬家」不再石沉大海**——模型碰到「把某个字段改个名字」这类要求时，最爱写一条 `move` 指令（这在 JSON 规范里确实最合适）。可**酒馆助手的变量更新引擎压根没实现 `move`**：指令被认下来、然后被**默默丢掉**，你看到的就是「跑完了但什么都没变」，而神谕以前还会把锅甩给「酒馆助手版本太旧」。现在神谕会在落地前把它**自动拆成两步**（先在新名字下建好、再删掉旧的，值原样搬走，连 `[数值,\"说明\"]` 那种带说明的字段也一起搬）——**只在能确认「旧的确实在、新位置的上一层也在」时才动手**，确认不了就原样放过、并**明说这条动词引擎不支持**、让你重新诊断一次。这是本次测试里的头号失败原因（768 次里 37 次）。② **模型少写一个 `</JSONPatch>` 也救得回来**——有些模型（尤其是 Gemini 系）指令都写对了、就是漏了最后那个闭合标签，于是整块修正**谁都读不到**，神谕只能报「没读懂模型的回复」。现在只要**指令本身是完整的**，神谕会把缺的那个标签补上，修正照常落地（补不齐、或补了也不合规就一个字不碰）。③ **指令列表的方括号写坏了，不再谎报「无需改动」**——模型偶尔会忘了给指令列表包上 `[ ]`、或者开了 `[` 忘了收尾。以前这种情况神谕解析不了，却会在记录里写「**已检查最新回复，本回合无需改动**」——那几条**本来是对的**指令就这么被悄悄扔了。现在这种坏损会先尝试补齐（能补就照常落地），补不了也会**如实告诉你「JSON 缺了括号之类的东西，没能解析——未写入任何值」**并请你重新诊断，绝不再冒充「无需改动」。④ **一条回复里出现两个更新区块 → 直接拒绝并请你重掷**——这种情况下同一笔改动可能被**执行两次**，而且多数卡片的状态栏会被**整个吞掉**（这是已知的显示地雷）。神谕不会替你合并、也不会挑一块执行，而是一个字都不写、把原因说清楚，请你再点一次「诊断」。\r\n\r\n> **v1.67.0 新增 / 修复（🩺 诊断 · 补丁写错了就当场掰正，没生效就说清为什么）**：有用户点「应用」后看到自相矛盾的一句——「**补丁运行了，但没有任何值发生变化 —— 未写入**」，底下四条却写着「**没能从状态变化里判断（可能已生效也可能没有）**」。既然确定一个字都没写，就不该再说「可能已生效」。这版做了两件事：① **落地前先体检并自动掰正**——神谕在把补丁交给 MVU **之前**会照 MVU 自己的规矩把补丁过一遍，把模型常犯的写法当场修好：动词写成 `set` / `update` / `修改`（MVU 只认 `replace` / `delta` / `insert` / `remove` / `move`）、路径末尾多写一个斜杠、`delta` 的增量写成 `\"+5\"` 这种字符串、`[数值,\"说明\"]` 字段被整对写回去（MVU 只认第一格）、`<JSONPatch >` 标签里多打了一个空格（MVU 就此完全看不见这块）、以及 v1.66.1 已经在修的「路径多写一层 `stat_data`」。另外，补丁里只要混进**一条格式不合规的条目**，MVU 就会把**整块指令一起丢掉**——现在那种条目会被单独剔掉、其余照常落地，状态行会告诉你剔了几条。每一类都只在**有证据**时才动手（改过之后才对得上你当前的变量），否则一个字不碰。② **没生效就说清为什么**——「一个值都没变」时，每条指令都会给出**确定的原因**（这个路径状态里没有 / 本来就是这个值 / 动词 MVU 不认识 / 值的类型对不上……）**外加一句下一步该怎么办**，不再出现「可能已生效」。如果补丁本身**完全合规却仍然零变化**，会直接点出真正的两种可能：**酒馆助手（MagVarUpdate）版本偏旧或没正常工作**，或**这张卡开了 schema 校验（mvu_zod）、类型不符的写入会被静默拒绝**——并告诉你怎么自查（先看看平时正常聊天时这张卡的变量会不会自己变）。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.66.1 修复（🩺 诊断 · 补丁写错了「根」也能落地）**：有用户点「应用」后看到「**已应用（29 条指令中 0 条生效）**」，底下每条都写着「路径不存在」——原因是模型把每条路径都多写了一层 `stat_data`（写成 `/stat_data/世界/时间`，而 MVU 认的是 `/世界/时间`），于是一条都没打中。现在神谕会在把补丁交给 MVU **之前**核对一遍：确认这条路径**只是多写了这一层**（去掉之后才对得上你当前的变量）时自动掰正，修正照常落地；对不上就原样放过、绝不瞎改（少数卡的变量里**真有**一个叫 `stat_data` 的项，那种卡一个字都不碰）。顺带修好了另一处**误报**：改动**列表里某一项**（比如「今日待办」的第 2 条的状态）本来就生效了，却会被报成「没能从状态变化里判断」，现在如实显示为已生效。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.52.0 新增（📖 世界书 EJS 模板渲染，opt-in）**：如果你的世界书条目里写了「提示词模板」（ST-Prompt-Template）扩展的 `<% %>` 模板（比如按好感度切换人设的动态条目），神谕以前读到的是**模板原文**——那些模板只在主聊天生成时才执行，所以神谕\"看得到但看不懂\"。现在在「设置 → 世界书 / 知识库」下勾选「**支持读取 EJS 世界书条目**」，神谕在**普通问答 / 剧情参谋 / 手动校正**读世界书时就会先把模板跑一遍，看到**与主聊天完全一致的成品文本**（变量值、条件分支都是真的），顺带还更省 token。需已安装「提示词模板」扩展；没装时勾了也会自动按原样读取、零副作用。⚠ 一点须知：含「**写**变量」（setvar 等）的条目会因此被**额外执行**、可能影响卡内变量——遇到异常关掉本项即可（默认就是关的）。诊断 / 世界书编辑 / 角色工坊 / 弧线 / 插件接口**有意不执行**模板（各有各按原文处理的理由，比如编辑模式改的就是模板原文本身）。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.51.0 新增（🖥 全屏阅读）**：标题栏 ✕ 左边多了一枚**全屏**图标（⛶）——点它把神谕窗口铺满整个屏幕，长对话读起来不再挤在小悬浮窗里；再点一次（图标变成收缩样）或按 **Esc** 即退出，回到原来的悬浮窗口（**位置 / 大小原样保留**）。手机、桌面都能用；纯显示切换、不动聊天内容，刷新页面回到悬浮窗口。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.49.0 新增（📖 世界书选择框加了「书名搜索」）**：世界书 📖 和角色工坊 🎭 的**选书列表**上方各多了一个搜索框——书多的时候（几十上百本）直接输入书名里的关键字就能筛出来，不用在一长串里翻找了（和条目列表早就有的筛选框是一对）。它**只缩小显示范围**，不改动你已经勾选的书；清空搜索框即恢复整列，没有匹配时会提示「没有匹配的世界书」。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.47.0 新增（✨ 校正目标的指令文本开放自定义）**：设置「系统提示词」下拉里新增一项「校正目标」——选中后下方出现第二个下拉，包含自动校正的五个目标（八股 / 对话 / 设定 / 魔法 / 详略），可逐个查看、改写它们的指令文本（留空 = 用内置版，随更新自动改进；「↺ 重置为默认」一键复原）。规则很简单：**勾选该目标才发送；自定义后整份原样发送**——内置版「有角色卡 / 前文 / 世界书依据时才追加第二段」的机制对自定义不再适用，你写什么就发什么（方括号标题由程序自动加）。两点须知：① 自动校正在调用前有一道**按内置目标含义**做的省钱预筛，把某个目标改写成与原含义无关的东西后，回复里没有内置检测器认得的迹象时会照旧判「无需校正」跳过，你的自定义文本就没机会出场；② 把内置文本**原样复制**进编辑框保存并不等于「没改」——保存即成自定义、两段式依据机制即失效，想回到智能档请点重置。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.46.0 新增 / 修复（四件事）**：① 📱 **触屏设备切换模式不再自动弹出输入法**——以前每切一次模式（世界书 / 参谋 / 校正 / 工坊 / 诊断，进和出都算）神谕都会自动把光标放进输入框，手机上就是软键盘「啪」地弹出来打断操作；现在触屏设备一律不自动聚焦（你点输入框时键盘自然弹出），桌面鼠标党手感不变，横屏手机 / 平板也认得出来（按指针类型判断，不看屏幕宽度）。② 🧭 **参谋方案区块容错**——模型偶尔把方案块标签写歪（比如闭标签写成 `</story_plan>`）或方案被截断没写完时，以前这块方案**看得见却点不了**（渲染出来了、采纳卡不出）；现在标签变体与截断方案都能照常出「开始引导」卡。③ 📖 **柏宝书摘要触达更广**——勾了「附带柏宝书历史剧情摘要」后，**世界书模式**（勾「同时带上最近剧情对话」时，此时运行概要也一并带上）与**已注册的插件模式 / 二创**（如大纲版，经接口读取故事记录时）现在也能读到被隐藏旧楼的摘要；诊断模式有意不接。④ ✨ **自动校正的提示词开放自定义**——设置「系统提示词」下拉里新增「自动校正 · 轻校」与「自动校正 · 精校」两项，和普通 / 诊断 / 世界书 / 参谋一样可改可复位（留空 = 用内置版，随更新自动改进；精校自定义后对两种「侧重」都生效）。注意自定义时保留输出格式要求（`<FixedReply>` 等区块），丢了校正结果将无法被解析应用。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.45.0 新增（🎨 窗口配色三档）**：⚙ 设置 →【界面】里多了「窗口配色」——**深色**（新装默认）、**浅色**、**跟随酒馆主题**（旧行为）。深色 / 浅色是固定配色，不受酒馆主题影响；如果你的美化主题是毛玻璃风格、导致神谕窗口里的字被后面的聊天透上来糊掉，切到深色或浅色即可（这两档会连毛玻璃一起关掉，主聊天再也渗不进来）。皮肤覆盖神谕画出的一切——主窗口、浮动方案条、实时输出窗、四张覆盖卡。**老用户升级后保持「跟随酒馆主题」，外观不会有任何变化**，想换再自己换。\r\n\r\n> **v1.44.0 新增（✂️ 输入框上方的「选段校正」快捷按钮 —— 默认关）**：在【校正设置 → 手动】里新增一个开关，勾上后聊天输入框上方那一排（和快速回复按钮同一排）会多出一颗「✂️ 选段校正」。在主聊天正文里划选一段再点它，就直接开窗、切到校正模式、把那段预先选好——省掉「开窗 → 切模式 → 再找一遍那段」的来回。什么都不划直接点也行，等于一键打开选段卡。按钮外观跟随你的主题，与旁边的快速回复按钮一致；没装快速回复扩展的话会自建一条同款的按钮条，关掉开关时一并收走。\r\n\r\n> **v1.43.1 修复（🎭 工坊：聊天里改出来的整稿会凭空消失）**：在工坊里让访谈师**整篇重写**一份角色稿时（比如「不要小修小补，给我一版重置的」），它给出的是一整份草稿而不是逐句小改——而神谕以前**接不住**这种草稿：稿子只印在聊天里，顶部的常驻卡纹丝不动，一直停在「已有访谈汇总（草稿还未生成）」，而且**一声不吭**（用户书亦报告）。现在这种整稿会**照常收进常驻卡**（自动展开工坊面板，跟点「🔨 生成」出稿一样，可以接着改、接着「写入」）；若它写的草稿格式不全（比如漏了机器读的头部行），也会**明说没收下、给出原因**，不再静默丢掉——你原来那份草稿也不会被这种半成品冲掉。\r\n\r\n> **v1.43.0 新增**：诊断 🩺 也能「套用我的补全预设」了。诊断设置里新增一个复选框，勾上后诊断指令会叠加在你策展好的补全预设之上（**手动诊断与自动诊断都生效**）——和世界书 / 参谋 / 工坊 / 校正一样，主要给模型拒绝做变量审计时破限用（诊断读的是主聊天正文，内容敏感时带审查的模型照样会拒绝）。若你在预设下拉里选的是**内置破限**，它同样跟着这个复选框走。默认关；预设的额外内容会分散模型注意力、影响诊断精度，不需要就别开。\r\n\r\n> **v1.42.0 新增**：主聊天快捷入口——最新一条 AI 回复的消息按钮行会出现一个 ✂️ 按钮——在正文里划选一段文字后点它（装了「右键消息菜单」类扩展的话，右键菜单里也会自动出现「选段校正」），神谕会自动打开窗口、切到校正模式，并把你划选的那段在选段卡里预先选好、滚到眼前。没划选直接点也行＝一键打开选段卡。若正文被翻译类扩展改写、或选的是状态栏里的字，定位不到原文时卡会照常打开并提示你在卡内重新划选（绝不会错选乱改）。若当时有回复正在生成，会先弹「仍要切换吗」确认——点取消则一切原样不动。\r\n\r\n> **v1.41.0 新增（🩺 把诊断修正写进正文 —— 默认关；1.65.0 起住在「诊断设置」栏、去掉「实验性」标注）**：自动诊断的修正一直只写进 MVU 的**实时状态**、不动消息正文。于是只要点一下 MVU 的**「重新处理变量」**（它会把那一楼的变量清空、只照消息正文重新算一遍），这次诊断的修正就**没了**——用户 smallmj 报告：他要靠这个按钮让智绘姬的插图加载出来，于是陷入「重新处理→修正丢→重新应用→插图又卡住」的死循环。**诊断模式的「诊断设置」栏**里有「**把诊断修正写进正文**」（默认关；1.65.0 起从「界面」组移到这里，与自动诊断勾选框做邻居）：勾上后，修正会作为一小段补丁写进这条回复**已有的那个更新区块内部**（不是另起一块——那会让多数卡片的状态栏被折叠面板吞掉），于是无论点多少次「重新处理变量」，算出来的都是修正后的结果。写进去的是**实际算出来的结果值**而不是「加多少减多少」，所以重算多少次都落在同一个数上。**注意**：自动诊断与手动「🩺 诊断」点「应用」都会写进正文；**非必要请保持关闭**。**顺带修好**：以前点「撤销此次修复」只还原变量、却把写进正文的那段留着，下次「重新处理变量」又会照着它算回来 = 撤销等于白撤（推导补块那条路一直如此）；现在撤销 / 重新应用都会**连正文一起**同步。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.40.2 修复（🩺 自动诊断把同一笔变化算两次）**：如果你的卡片用的**不是** MVU 那套标准 `<UpdateVariable>` 标签，而是自己的写法（比如 `<update>` ＋ `<json_patch>`），神谕以前**认不出**它——于是每回合都误判成「这条回复还没更新过变量」，自己照剧情**又推导了一遍**，跟主模型那份叠在一起：**花掉的钱扣两次、好感度加两次**（用户 smallmj 报告）。现在更新区块的识别**不再写死一种标签**，卡片自定义的写法也认得；并且判断改成**宁可只核验、不轻易推导**——只要看出这条回复里**有**更新（哪怕格式不标准、我们摘不干净），就一律只做核验，绝不重算一遍。真的一个更新块都没有时，才照旧推导补上（「替代 MVU 额外模型解析」这个用法不受影响）。**顺带修好的两处**：① 这类卡片的更新块以前会**漏剥**，原样混进普通聊天 / 剧情参谋的上下文里（增量数字会误导模型瞎报数值）；② 开了**自动校正**时，换成校正稿的那一版**会把卡片的更新块弄丢**。另外，自动诊断发出去的提示词现在也能在「**调试提示词**」面板里看到了。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.37.0 新增（✂️ 选段校正 · 多段钉选——一次改好几段）**：选段校正现在能**一次钉住好几段**分开改。在弹出的全文里划选一段、点 **📌 钉住这段**（最多 8 段），每段下面各写一句「这段怎么改」——**留空就用上面的整体要求**；钉好的段在原文里标**冷蓝色**、正在划选的那段仍是琥珀色。段数会**如实报价**：没钉或只钉一段还是老样子「开始校正」，钉了 2 段起按钮变成「开始多段校正（N 段，N 次调用）」。点下去后**每段各发一次调用**（最多 3 路并行、其余排队），改完给一张**逐段清单**——每段各有 **[看改动]** diff、各自打勾决定采不采用，标题如实写「改了 X 段 / 保留 Y 段 / 失败 Z 段」，失败的段还有 **[重试失败的 Z 段]** 一键重发（沿用原来那次的请求，不重新抓上下文）。确认后**代码按字符偏移把各段一次性精确回插**（从后往前拼、段落之间绝不错位），原回复照旧留在左滑、不破坏存档。**你没钉住的文字一个字都不进模型**，从机制上就不可能被改动。**只钉一段（或不钉、直接划选一段）时，行为和旧版选段校正完全一致。**\r\n>\r\n> **v1.36.0 新增（⏳ 生成中切模式先确认 + ✂️✂️ 深度精简后台保活）**：两件事，都是治「切模式把正在生成的回复切没了」。① **切换模式的中断确认**——以前有回复正在生成时点别的模式按钮，这条回复会被**直接中止丢弃**（各模式侧聊房间独立、在途回复切走即作废——这是设计行为，但容易误当 bug）。现在会先弹一个确认框「当前还有回复正在生成——现在切换会中止它，未完成的内容将丢弃」，确定才切、取消留在原地。② **深度精简享受锻造同款后台保活**——「✂️✂️ 深度精简」是和锻造一样的多分钟重调用，以前切个模式就把它中止、白花钱；现在切走后它在后台照常跑，回到工坊时流式气泡自动接上，完成后成稿按原始房间落盘归位（所以它也不会触发上面的确认框）。两点不变：生成期间发送键是 ⏹ 停止键（点它仍会中止后台调用）；**切换聊天**仍会中止一切在途调用（结果属于旧聊天，不会写进新聊天）。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.34.1 修复（✨ 思维链兜底加强 · 只剩 `</think>` 的思考也剥得掉）**：有些预设会把 `<think>` 开标签**预填在发给模型的消息里**（有些推理模型也会省略开标签），于是模型回复里**只剩一个 `</think>` 闭标签**、前面一整段思考被当正文直接吐出来——神谕以前遇到这种「只有闭标签」的情况只删掉标签字面量、把整段思考**漏在气泡里**（普通聊天 / 剧情参谋尤其常见，思考还会被当上下文喂回下一轮）。现在**闭标签出现在开标签之前时，从开头到 `</think>` 的整段思考会连内容一起剥掉**（气泡显示与侧聊历史两头都剥）。护栏：已知结构区块（`<StoryPlan>` / 校正稿 / 角色草稿 等）若排在闭标签之前，则一律不动——绝不会误删你的方案或草稿。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.34.0 新增（🎭 角色工坊 · 台词丰满）**：不少朋友反映锻造出来的角色卡里**台词偏干**——意思对、性格对，但一句句短得像电报，用起来总要再手动让模型「把台词写得更丰满自然些」。现在工坊设置里多了一个开关「**台词丰满（锻造台词写成完整人话）**」（默认关）：勾上后，锻造稿里所有台词（说话方式的示范句、多副面孔的各面语料、画面里的对白）都会写成**当面说出口的完整人话**——带着角色当下的口气和说话习惯、容得下情绪和细节；**话少的角色照旧话少**，但开口的那几句会把事情一口气说完整，而不是拆成几个词往外蹦。角色个性、条数与卡片结构完全不变。这一段追加指令在 DeepSeek / Gemini / Claude 上都做过对照验证（包括「寡言角色会不会被写成话痨」「泼辣与沉默角色的嘴会不会混」这类专项裁判）——嫌台词干就开它，喜欢极简电报腔就保持关闭。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.32.0 新增（🛡 长上下文防跑偏 + 明确点名可代笔）**：修复一类实测问题——聊天记录很长时（两三万字以上尤其明显），在**普通聊天 / 剧情参谋**里发「然后呢」「继续」这类短话、或把本想发到主聊天的**戏内发言**（角色台词、括号动作、贴来的正文片段）误发进神谕，模型会不再讨论、直接替你**续写正文**（严重时用第一人称冒充你的角色说话）。现在这两个模式会把故事记录包装成**只读引用材料**、并在其后加一道「戏外提醒」：歧义短话一律当成讨论（给分析或反问确认），发错窗口的戏内发言会被指出来而不是接着演。同时定下新规矩：**你明确开口点名要它代笔时**（帮写台词 / 独白、改写润色某段、代拟你的下一条回复、让参谋直接写下一幕草稿……），它会**照做**——以戏外口吻交付、注明是草稿、只写你点名的那一段、写完即停。诊断 / 世界书 / 校正 / 工坊模式不受影响。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.31.0 新增（📖 侧聊也能触发世界书绿灯条目）**：以前**绿灯（关键词触发）条目只看主聊天**——你在神谕侧聊里输入触发词是不会激活它的（「明明打了名字，相关设定却没带上」就是这个原因）。现在**普通聊天、剧情参谋、手动校正（勾了「世界书」时）的侧聊问答也参与关键词匹配**：你和神谕**双方**最近几条侧聊消息里的触发词都算数，条数窗口与主聊天一致（用 ST 世界书设置里的**「扫描深度」**，滑出窗口即失效——和主聊天同样的记忆长度）。主聊天自己的扫描窗口不受挤占，蓝灯（常驻）条目行为不变。**角色工坊**则是可选开关「**关键词触发世界书**」（默认关）：开了会把聊天与访谈里提到的设定条目作为**参考补充块**喂给访谈师和锻造——你**选条目器里勾的书 / 条目仍是唯一权威**，补充块只加不减、已勾的条目不会重复投喂。诊断模式保持只扫主聊天（精选 / 混合契约不变）。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.30.0 新增（🎭 角色工坊 · ✂️ 锻造稿精简）**：锻造出的 NPC 草稿卡上多了两个按钮——**「✂️ 精简全稿」**（一次调用：拆长句、删跨节重复，读起来省力得多）和**「✂️✂️ 深度精简」**（3 份并行分节编辑 + 1 份删减手术单、由装置逐刀核验执行，删得更深）。精简**永远不动原稿**：成功后卡上出现**「原稿 ⇄ 精简稿」切换**，写入和后续修订都以你当前显示的版本为准；一整套守卫（章节头 / 台词 / 状态行 / 画面·衍生实体 / 协议句）任何一道不过就**自动回落原稿**并如实说明。设置里另有**「锻造后自动精简」**开关（默认关）——开着时只在 NPC 草稿明显冗长（长句密集）时才自动补一发，本就精炼的稿子不会白花调用；强输出模型（如 Claude）建议开，DeepSeek / Gemini 的锻造稿通常本就精炼、开不开区别不大。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.27.0 新增（✨ 校正 · ✂️ 选段校正——划一段、只改这一段）**：手动校正新增「选段校正」。在「校正设置」点 **✂️ 选段校正**，会弹出当前这条回复的全文，你**用鼠标 / 手指划选**要改的那一段、写一句「怎么改」，就**只把这一段**发给模型重写、改好后**精确回插原位**——你**没划到的地方（状态栏、面板、别的段落）一个字都不会动**（它们压根不进模型，所以从机制上就不可能被误删 / 改花）。特别适合两种情况：① **长聊天 / 弱模型**下整条校正容易「抄原文不改 / 顺手乱删」时——只改一小段，模型稳得多（这一点经真实 DeepSeek 44 发实验验证：划选重写在 8 万 token 上下文下**零退化**）；② **外科手术式的小改**（「这句对白改冷一点」「这段重写简洁些」）。改写稿会先给你**看改动 diff**；模型要是**基本没改**、或**越界改到了别处**、或长度异常，也会**明确警示**（不拦你，看清了再点）。确认无误再**应用**——原回复永远留在左滑、随时能滑回，**不破坏存档**。想改分散的好几段？分两次划选、各改一次即可，中间没划的那段始终不动。\r\n\r\n> **v1.25.0 改进（✨ 校正 · 三个稳健性修补）**：① **「模型基本没改」会明说了**——手动校正遇到模型几乎原样返回（高上下文下 DeepSeek 等常见的「抄原文不改」）时，校正稿上方新增一行**琥珀提醒**「模型基本没改（改动约 N 字）……建议调小前文或重试」，不再拿一枚看似正常的「应用」按钮糊弄你（应用按钮仍在——万一你要的就是改一个错别字）；自动模式则直接**按「无需校正」处理、不落稿**。② **新增「校正回复上限」设置**——长楼层（约 3000 字以上）改写常因输出被 4096 token 地板截断而「总是失败」，现在可在「校正设置」里把上限顶高（如 8192 / 12288），留空 = 自动（对手动 + 自动都生效；超过服务商单次上限会被拒，报错就调回来）。③ **老用户一次性迁到精简默认**：1.24.0 改了手动校正默认（不带前文 / 世界书 / 概要），但**老存档里已保存的旧默认（`-1` 全部前文）不会自动更新**——现在首次载入会**一次性**把仍停在旧默认的几项迁到精简默认并**弹一次说明**，想要全量前文的把「加载前文条数」改回 `-1` 即可。另修一处内部解析：模型在思考里**提到** `<FixedReply>` 标签时不再被误当成稿开头。\r\n\r\n> **v1.24.1 调整（🎭 角色工坊 · 章节面板再精简）**：**「弱点缺陷」「能力技能」默认不再勾选，并移到章节行末尾**——默认草稿聚焦核心九件（基本信息、外貌、背景、人际、性格、说话方式、目标、深层人格、防误读），想写短板或技能时勾上即可，勾了就一定会写（所见即所得不变）。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.24.0 修复 + 改进（✨ 校正 · 手动模式默认精简上下文 + 结构块保留）**：修掉手动校正「把状态栏 / 面板 / HTML / 图生标记这类**非正文内容**也一起删掉 / 改花」的问题，并**改了手动模式的默认**：① **默认不再带前文 / 世界书 / 剧情概要**（只发这一条回复 + 角色卡）——弱模型（DeepSeek / Gemini 等）在**高上下文**下常会认不准要改哪一条、把前文内容混进结果；设置面板顶部有一行提醒，**确有需要（对齐设定 / 前情）时再逐项勾开**即可。② 手动校正现在**默认原样保留回复里的结构块**（状态栏、`[方括号]`标记、HTML / XML 面板、选项、图生提示等），不再被「让描写更生动」这类泛指令顺手删掉；**但你点名要改时以你为准**——比如「把状态栏里的血量改成 50」，它就只改那一处、其余原样。（自动模式本就有整套结构保护，不受影响。）经 DeepSeek + Gemini 冷模型实测：结构块存活 100%、点名改块只动那块。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.23.4 调整（🎭 角色工坊 · 面板精简 + 访谈师会追问外貌了）**：① **「行为逻辑」章节从面板移除**——让草稿包含面板更聚焦（老存档里勾过它的会自动取消，草稿其余部分不受影响；它的底层工艺仍按最新验证轮保持在最佳状态，将来需要随时可以恢复）；② **访谈师把「外貌特征」升级为必问项**——只要本次要写外貌、而你还没给出「一眼认得出TA」的素材，它就一定会问你要，并当场提醒：不给真素材的话，AI 写外貌爱给谁都安上伤疤、老茧这类通用件——TA 的日子留在身上的痕迹（常年做的活、常待的地方、打理自己的习惯）才认得出TA。答不上来也没关系，说「随便」它就记下「交给锻造从TA的经历推导」接着往下聊（没勾外貌时不会问）。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.23.3 打磨（🎭 角色工坊 · Gemini 服从性九处修复）**：上一轮治理「跨卡复读」，这一轮对着 Gemini 生成的出厂演示卡逐条审计，把它容易「不守规矩」的九处提示词改成了骨架化写法（对 DeepSeek 同样生效，全部经冷模型电池验证、不降写卡工艺）：① **多副面孔每张面都有名字了**——每面以〔＿＿面〕两三字小标题起头（此前 Gemini 的面孔全部无名、直接从触发条件开写）；② 性格画像的**衍生条目带色组标题**（「X衍生一：…」式，一眼看出属于哪个颜色组），每条收在两到四句、不再越写越长；③ 言行反差改用**「画面一」「画面二」**序号成段，日常画面占多数、战斗对峙至多一个且只能压轴——不再一半篇幅在打架；④ **佩剑、盔甲不再被当成身体特征写进外貌**，体型描述带上成因（为什么练成这样）；⑤ 点睛比喻的收尾不再是「还能碎几次？」式倒计时问句，也不再把别节内容粘贴过来、不再把比喻翻译回大白话；⑥ 目标动机固定写出「嘴上说的那版 / 真正驱着TA的那版」两层；⑦ 背景经历的底色不再和塑形重复同一件事；⑧ 行为逻辑的例子回到日常琐事（吃亏、尴尬、求助时怎么办，不再动辄拔剑）；⑨ 防误读固定含「说话的方式」与「写法」两条常驻条目。**已知限项**：Gemini 偶尔仍会给用剑角色配「虎口老茧 / 指节粗大」这类职业通用印记——嫌俗套的话，对草稿说一句「修订：把外貌印记换成从TA自己经历里长出来的」即可。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.23.2 打磨（🎭 角色工坊 · 跨卡「复读」治理）**：针对「建了几个角色，卡里总出现同样的东西」做了六处提示词外科手术（每处都经冷模型验证、且不降低写卡工艺）：① 道德底线不再人手一句「那是TA对自己最后的定义」——收尾改用角色自己的话；② 伴生实体条目不再照抄示例句，改成各卡自己的表述；③ 言行反差里的「食堂打饭」示例场景移除（合拍角色会整段搬走它）；④ 外貌特征引导「印记从TA的生活里长出来」——疤/耳垂缺口不再人手一份；⑤ Gemini 的性格三色不再是字面颜色（灰/金/白 → 真正的机制词）；⑥ 点睛比喻的意象锚在角色自己的世界里（荒原角色不再配海雾灯塔）。另附一条小贴士：**锻造偶尔会「没产出草稿」**（任何上下文长度都有约 8% 概率，是模型把输出预算全花在思考上）——**重试一次即可**，不是设置问题。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.23.0 大改（🎭 角色工坊 · 锻造工艺全面重修）**：锻造提示词按「写卡教室」八章课程逐节重修——15 个章节各配一套**填空式骨架**（性格调色盘三色各 3-4 条带标题的场景衍生、深层人格七件、防误读逐条「关于TA的〔特质〕」…），由 8 个编辑代理对着冷 DeepSeek / Gemini 逐节调优后合并验收。用户可感的变化：① 生成的卡**质感明显上一档**——写行为不贴标签、场景收在事实上、善意藏在做法里；② **「生活习惯」chip 改为「行为逻辑」**（日常琐事里TA会怎么做——吃亏 / 尴尬 / 求助时的具体反应；旧存档的勾选不受影响）；③ 世界书有条目格式规定时（如【出身】【现状】开头、末尾状态行）**优先按世界的规矩来**；④ 锻造回复上限的自动下限 **8192 → 12288**（此前全章节重型锻造约半数被截断）；⑤ persona 目标勾了「多副面孔」时台词全部住进各面语料（未勾仍是至多三句）。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.18.3 改版（✨ 校正 · 新手友好界面 + 流式校正）**：「校正设置 · 自动」重排——默认只见**判定行、两个运行开关、校正目标、强度**（原「校正提示词」下拉改叫「强度」；✂️收紧开关**移除**、轻校恒含收紧），其余全部收进**「进阶设置（一般不用动）」**折叠。保留区上方新增**检测收据**：实时列出本条回复**实际识别到并自动保留**的结构块，认漏的块**点一下**就固定进保留区；识别不对的格式欢迎在 **Discord 私信 @Prince**，会加进测试集修复。切自动时的提醒框整个重写（承诺更实在：**常见格式**自动识别、认不准会**问你一次**）。**「按目标校正最新回复」现在流式直播校正稿**（尊重「流式」开关，停止键随时中断）。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.18.0 补充（✨ 校正 ·「整体校正」默认开 + 未知标签也会问）**：在分段引擎之上，默认改为**「整体校正」**：正文合并成 **1 次调用**（不再逐段多次），夹在正文之间的结构块（结算面板 / 图生 / 注释…）在调用里换成**位置锚点**、校正后由代码**原位放回**——省调用、整篇更连贯；模型极偶尔挪动锚点时**内容绝不丢**（兜底接到正文末尾，记录里会如实说明，左滑「用原文」即可还原）。想要「位置由代码百分百把控、单段失败只损失那一段」的稳妥模式，把「校正设置」里的**「整体校正」**勾选关掉即可回到分段逐次调用。另外两处：① 卡片用**没见过的标签**包正文（如 `<narrative_x>`）时，现在也会**问一次**「正文像是包在 <narrative_x> 里——点此确认」（以前会静默跳过）；② `<action_info>` 结算面板加入已知结构名单（命定之诗类战斗卡的面板从此**保证**原样保留）。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.18.0 新增（✨ 校正 ·「分段校正」——多段正文全都校、结构块绝不送模型）**：自动校正的引擎升级了。现在它先把回复**拆成「正文片段 + 结构块」**，正文**逐段**各发一次普通校正调用，状态栏 / 选项 / 注释 / 代码块 / `[IMG_GEN]` 这些结构**压根不进模型**、由代码原位拼回——所以「结构被改花 / 被挪到结尾」这类问题从机制上就不会发生。三个直接的改善：① **多个 `<content>` 块现在全都会校正**（以前只改第一块）；② 正文里**埋着**的 `<item_info>`/`<details>` 等结构块自动保住（不用再手动填保留区）；③ **没有包裹标签、散文和结构块混排的卡**（问题报告最多的一类）也能校了——第一次会弹一个**「需要确认一次」**：点一下确认「正文是标签之外的散文」，之后每条回复自动分段校正、按聊天记住。侧聊记录现在**如实**写「已校正 N 段正文中的 M 段」＋每段未校正的原因；大半正文没校成会给 ⚠️ 警告并建议重试。另外接上了一批防呆：作用域标签失焦自动清洗（全角括号也认）、保留区填错尖 / 方括号会警告并可一键改正、开自动但没配连接会提醒。**已知取舍**（v1 有意为之）：各段独立校正、跨段重复的套话不互相去重；单条回复最多发 4 次片段调用（最大的段优先，超出的如实记录）；行内样式标签跟正文走，偶尔可能被模型顺手删掉（可用排除区点名保留）。干净单块 `<content>` 卡和纯散文卡走的还是原来那条路径，行为逐字节不变。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.17.22 修复（✨ 校正 · 与 MVU「额外模型更新」不再抢写，opt-in）**：如果你开了 MVU 的「额外模型更新」（用另一个模型异步解析变量），它会和自动校正在同一条回复后**同时抢着写**，可能把数据写乱。现在「校正设置」新增一个开关 **「⏳ 与 MVU 额外模型更新并用」**——勾上后，自动校正**照常立刻开跑**（和 MVU 并行、几乎不多等），只在**生成新回复稿之前**等 MVU 把变量写完、再把它写好的变量块合并进来，两者不再抢写同一条消息。**默认不勾**：不用额外模型更新的人完全不受影响。\r\n\r\n> **v1.17.21 新增（✨ 校正·精校 加了「Gemini 类」侧重）**：精校的「侧重」下拉多了一项 **Gemini 类**——用 Gemini（`gemini-3.1-pro-preview` 等）跑校正就选它。（实测下来 Gemini 的脾性和 DeepSeek 一类：它自己就会把「魔法当物理讲」那种成串报参数的台词清干净，而 Opus 版的「强攻」反而会把正式场合 / 庄重的台词改过头，所以 **Gemini 类目前直接沿用 DeepSeek 版的提示词**；将来若做 Gemini 专属版，你选的「Gemini 类」不用改、会自动升级。）DeepSeek / Opus 用户完全不受影响。\r\n\r\n> **v1.17.20 改进（小修）**：① ✨ 校正设置里「只校正此标签内的正文」输入框**去掉了灰色的 `content` 占位提示**——之前框里那行灰字看着像已经填了值，容易让人以为「删不掉 / 已经设成 content 了」；其实**留空是有效设置**（＝校正整条回复），现在清空后就是真正的空框，不再有误导的灰字。（默认值仍是真正可删的 `content` 文本，只是灰色幻影没了。）② 手机魔棒菜单里的复位项**标题从「神谕窗口归位（居中）」缩短为「窗口归位」**——有手机用户反映太长了；居中图标不变。\r\n\r\n> **v1.17.19 改进（手机）**：现在**整条标题栏都能拖动窗口了**——之前标题栏挤了 8 个按钮，只有按钮之间的小缝能拖，手机上很难抓住。现在手机上**按住标题栏任意处（包括按钮）拖动即可移动窗口**；轻点按钮仍是原来的功能（靠「按下后有没有拖动」区分轻点 / 拖动）。（桌面不变。）\r\n\r\n> **v1.17.17 新增（✨ 校正·自动模式「精校」提示词）**：「校正设置」的自动模式新增**「校正提示词」**下拉——**轻校**（现行提示，默认，行为完全不变）/ **精校**（更彻底的**三道工序**校正：收紧 → 去对白 AI 腔 → 去叙述 AI 腔，已含收紧）。选「精校」时再出一个**「精校侧重」**：按你用的模型选——**DeepSeek / 国产模型**选「DeepSeek 类」，**Claude / Opus** 选「Opus 类」。（两版对「像念说明书一样成串报参数」的台词处理方向**相反**：DeepSeek 版更克制、Opus 版对这类「数据包腔」更主动清理；选错侧重反而会过校正，所以按模型分开选。）默认「轻校」，**不选精校则一切照旧**，现有用户零影响。\r\n\r\n> **v1.17.16 新增（✨ 校正·自动模式「自动配置 + 防呆」）**：自动校正现在会**自己认出你卡片的正文标签**——第一条回复后台一嗅探，是 `<gametxt>` 还是 `<正文>` 都能自动切好、**按聊天记住**，你基本不用手配；配错也不闯祸（设的标签这条回复里没有 → **跳过不动**，绝不把整条状态栏 / 选项 / 世界书改花）。「校正设置」里新增：**「扫描本卡正文标签」**（一键填好作用域 ＋ 把正文里的结构块勾选加进保留区）、**判定预览行**（切到自动就显示「这条回复此刻会被怎么处理」）、**「恢复推荐设置」**一键还原。另修两个真 bug：校正中途**切聊天**不会再把改动写进别的对话；模型回复被**截断**成半句时不会再被误当校正稿应用。你**手填**的标签永远不会被自动覆盖。\r\n\r\n> **v1.17.15 改进（手机）**：修掉手机上「窗口按钮挤在最顶上够不着 / 窗口拖丢了找不回来」的老问题——① 首次打开时窗口**居中**弹出，标题栏不再顶到状态栏 / 刘海底下；② 魔棒菜单里（手机专属）新增一项**「神谕窗口归位（居中）」**，一键把窗口**复位到屏幕中央 + 默认大小**——就算窗口被拖到屏外、大小拖坏了，也能随时把它救回来。（桌面不受影响。）\r\n>\r\n> **v1.17.14 修复**：✨ 校正点「按目标校正最新回复」后**现在能中断了**——发送键会变成「停止」键，点它即刻停下（此前发出去就只能等它自己跑完 / 超时）。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.17.13 修复**：✨ **手动校正**遇到模型没吐出规范的 `<FixedReply>` 时，不再直接报「没能解析出校正稿…请检查连接/模型」——会尽量从回复里**把校正稿救回来**（弱模型 / 标签乱掉 / 思考占满额度都能兜住），真被截断时也会明确告诉你是「截断」。（自动模式的严格解析不变。）\r\n>\r\n> **v1.17.12 修复**：✨ **自动校正 / 自动诊断**偶发「改到上一条回复、而不是刚收到的这条」的问题修好了——现在牢牢**钉住触发的那条消息**；万一那条一时为空 / 被更新的楼层顶掉，就干净跳过，绝不误改旧回复。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.17.11 改进**：切到 ✨ 校正「自动」时的提醒框重写成**给新手的简单说明**：自动校正**默认只改 `<content>` 里的故事正文**，正文外的状态栏 / 选项 / 世界书 / 图片 / 面板都会原样保留，一般什么都不用设；唯一要确认的是——若你的卡片用别的标签包正文（如 `<gametxt>`），把「只校正此标签内的正文」那栏改成那个标签名即可。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.17.10 修复**：✨ 校正「按目标校正」卡的**「看改动」不再误报**——以前它把你放进保留区、其实好好保住的块（如 `<branches>`、`<sceneinfo>`）显示成一大片红色删除，让人误以为被删了（其实那些块根本没送去校正、应用后也在）。现在「看改动」对比的是**实际会应用的结果**：保留的块不再标红，只有真正改动的正文、和你没保留而被删的块才会显示。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.17.9 改进**：✨ 校正「排除区」更强了：① 支持**嵌套同名标签**（`<div>` 套 `<div>` 现在会**整块**保留最外层，不再被切碎）；② 支持**方括号块**（图生卡的 `[IMG_GEN]…[/IMG_GEN]` 这类，直接把 `[IMG_GEN]` 写进保留区即可）。配合 1.17.8 的「只校正此标签内的正文」，结构化卡片的状态栏 / 选项 / 图生 / 面板基本都能稳稳保住。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.17.8 新增（重要）**：✨ 校正新增**「只校正此标签内的正文」**（默认 `content`）。结构化卡片（带状态栏 / 选项菜单 / 世界书 / `<htmlcontent>` 地图等）把正文包在 `<content>…</content>` 里，开启后**只校正正文**，正文**外**的所有块原样保留、**原位不动**——彻底解决「自动校正把正文外的东西全删了 / 标签放进保留区也没用」。只需填**一个**标签名（卡片用别的标签包正文就改成那个），留空 = 校正整条回复。回复里没有该标签时自动校正整条（简单卡不受影响）。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.17.7 新增 × 2**：①【🧭 剧情参谋】的系统提示词现在也能在【设置 → 系统提示词】里查看 / 修改了（此前只有诊断 / 世界书可改；只开放单拍参谋指令，弧线编译器不动）。②切到【✨ 校正 → 自动】时会弹一次性提醒：自动校正会重写整条回复，像 `<sceneinfo>`、`<details>` 这种**成对标签块**若想原样留住、不被挪走 / 删掉，请把它的**起始标记**（如 `<sceneinfo>`，结尾的 `</sceneinfo>` 不用写）加进「排除区 · 保留」。可勾「不再提示」。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.17.6 修复**：🩺 **变量诊断**手动「应用 / 撤销」之后，楼层变量面板（状态栏）现在会**自动刷新**成新数据，不用再手动点「重新读取初始变量」了（自动诊断本来就会刷新，这次补上了手动这条路）。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.17.5 修复 / 改进（手机）**：剧情引导关窗后那枚**折叠的圆罗盘悬浮窗**——①静息时做成**半透明**，不再挡住下面的正文（碰一下 / 拖动时自动变回清晰）；②现在**能再次拖动**了（之前折叠成小罗盘后就拖不动，因为整枚药丸就是一颗按钮，被当成「点击」而非「拖拽」——轻点仍是展开，拖动才是移动）。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.17.4 新增**：自动校正 / 自动诊断跑的时候，「正在自动…」那条提示现在**点一下就能中断**（后台跑太久、或想停下时用）；中断发生在写入之前，所以这条回复不会被改动。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.17.3 修复**：✨ 校正时设为「保留」的标签块（比如让 AI 写在正文中段的 `<details>`），改完会**留在原来的位置**，不再被挪到回复末尾。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.17.2 修复**：✨ 校正应用后，主聊天那条回复现在会**立刻切到校正稿**，不用再「点一下 / 划一下」才显示（用 小白X / 翻译扩展 渲染的卡此前会停在旧回复；酒馆助手渲染的卡不受影响）。\r\n>\r\n> **v1.17.0 新增**：✨ 校正模式、发送失败「↻ 重试」、顶栏「⋯ 更多」菜单、世界书多选 + 条目内容预览、「仅角色相关世界书」、读取隐藏楼层。\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 安装与打开\r\n\r\n把整个 `story-oracle/` 文件夹放进 SillyTavern 的第三方扩展目录，刷新浏览器：\r\n\r\n- **较新版 ST**：`SillyTavern/data/<用户名>/extensions/story-oracle/`（默认 `default-user`）\r\n- **较旧版 ST**：`SillyTavern/public/scripts/extensions/third-party/story-oracle/`\r\n\r\n打开**魔棒菜单**（输入框旁的 🪄）→ **故事神谕**。想更快进出，可在设置里勾「在聊天输入栏显示快捷按钮」，输入框旁会多一个一键开关的 🌙。\r\n\r\n### 🔔 更新提醒（1.38 起）\r\n\r\n打开神谕窗口时会**自动检查一次新版本**（每次刷新页面后的首开各查一次）：发现 GitHub 上有更新，标题栏的 **⋯ / ⚙ 按钮**和设置面板顶部的**「更新」组**会亮**红点**，组里显示「发现新版本 vX.Y.Z」和一个**「立即更新」**按钮——点它走酒馆自带的扩展更新机制拉取新版，成功后 **5 秒自动刷新页面**生效（**点一下提示可取消刷新**，稍后自己刷新也行）。\r\n\r\n- **一键更新的前提**：扩展是通过酒馆「下载扩展」（填 GitHub 地址）安装的。手动复制文件夹安装的话一键更新会失败，按提示到「扩展管理」里更新、或到 GitHub 重新下载覆盖即可。\r\n- **隐私**：检查只是读取 GitHub 上的**公开版本号文件**（打不开时换 jsDelivr 镜像再试一次），**不发送任何数据**；失败就静默跳过，不打扰。\r\n- 不想要的话，「更新」组里**取消勾选「自动检查更新」**即可（之后不再有任何联网检查）。\r\n\r\n## 设置\r\n\r\n标题栏「⋯ 更多」菜单 → ⚙ **设置**。两种连接方式：\r\n\r\n- **直连（Direct，默认）**：填端点 URL（如 `https://your-proxy.com/v1`，会自动补 `/chat/completions`）、API 密钥、模型。密钥明文存在 ST 的 settings.json（个人 / 自建实例无妨）。\r\n  - **经酒馆后端转发（避免跨域 CORS）** ✅：直连报 **CORS / failed to fetch** 时勾选此项——**用的还是上面这个端点和密钥**，只是改由酒馆服务器代发，绕开浏览器跨域，**无需连接配置文件**。勾选后**「获取模型」也经酒馆服务器代发**（1.18.1 起），拉模型列表不再撞跨域。\r\n  - **地址原样使用（不自动补 /v1）**（1.22 起）：给路径特殊的中转站用——地址明明填对了却 404 / 拉不到模型，多半是被自动补了 `/v1`。勾选后按你填的地址原样请求（补全只剩 `/chat/completions`，「获取模型」同理打到 `地址/models`），常与上面的转发开关配合使用。\r\n  - **连接存档**（1.20 起，1.40 更名）：直连区底部可把当前的**端点 / 密钥 / 模型（1.22 起含「地址原样」开关）**存成命名存档，随时用「保存 / 加载 / 删除」一键切换不同服务商；删除前会弹确认框。⚠ 这里的「存档」与下面「系统提示词」区的**补全预设**是两回事——1.40 前它叫「连接预设」，有用户因此误以为那是自定义预设区，故更名。\r\n- **连接配置文件（Profile）**：选一个你保存好的 ST 连接配置；请求走 ST 后端转发，**不会被 CORS 拦**。⚠ 注意：若该配置文件**没有自带独立密钥**，ST 会回退用你**当前激活连接**的密钥——此时神谕选的配置文件必须与酒馆当前正在用的连接一致，否则会 **401 / 400**（密钥被发给了不认它的端点）。想彻底避开这个坑，多数情况下直接用上面的「直连 + 经酒馆后端转发」更省事。\r\n- **附加参数**（1.70 起）：「连接」区的「附加参数」按钮会弹出与 ST「自定义（兼容 OpenAI）」接口同款的三个框——**包括主体参数**（随每次请求发送的额外参数，YAML 或 JSON 对象）、**排除主体参数**（要从请求里剔除的参数名列表）、**包含请求标头**（额外请求头）。最常见的用途：**给 DeepSeek 类中转关掉思维链**——不关的话模型会先跑一大串思维链才回复，白等还费 token。在「包括主体参数」里填你的服务商认的那个开关即可，例如：\r\n  ```yaml\r\n  enable_thinking: false\r\n  ```\r\n  （各家写法不一：有的是 `enable_thinking: false`，有的是 `thinking: {type: disabled}` 或 `reasoning_effort: none`——以你服务商的文档为准。官方 DeepSeek 直接把模型换成 `deepseek-chat` 就没有思维链，不用填参数。）三框留空 = 一切照旧。生效范围：**直连模式**（含勾选「经酒馆后端转发」）全部生效；**连接配置文件**模式下只有 API 类型为「自定义（兼容 OpenAI）」的配置档生效，OpenAI / Claude / Gemini 等官方接口会忽略这些参数。填错格式不会被静默忽略——发送时会明确报错指出是哪个框。\r\n\r\n常用选项：温度、最大 token、**上下文深度**（喂多少条最近消息，`-1` = 整段、`0` = 不喂）、是否带角色卡、系统提示词。普通模式还会**默认带实时变量状态**（stat_data），所以「好感度多少」会按真实数值回答；关掉或卡无 MVU 时它会**如实说看不到数值**而不瞎编。世界信息来源可选「全部激活的世界书」「**仅角色相关（排除全局）**」等，并可开「**读取隐藏楼层**」让它读到 `/hide` 的楼层。世界书还有一档「**自定义（手动挑书和条目）**」（1.81.0）——像世界书管家那样多选要发的书、再逐条勾选，只发你勾的（无视关键词与启用 / 禁用；开了「混合模式」才会再加上已选书里当前触发的绿灯），带筛选与仅蓝灯 / 仅绿灯等快捷键，选择**按当前聊天记忆**，一本书第一次进入范围时按当前激活情况预选一份；整本都是蓝灯、靠插件限流、神谕却整本照发时用它。两点注意：诊断 / 变量编辑器的默认扫描也跟随它，但它们仍会另外带上变量规则条目；校正的「带上当前激活世界书」不受它影响。设置项按用途分组、可折叠，默认只展开「连接」。\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🔓 内置破限（1.40 起）\r\n\r\n模型动不动就拒绝、说教、或者把该写的地方一笔带过？设置里的**「补全预设」**下拉现在自带一项：\r\n\r\n> **🔓 内置破限 · 初心破限1.2（出自 初遇大佬）**\r\n\r\n选它就生效。**新装用户、以及从没选过预设的用户，默认已经帮你选好了**；如果你**已经选好并挑选过\r\n自己的预设**，我们**不会动你的选择**。\r\n\r\n**它是「包一层」，不是「换掉」。** 普通预设那条路是**整体替换**掉神谕自己的提示词；内置破限不一样，\r\n它把破限块包在神谕自己的提示词**外面**——神谕的分析框架、戏外守卫、各模式的结构化格式全都照常在用。\r\n所以下方的系统提示词文本框**不会被停用**。\r\n\r\n**默认只作用于【普通聊天】。** 其它模式要不要跟着用，由你自己决定——去各模式的设置里勾上\r\n**「经自定义补全预设」**即可（世界书 / 剧情参谋 / 角色工坊访谈 / 校正手动 / 校正自动）。\r\n**🩺 诊断模式永远不接**：它只做机械的变量修复，没有「拒绝」这回事，而它的解析器最敏感。\r\n\r\n**随时可以取消**：在同一个下拉里换回「— 自定义 —」或你自己的预设就行。\r\n\r\n开了之后，剧情参谋会明显更爱主动说「我可以帮你把这段写出来」。\r\n\r\n> 破限内容出自 **初遇大佬**的《初心破限 1.2》（内置版随作者更新 1.0 → 1.2）。1.2 里作者删掉了\r\n> 自然语言 main 提示词，只保留 `<sys>` 规则块与句末破限，内置版随之照办。原预设里的思维链层\r\n> （Think Override / Think Lock，1.2 起 Think Override 默认开启）**依旧没有包含**——它与破限功能\r\n> 无关，却会让思考过程泄漏进气泡、并打乱诊断 / 世界书 / 校正 / 工坊的结构化输出格式。\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 💬 普通聊天\r\n\r\n默认模式，问剧情即可。系统提示词每次发送时重建，所以神谕看到的永远是最新故事状态。\r\n\r\n## 🩺 诊断模式（Diagnose）\r\n\r\n修复 MVU（MagVarUpdate）的状态变量。神谕读取本卡的 MVU 规则、当前 `stat_data`、以及最新回复里的 `<UpdateVariable>`，对照剧情给出一份**保守的纠正补丁**；气泡下方出现 **将修复应用到状态** 按钮，通过 MVU 自己的管线应用，并可一键**撤销**。全量审计输出较长，token 上限已自动抬到 ≥4096。\r\n\r\n**补丁体检 + 自动掰正（1.67.0 起，自动生效、无开关）。** 点「应用」时，补丁会先照 MVU 自己的规矩体检一遍，把模型常犯的写法当场修好（动词同义词 → `replace`、路径末尾多余的斜杠、`delta` 写成 `\"+5\"` 字符串、`[数值,\"说明\"]` 字段被整对写回、`<JSONPatch >` 标签里的空格、以及多写一层 `stat_data` 的路径），并把混进来的**格式不合规条目**单独剔掉——不剔的话 MVU 会把**整块指令一起丢弃**。每一类都只在**有证据**（改过之后才对得上你当前的变量）时才动手；修了几处会显示在状态行里。手动「🩺 诊断」与自动诊断走的是**同一条**流水线。\r\n\r\n**没生效时会告诉你为什么。** 如果一个值都没变，每条指令都会给出确定的原因（路径不存在 / 本来就是这个值 / 动词 MVU 不认识 / 值的类型对不上 / 路径里有下划线开头的内部字段 / **这一层是卡片没标成可扩展的对象或列表、不允许往里新增项** / **要加减的那一项不是数字也不是日期**……）和一句下一步建议——后两类是 1.77.3 起照着**卡片自己的结构定义**判的。若补丁本身**完全合规却仍然零变化**，会告诉你**去哪看真正的原因**：酒馆助手 →「MVU 变量框架」面板 → 通知 → 勾上「变量初始化/更新出错时通知」，再跑一次，弹出的 `[MVU]`（挂了 mvu_zod 的卡是 `[MVU zod]`）提示会写明是哪条指令、为什么被拒。\r\n\r\n**自动诊断（AUTO）⚠ 实验性。** 在诊断模式的「**诊断设置**」栏里勾上「**自动诊断每条新回复**」即开启（1.65.0 起：诊断按钮只管开 / 关诊断这一房，自动与否由这个勾选框独占；首次勾选会先弹一次性说明，确认后才真开）。开启后诊断按钮变红，主聊天每来一条新回复都会在后台自动诊断并**自动应用**——判断依据是「**变量引擎这一回合到底执行了没有**」（1.69.0 起）：真执行了就只做核验（卡片用自定义标签如 `<update>` 也认得，v1.40.2 起）；正文里**完全没有**更新区块，就据剧情推导补上；**区块在、但写坏了一条都没执行**，则据剧情**重新推导**这一回合（这一支只写变量、不动消息正文）。每轮在侧聊留一条记录（有改动的带「撤销」；「没能读懂模型的回复」那种记录里，回复摘要若被截断（末尾 …），记录上会有「**查看完整回复**」按钮，点开就地看模型回复原文——仅本次会话内有效，1.71.1 起），并把更新写回消息、刷新状态栏。**这一楼要是根本没有 MVU 数据**（MVU 选了「额外模型解析」却没勾「启用自动请求」，它对这楼什么都不做），自动诊断会先把上一楼的状态抄过来、补上状态栏占位符再诊断（1.77.2 起；先给 MVU 三秒半，它自己处理了就不插手）。**离开诊断模式不会关掉它**——按钮保持红色表示它仍在后台跑；要停就回诊断模式取消勾选。\r\n\r\n**失败自动重试（1.74.0 起，默认关）。** 诊断设置里勾「**🔁 失败自动重试**」后，自动诊断这一轮没跑成会自动再试：次数可填（默认 2，上限 99），并可分别勾选三类失败情形——**空白回复**（模型没返回内容）、**格式错误**（没能读懂 / 拒收模型给的更新，含「一条回复两个更新区块」这类按规则拒收的情形）、**调用失败**（网络错误 / 超时等），三项独立组合。每次重试都是**完整的一轮**：重新等 MVU、重新读取当前状态、重新组提示词，然后再发一次请求；进行中的提示写明第几次重试、点一下即中断。诊断成功、核验通过无需改动、以及安全跳过（切聊天 / 状态已变 / 手动中断 / 新回复顶掉本轮）**永不重试**。只作用于自动诊断；手动点「🩺 诊断」不受影响。\r\n\r\n如果同时使用 TavernHelper / MVU 的「**额外模型解析**」，再勾选「**⏳ 兼容 MVU『额外模型解析』**」（默认关闭；不用外部解析的人不会多等）。神谕会在回复落地后观察 **4 秒**：没检测到外部解析就立即按普通自动诊断继续；一旦检测到，则等待它的**整个重试批次**收尾，而不是被重试之间短暂的“空闲”骗过去。外部解析成功写出更新块时，自动诊断负责核验；外部解析失败、重试耗尽或没有写出有效块时，自动诊断照常据剧情推导。单批最多等待 **10 分钟**，仍无法确认收尾就安全跳过本轮，绝不抢写。自动校正若也开启，可以照常并行生成，但会在落新 swipe 前共享这次等待，并把 MVU 后写入的更新块与状态栏占位符合并进校正稿。用户在等待中发出下一条消息时，旧的神谕作业会静默作废；MVU 自己的外部请求不会被强行取消。\r\n\r\n**允许与其他脚本并写 MVU（1.83.0 起，默认关）。** 有些角色卡自带「回合后」脚本（世界推进、变量核验之类），会在每条回复落地后自己改写 MVU 变量，有的还先自己调一次模型；而自动诊断是先记下当时的变量、再去问模型、回来才写入——这中间只要变量被别人动过，以前就整轮作废，记录里每回合都是「已跳过：MVU 变量在自动诊断运行期间被改动」。在诊断设置里勾上「**🧩 允许与其他脚本并写 MVU**」后，自动诊断不再整轮放弃：模型给的修正**逐条**看，落在没被别人动过的值上的照常写入（写在当前最新的变量之上），正好撞上别人刚改过的值的那几条**跳过不写**，并在记录末尾点名是哪几条（路径）；全部撞上时仍是跳过。只认标准 `<JSONPatch>` 写法，`_.set` 写法的补丁裁不开、照旧整份跳过。另外从 1.83.0 起，模型核验通过、给了**空补丁**的回合不再因为「变量变过」被记成跳过——本来就没有要写的东西，记录直接说「无需改动」。手动点「🩺 诊断」后的「应用」按钮不受这个勾选影响。\r\n\r\n> **v1.66.0 界面修复**：诊断设置太多时，设置栏最多占神谕窗口一半，超出部分在栏内滚动，不再把聊天区和输入框顶出窗口；上方「诊断设置」仍可折叠。\r\n\r\n> ⚠ 这是**唯一会自动写入 MVU 状态**的功能，故**默认关、需手动切到红色**，首次开启有提醒。拿不准就停在手动「🩺 诊断」——它只在你点了之后才出补丁。\r\n\r\n**把修正写进正文（可选，默认关）。** 默认情况下，诊断的修正只写进 MVU 的**实时状态**、不改动消息正文——于是一旦点了 MVU 的**「重新处理变量」**（它会把那一楼的变量清空、只照正文重新算一遍），修正就没了。在诊断模式的「**诊断设置**」栏里勾上「**把诊断修正写进正文**」后，诊断的修正（自动与手动）会作为一小段补丁写进这条回复**已有的更新区块内部**，重新处理变量时照样算得出同样的结果；撤销时那段也会一并撤掉。写进去的是**结果值**（绝对值）而非增减量，所以反复重算不会漂。**自动与手动诊断都覆盖**——手动「🩺 诊断」点「应用」同样会写进正文，撤销时一并移除。非必要请保持关闭。\r\n\r\n**精选条目（可选）。** 勾「用精选条目」后可像世界书模式那样**逐条挑**要喂给诊断的条目，且**无视** ST 的启用 / 禁用状态——于是被禁用（以保持主聊天干净）的变量规则条目也能单独喂给诊断。带快捷选择与筛选，**按当前聊天记忆**。\r\n\r\n**🎛 变量编辑器（1.55.0 起）。** 诊断设置里的 **「🎛 变量编辑器」** 按钮会打开一个「游戏修改器」式面板：把本聊天当前的全部 MVU 变量摆成**分页 + 可折叠树**（分页跟随角色卡自己的分组结构），想改哪个直接改——数字框（认得出取值范围时带滑杆）、文本框、开关，列表可**加项 / 删项**，`[数值,\"描述\"]` 这类带说明的字段只改数值、说明原样保留。（1.89.0）在挂了变量规则的卡上，诊断写入前会先按规则预演、只写能过的部分，并提供「🩺 检查存档」找出存档里已经不合规的值。页签里的文件夹 / 字段 / 列表还能用 **🗑 删除**（1.88.0；先标记、按「应用」才生效，↩ 取消标记，应用后可撤销；页签本身不能删）。改动会高亮计数，按一次**「应用」**统一写入（走 MVU 自己的写入通道，**不发模型调用、不花钱、绝不改聊天消息**），状态栏立刻刷新，同时诊断侧聊里留一条「🎛 手动编辑」记录，带**「撤销」**按钮。搜索框可跨分页找字段名。\r\n\r\n- **「🔍 分析取值规则」（可选，一次模型调用）。** 有些卡在世界书规则里限定了某些字段只能取几个值（比如心情只能是「平静 / 开心 / 生气」，因为要联动前端立绘）。点这个按钮会把本卡的变量规则交给你的模型分析一次，识别出的受限字段变成**下拉框**、数值范围喂给滑杆；结果**按聊天缓存**（之后免费），可「重新扫描」。扫描中可点 **⏹ 中断**。识别难免有漏——每个下拉框旁都有 ✎ 可切回自由输入。\r\n- **撤销的范围。** 每条「手动编辑」记录的撤销恢复的是**那次应用前的整份状态**：如果你之后又应用过别的修改（或自动诊断写过），撤销较早的那条会把后面的改动一并回退。撤销按钮在**本次会话内**有效，重载页面后记录变为只读（与诊断记录一致）。\r\n- **小提示。** 恰好只有 2 个文本项的列表（如背包里只有两件东西）会被 MVU 的惯例当成「数值+描述」对来显示——只影响显示方式，不会破坏数据。1.56.0 起，这类字段旁会多一个 **≡** 按钮：点一下就**当作列表**显示（可加项 / 删项），**⇄** 可切回，选择**按聊天记忆**。\r\n- **扫描回复被截断？** 若你的模型是「思考型」（推理占用大量输出额度），扫描回复可能没写完；1.56.0 起会明确提示「回复不完整（可能被截断）」——换非思考型模型或重试即可（1.57.0 起扫描输出上限抬到 16384）。\r\n- **⤢ 放大编辑（1.57.0 起）。** 文本框太小？每个文本输入框旁都有 **⤢**：点开一个大编辑窗（占满编辑器面板），改完按「确定」写回、「取消 / ✕ / 点遮罩」放弃；没改动就按确定等于什么都不做。注意：字段值本身是单行的——大窗里换行会被合并并明确提示。\r\n- **编辑器跟着剧情走（1.59.0 起）。** 编辑器开着的时候，如果剧情又推进了（新回复、自动诊断修正等），面板会**自动刷新成最新值**——你正在改的值不受影响，并会提示「没动过的值已同步」。你正在打字或开着放大编辑窗时它会安静等你弄完再刷新。另外：如果某条「手动编辑」记录之后状态又变过，点它的「撤销」会先**跟你确认**（因为会连后来的变化一起回退）。\r\n\r\n**🎛 修改器（1.63.0 起）。** 想让某个变量「自己维持」而不用每次手动改？变量编辑器里**每个可编辑字段行末尾都有一个 🔒 按钮**——点一下就把这个字段**冻结在当前值**：往后每一条新回复处理完（校正 / 诊断都跑完之后），神谕都会安静地把它拉回你锁定的那个数，哪怕剧情或诊断把它改动了；再点一次解冻。除了冻结，字段还能挂**「每回合 ±X」**（比如金钱每回合自动 +100）和**「上下限」**（比如体力不低于 0、不超过 100）——三种规则可以同时叠在同一个字段上，算法固定是**先 ±X、再夹上下限、冻结压过一切**。变量编辑器分页末尾有一个专门的 **「🎛 修改器」** 页，列出本聊天全部生效中的规则（点 ✕ 删除），并可用它的表单给已冻结过的字段追加 ±X / 上下限规则（先用 🔒 冻结一次，字段才会出现在表单的下拉里）；页面底部会显示「上一回合」修改器改了什么，方便确认规则确实在生效。\r\n\r\n- **规则跟着聊天走，不告诉 AI。** 规则按**当前聊天**保存（换一个聊天互不影响），纯粹是代码在算——不发模型调用、不花钱，AI 完全不知道这些规则的存在（不会出现在任何提示词里），所以不会被剧情「解释」或绕开。也因为是安静运行，不弹提示、不留侧聊记录——想确认它有没有生效，去 🎛 修改器页看那行「上一回合」。\r\n- **手动改和规则会打架吗？** 不会——你在变量编辑器里手动改了一个被冻结的字段并点「应用」，那个字段的**冻结目标会自动更新成你刚写的新值**（不然下一条回复就把你的手改又拉回去了）；同一字段上的 ±X / 上下限规则不受影响，仍是原样。撤销 / 重新应用这条「手动编辑」记录时，被顺带更新过的冻结目标也会跟着换回撤销前 / 撤销后的那个值——不会出现「点了撤销，结果下一条回复又被规则悄悄拉回来」的情况。\r\n- **⚠ 会被「重新处理变量」冲掉。** MVU 的**「重新处理变量」**是照消息正文**从头重新推算**一遍 `stat_data`——它不知道修改器规则的存在，算完会把规则刚写的值盖掉。用过「重新处理变量」之后，等下一条新回复，修改器会自动把规则再套一遍拉回来；中间那一楼如果你正好在看状态栏，可能会看到数字先掉回没套规则前的样子，属正常现象，不是 bug。\r\n- **冻结只对「能编辑的单值字段」生效。** 如果一个被冻结的字段后来变成了列表或分组（例如两项的列表被剧情又加了一项、或规则的路径本来就指向一整组数据），修改器会安全地跳过这条规则，绝不会拿冻结的旧值去顶替整个列表/分组；🎛 修改器页「上一回合」那行的「跳过 N 项」会体现这种情况。想继续冻结，把规则删掉、在字段变回单值之后重新点一次 🔒 即可。\r\n\r\n## 📖 世界书模式（Lorebook）\r\n\r\n**聊**世界书（里面写了什么、设定在哪条、有无矛盾、怎么扩写），或让它**直接改**世界书。进入后标题下方有一条工具栏：\r\n\r\n- **选书**：默认「当前激活的全部世界书」，也可**勾选某一本或几本**（支持多选）。\r\n- **条目选择器**：默认发整本，可展开后用复选框只挑几条发给神谕（带筛选 + 全选 / 仅蓝灯 / 仅绿灯 等快捷键，**👁 内容预览** 可每条显示一行摘要）。\r\n- **🪄 智能选条（1.54.0 起）**：条目选择器工具栏上的 🪄 按钮——**用人话下勾选指令**（「把讲战争线的绿灯条目全勾上」「取消所有涉及感情戏的」「《某某书》整本取消」…，机械条件与内容语义随意组合）。AI 读一份浓缩目录来定方案；拿不准时会自己在书里做**免费的关键词检索**、或调出个别条目原文细看（**最多两轮**，每轮都在窗口里明说，绝不静默多花钱）。结果先给你一张**预检卡**：将勾选 / 取消哪些、每条为什么、它搜了什么词、有没有它编出来的假 uid（会被剔除并标明）——点【应用】才真正生效，点【还原】一键回到之前的勾选。它**只动勾选、绝不改书的内容**；勾选的含义与手动勾选完全一致（应用改动时仍读整本书）。只影响发给 AI 的内容，应用时仍读整本，编辑任何条目都照常生效。**（1.40.1 起）你的勾选会按书名记住、刷新与重开都还在**，不用每次重勾；把某本书**整本勾满**会自动回到「发整本」状态——这样以后往这本书里新增的条目会自动被包含，而不是被旧勾选挡在外面。想只发整本，点「全选」即可。**（1.58.0 起）流式直播**：如果你的「流式」设置开着，🪄 工作时会在窗口里**边写边看** AI 的原文——它在想什么、搜什么、拟什么方案都实时可见（看的时候往上翻不会被拽回底部）；写完照旧出预检卡。流式关着则和以前一样只显示进度行。\r\n\r\n要求改动时，神谕会用中文说明改了什么，并附 `<LorebookEdit>` 区块（**分隔格式**而非 JSON，长正文放进 `<<<content … content>>>` 围栏里原样书写、无需转义）。四种操作：`create` 新建、`edit` 整条覆盖、`patch`（默认——「开头几字 || 结尾几字」锚定只换一段）、`delete`。随后出现 **将改动应用到世界书** 按钮：通过 ST 的 `saveWorldInfo` 写回、逐条列出结果、可一键**撤销**；找不到的 uid / 锚点会**安全跳过并说明原因**，绝不半途写入。锚点匹配对细小差异很皮实（v1.19.2 起）：跨中文破折号（——）、引号风格不同（「」/『』/“”/\"）、顿号↔逗号等标点小差异都能命中；仍未命中时，提示会建议改用「起始 || 结尾」两端锚点再试。正文**原样保存、不做宏替换**（`{{user}}` 等保持原样，不会把名字写死进书）。新建条目默认开「非递归」。\r\n\r\n**应用前预检（1.53.0 起）。** 回复里带 `<LorebookEdit>` 时，「将改动应用到世界书」按钮上方会先出现**逐条预检行**：能应用的照常；锚点没找到 / 命中多处的**当场置灰并写明原因**，不用点了应用才发现；条目其实在另一本已勾选的书里会自动改锚并注明「已改锚到《书名》」；目标是**常驻**条目时有 ⚠ 提示（常驻条目通常是你的核心设定，改前多看一眼）。配套几条更聪明的守卫：同一锚点在条目里**命中多处**时不再默默改第一处，而是跳过并提示把锚点写得更独特；补丁其实**早已生效**时直接告知「无需重试」（不会反复空试）；`create` 撞上**同名条目**自动转为编辑该条（不再造出重复条目）；**没有关键词**的新条目自动设为常驻（否则它永远不会被注入）；跨多段的长锚点现在**整段命中**（旧版只命中首段、会留下半替换残余）。此外神谕每次作答都拿着**最新保存的书文快照与上次应用结果**——「帮我确认改动都写进去了吗」这类核对**以当前存档为准**，不再凭记忆瞎猜。\r\n\r\n**体积读数（1.62.0 起）。** 条目选择器的汇总行现在除了条数，还会给出**这次大约会发出去多少 token**（`条目：全部（449） · 约 88 万 token`），随勾选实时变。**超过约 10 万 token 时这个数字会变红**——提醒你这一发很可能超出模型的上下文上限而被拒（世界书模式发的是**整本选中的内容**，与酒馆自己的「世界书激活预算」无关，禁用的条目也照发）。红了并**不会阻止你发送**，只是提醒；想降下来就用条目选择器或 🪄 智能选条少挑几条。数字是估算值，故标「约」。\r\n\r\n> 整本注入 token 可能较大，条目多时用条目选择器只挑几条即可。\r\n\r\n## 🧭 剧情参谋模式（Story Advisor）⚠ 实验性\r\n\r\n和神谕一起**构思剧情接下来怎么走**，并可一键让主聊天**被悄悄引导**。神谕会按你在设置里选的**上下文深度**与**世界书**范围读取对话与设定（**剧情概要**始终读取），据此找沉睡的伏笔、未兑现的线索、人物弧光的下一步，把可落地的走向列成**方案卡片**（`<StoryPlan>`：目标 + 起始迹象 + 契合点）。若先在普通模式聊出了感觉，切过来会有【🧭 把刚才的讨论整理成方案】按钮。回复中的 **Markdown**（加粗 / 标题 / 列表 / 表格）会正常渲染（1.18.2 起；表格 1.18.4 起），原始 `<StoryPlan>` 块以等宽小块原样展示、采纳卡片照旧。\r\n\r\n在卡片上选**强度**（**只铺垫** / **自然推进** / **尽快引爆**）→【开始引导】，方案就作为一条幕后指令注入主聊天（ST 的 `setExtensionPrompt`，深度在「参谋设置」里调，1.77.5 起；模型不听引导就调低，最低 0）。之后**正常 RP 即可**——主线会逐步把剧情推向该方向，且**用户行动永远优先**（你偏离时它跟随）。采用后顶部出现**方案条**（关掉窗口会变成可拖动的「🧭 引导中」悬浮标签），可随时切强度、查看注入原文、或【完成】/【放弃】。方案存在**当前聊天**里，刷新 / 切换聊天都不丢、绝不串台。\r\n\r\n**✏️ 编辑注入内容（1.48 起）。** 方案条上的 **✏️**（预览收着时它也在）可以把注入主聊天的那段幕后指令**整份改写**——想补的细节、想禁的写法，直接写进去、点【保存】立刻生效（刷新页面也还在）。其中「**节奏：**」那一行**保持原样**时，上方三个强度档**照常可切**（只替换那一行，你写的其它内容一字不动）；一旦你**改动或删掉**那一行，就当作「节奏也自己定了」，强度档随即**置灰**（说明行会写明原因）。想找回自动生成的文本，点编辑器里的【**恢复默认**】（当前档位保留）。编辑期间强度档也暂时置灰——换档会重画方案条，把还没保存的字冲掉。自定义**随本次方案生灭**：【完成】/【放弃】/ 换一个方案都会清掉。\r\n\r\n**故事弧线（长线引导）⚠ 实验性。** 把单步方案升级成**多拍长线**：先定一条**贯穿线**（整条弧要讲的事），之后一拍接一拍走，每次过渡由一次后台调用现编下一拍注入主聊天，直到贯穿线**真正收束**才结束。新建时填表选**模式**（**透明** = 你看得到每拍指令；**盲盒** = 只看到给玩家的目标，幕后意图藏在剧透模糊后）、贯穿线、路标、篇幅、**难度**（平和 / 常规 / 凛冽，越高赌注越大，但「退出」永远在不可逆转折之前可达）、红线。任何时候都能【退出】、主聊天即刻复原。\r\n\r\n**1.71.0 起弧线也有 ✏️**：改的是**当前这一拍**的注入指令，用法与上面单步方案的编辑完全相同（「节奏：」行保持原样则强度档照常可切、【恢复默认】找回自动生成、保存立刻生效且刷新不丢）。【完成】/【换个思路】现编出**新的一拍**时回到自动生成——新拍新指令，不满意可以再改。**盲盒弧线**下点 ✏️ 会直接**看到幕后指令（含剧透）**，想保住盲盒体验就别点它；另外编辑只改注入的文本本身，给玩家看的目标和「✓ 目标已达成」的判定**都不受影响**。\r\n\r\n> ⚠ 弧线比单步方案更吃模型与 token（每拍都通读整段历史 + 世界书），建议配**较强的模型**（DeepSeek / Gemini Pro / Opus）；流式、超时取消、📡 实时输出都已内置。\r\n\r\n**序列引导（预写一整段长线，逐拍推进）1.72 起。** 单步方案一次只引导一个目标，弧线是「定个大方向、每拍现编」；**序列引导**介于两者之间——你和参谋把一整段长线剧情（一个学年、一卷、一段旅程）**聊到定稿**，参谋就把它排成**一条有序的拍列表**：每一拍与单步方案完全同规格（目标 + 起始迹象 + 契合点），**全部摊开可见、没有任何隐藏内容**。点卡片上的【**开始序列引导**】一次采用整条；**采用时不问强度**，逐拍默认「自然推进」，之后在方案条上按拍调。\r\n\r\n采用后**同一时间只有当前这一拍在引导主聊天**，演完点【**完成**】换下一拍——**换拍是纯翻页：不调模型、不花 token**（每一拍的注入指令在采用时就已经写好了，与单步方案由同一套逻辑生成，引导质量一模一样）。**1.75 起，引导指令与状态行会并入你自己的那条消息再发出**（不改聊天记录、你看不到；提示词查看器里看到的仍是贴合前的样子），这样无论走官方 DeepSeek、自定义中转还是 Claude / Gemini，模型看到的位置都一样——长聊天里「尽快引爆没反应」「落拍感应不响」的问题就是这么来的。状态行写在回复最末尾，若你的回复长度上限（max tokens）卡得很紧、模型写到一半被截断，它会是第一个丢掉的——落拍感应偶尔不响先看看这个。方案条条头显示「第 X / Y 拍」，条体是当前拍的目标 + 三档强度 + ✏️，下面是**拍列表**：✓ 已完成 / ▶ 进行中 / ○ 待播 / ⤫ 已跳过，点任意一行展开它的目标 / 起始迹象 / 契合点；**待播的拍每行带 ✏️ 与【跳过】**（改注入内容、或让它不上场），已完成 / 已跳过的行只读。✏️ 的规则与单步方案、弧线完全一致（「节奏：」行保持原样时强度档照常可切、【恢复默认】找回自动生成的版本、保存立刻生效且刷新不丢）。\r\n\r\n想**大改**（重排、加拍减拍、换个方向）就点【**💬 找参谋改改**】：**点它什么都不会被拆掉**——当前这一拍照常引导着主聊天，只是自动开窗、回到参谋房，参谋会先说一句「你当前在第 X / Y 拍……」接着聊。聊好后它会把**剩余的拍**重新列一张卡给你，采用它 = **只替换当前拍往后的部分**，已完成 / 已跳过的历史一拍都不动（被替换掉的那些拍上的 ✏️ 自定义也随之作废——新拍新内容）。第 1 拍还没开演就找参谋改，实际效果就是整条换新。整条不想要了点【**放弃**】（会先确认一次，比单步方案损失大）。\r\n\r\n> ⚠ **每条聊天同一时间只能有一个引导构件**：单步方案 / 弧线 / 序列三选一。采用序列会替换掉在跑的方案或弧线；反过来，序列还有没演完的拍时去采用单步方案或新建弧线，会**先弹一次确认**再丢弃。序列的状态（每一拍演到哪了、你改过的注入文本）都存在**当前聊天**里，刷新 / 切换聊天不丢、绝不串台。\r\n\r\n**🧭 数据库联动（实验）1.78 起。** 同时装了 **SP·数据库** 且开着它的「**剧情推进**」的人才需要这一项。数据库的剧情推进会在每次发送前跑一个自己的「规划器」，把接下来该怎么走的规划写进你的消息里——但那个规划器**看不到参谋的引导**，于是常常各说各话，主模型更听写在你消息里的那份，参谋就像被「顶掉」了。勾上参谋条「参谋设置」里的 **数据库联动（实验）**，故事神谕会在数据库开始规划之前把**当前引导**附给它的规划器看一眼、规划完再原样拿走：**发给主模型的提示词与只装数据库时逐字节相同**，你的消息、聊天记录、世界书一字不改。只在你的消息是最新一条、正常发送（非重掷 / 重滑 / 自动触发）时才动作；没装数据库时勾着也不会做任何事（勾选框下面会显示有没有检测到数据库）。\r\n> 说明：这是一个过渡方案，靠事件先后次序工作。我们同时挂出了一个只读接口（见下方「扩展开发接口」），并已向数据库作者提出让它的规划器直接读取参谋引导的建议；一旦对方接入，这项勾选就不再需要。引导文本里若含 `$8`、`{{…}}` 这类数据库自己的占位符写法，附给规划器的那份副本会做无害处理（主模型读到的引导不受影响）。\r\n> 进阶（1.84 起，默认关）：如果你反而希望引导**留在**你的消息里一起发给主模型（份量更重），`index.js` 顶部有一行 `const ENABLE_DB_BRIDGE_KEEP = false;`，改成 `true` 后参谋条会多出一个子勾选框「发给主模型前剥掉引导块」，取消勾选即保留。代价请先知道：引导会随数据库的改写**存进聊天记录**（之后每轮都作为历史重发）、发送时贴进你消息的那份引导会因重复而整轮不贴、盲盒拍的隐藏目标会出现在你自己的消息里。只建议清楚这些后果的人开启（来自社区 PR #1，作者 f1luct）。\r\n\r\n**🧭 下一拍建议 1.87 起（仅在序列引导进行中生效）。** 序列引导把剧情一拍一拍往前推，但轮到你说话时，不一定马上想得到「这一拍该怎么接」。勾上参谋条「参谋设置」里的 **下一拍建议**，序列在跑时主聊天**最新一条回复**下方会出现一张小卡（写着第几拍、这一拍的目标）：\r\n- 点「**生成建议**」→ 神谕发一次请求，给出 4~7 条候选：**3 条「我」**（你自己的动作 / 台词）、**1~3 条在场角色**（写成「角色名：……」，发出去就是让那个角色这么做）、**0~1 条「时间」**（需要换场或跳时间时才给）。这一拍离正文末尾还隔着地点、时间或关系的变化时，候选里会有一条先写「中间那一步」；**分镜 / 转场拍**（拍标题里带「分镜」「转场」「切到」「视角切」「B线」「支线」）玩家不在那个场景，不给「我」。\r\n- **点一条 = 填进输入框**：输入框空着就直接放进去；已经打了字，就接在后面另起一行——**不会覆盖你的字，也不会替你发送**，改一改再发即可。「填入整段」把全部候选按行放进去；「重新生成」换一批；生成中可以点「停止」。\r\n- 它读的是：**这一拍的引导指令原文**（和主模型收到的一模一样，包括你用 ✏️ 改过的内容）、**角色卡与你的人设**（跟随「带角色卡」设置）、**世界书里这次被正文或引导点名的「绿灯」条目**（跟随「世界书」范围设置：关 = 不带；「自定义」= 只带你勾选的条目）、以及**刚写完的那条回复**（默认截取末尾 4000 字）。用的是神谕自己的连接；参谋模式勾了「套用我的补全预设」且选着内置破限时，它也一样套上。\r\n- 结果存在**当前聊天**里：刷新页面还在；换一个 swipe、改了那条回复、或者这一拍完成 / 改动了，旧候选就会作废、回到「生成建议」。玩家已经发出下一句（最新一条是你自己的消息）时不显示。**只在序列引导进行中出现**——单步方案、弧线、没有引导时都没有这张卡。\r\n- 「**下一拍建议 · 更多设置**」里：**每条新回复自动生成**（默认关；打开后每条回复多花一次 API 调用，会等自动校正 / 自动诊断跑完再生成）、**喂给它的最新回复最多截取多少字**（100–20000，默认 4000）、**选项写法**（附在请求里的额外要求，默认是一份通用写法；可改写、「↺ 恢复默认」、「✕ 清空」＝不附）。\r\n> 来源：社区插件「故事神谕 · 下一拍建议」（作者 **棉花娃娃**，GitHub：yacovonebeswick-art），经作者同意并入本体；并入时把作者自用的玩家人设（「普通人」口吻、冷淡文风等）改成了跟随你自己的人设与角色卡。之前装了**独立版**插件的朋友请在扩展管理里停用它——同时开着会在每条回复下出现两张卡（神谕检测到它时，设置提示里会提醒你）。\r\n\r\n## ✨ 校正模式（Reply Fixer）\r\n\r\n专门「修」**最新一条 AI 回复**：清掉 AI 八股套话、机械对白、过度精确的「数学论文腔」、把魔法写成理科、拖沓流水账，也能执行你定的角色知识边界 / 剧情护栏。**改动一律作为新的 swipe（重摇）应用**——原回复永远在「向左划一下」的地方；回复里的 `<UpdateVariable>` 区块会原样接回，**绝不弄坏 MVU 数值或状态栏**。若这张卡的美化是**一整份网页**（主聊天里由酒馆助手渲成内嵌页面），校正稿卡片会改用**纯文本排版**显示正文、不再摊出那份 HTML 源码；美化照旧，点 **[应用]** 之后在主聊天里就能看到（v1.84.1）。\r\n\r\n「校正设置」面板顶部有个下拉，切换**手动 / 去 AI 味 / 自定义**三套用法：\r\n\r\n- **🖐 手动** —— 直接在输入框**用人话说要改哪里**（「这段对话写口语点」「把这句删掉」）。只动最新这条、只改你点名处，其余不动——回复里的状态栏 / 面板 / 图生标记等**结构块也默认原样保留**（除非你点名要改它里面的内容）。**默认精简上下文**：只发这条回复 + 角色卡，不带前文 / 世界书 / 概要（弱模型高上下文下易认错要改的楼层，需要时在面板里再逐项勾开）。改完先给一张**校正稿卡片**，满意再点 **[应用]**（这才变成 swipe）。\r\n- **🤖 去 AI 味** —— 专治「一读就知道是 AI 写的」：**勾选长期想清理的目标**（5 个开关：AI 八股 / 套话、对话机械、过度精确、**魔法被写成理科**（仅奇幻，默认关）、描写拖沓 / 流水账——其余四项默认开），选**强度**（轻校默认 / 精校更彻底 + 按模型选侧重），可再填**角色知识边界 / 剧情护栏**约束、设**排除区**（保留 = 强制原样保留自动没认出的块；丢弃 = 直接删掉，如 `<thinking>`）——这些和作用域 / 套餐都收在**「进阶设置」**折叠里。两种触发：点 **[按目标给最新回复去 AI 味]** 跑一次（**流式直播**校正稿，停止键可随时中断），或勾 **[每条新回复自动去 AI 味]** 常驻后台跑（✨ 图标染金为提示）。\r\n- **📋 自定义（v1.77.0）** —— 下拉第三档：**用你自己的模板处理每条新回复**（例：正文自动翻译成日文）。模板**只写要做的事**，输出格式与保留标记由神谕自动附上；一个聊天里「每条新回复」要么跑校正、要么跑一份模板，二选一。「**沿用校正的正文识别**」勾选：开 = 只处理剧情正文，状态栏 / 变量块等原样保留；关 = 整条回复交给模板、输出原样替换（原文仍留 swipe 0）——**保留区 / 丢弃区两边都留空**时整条逐字节原样交给模板，任一区填了东西就先按区抠取再送。整条模式下神谕会额外要求模型原样保留所有标签与结构块，但**能不能守住取决于模型**——带状态栏 / 变量块的卡建议保持「沿用识别」开着（它藏起变量块，但认不出结构时包裹标签仍会交给模型）；本档有自己的保留区 / 丢弃区；同一标签两边都填按保留处理。**最少字数**（正文短于它就不发起调用）在自定义面板里设，**与自动共用同一个值**（自动面板一直没有这个框），改一边两边都变。长回复记得抬高「进阶设置 → 校正输出上限」：日中镜像这类会把字数翻倍的模板，DeepSeek 约每字 1.4 token、Claude 类约 2.0 token——4096 的地板在 2–3 千字的普通回复上就会截断（截断会被拦下不落 swipe），8 千字楼层用 Claude 类要 15k 以上。示例模板：`把 <text_to_transform> 里的叙事正文逐句完整翻译成自然的日文；对白引号用「」；{{user}} 与 {{char}} 的名字按原文保留。`\r\n\r\n  **📦 内置示例（就在模板下拉里）** —— 下拉里自带两份内置示例（名字后带「**（示例）**」，排在最下面的「内置示例」一组里），选中就能用；改过再按保存会另存成你自己的一份，示例本身不会变。两份分别是「**对白更生动+旁白去味（示例）**」（把对白改得像活人开口、顺手清掉旁白里的套话，人物 / 事件 / 名字一个不动）与「**排版美化·对白气泡（示例）**」（一个字都不改，只把每行对白排进一个小气泡、加轻量分隔）。两份都在 DeepSeek V4 Pro 与 Gemini 3.1 Pro 上真跑过多轮；**两条已知边界**：① 对白模板遇到**不带「名字：」前缀、靠叙述交代谁在说话**的卡时，DeepSeek 基本只做「旁白去味」那一半、引号里的话一字不动（Gemini 两半都做）；② 排版模板遇到 `“…”某某说，“…”` 这种把动作句夹在两段引号中间的写法时，DeepSeek 会把中间那个逗号「修」成句号、并把「某某说，」删掉（Gemini 正常）。都是模型习惯，换模型即可。\r\n\r\n  **怎么写一份模板**（这两份就是照这几条写出来的）：\r\n\r\n  - 写「**改完之后是什么样**」，别写「先做什么再做什么」；输出格式、标签、锚点都不用写——神谕会自己加。\r\n  - 每句话都要对得上一个**真会出问题的地方**；没出过问题的先别写。\r\n  - 要保住的东西写成**看得见的样子**（「行首仍是名字加冒号」「逗号句号照旧」）比写原则（「不要改」）管用。\r\n  - 一种版式**只给一个骨架**，别给多种；骨架本身要亮暗主题都能读（半透明灰、不设字色）。\r\n  - **不要**把范例正文或「理想输出」贴进模板，**不要给概念起名字**——模型会把它们原样抄进正文。\r\n  - 不同模型会往不同方向填空（有的爱压缩、会丢专名；有的顺手「修」标点）；**模板改不掉的模型习惯就换模型或接受**，别一句句加码——专为某家写的句子常让它更偏。\r\n  - **只加标记不改字**的模板，输出得比原文长得够多（气泡的 `style` 属性就够），否则「无需处理」闸会把稿子拦下不落。\r\n  - 300–600 字够用；两份内置示例分别是 451 字和 593 字。\r\n\r\n  **🌐 模板广场（v1.86.0）** —— 模板行最右边的按钮：\r\n\r\n  > **目前 🌐 广场暂停开放**（按钮暂时不显示），「一键投稿」已取消。**📤 分享** 照常可用：复制分享文本，发到神谕 Discord 的模板分享频道就行。\r\n\r\n  - **🌐 广场**（暂停中）：大家分享、作者审核过的模板都在这里。上面可以按**标签**筛、按名字 / 作者 / 说明**搜索**；每条都写着版本号、作者（没署名显示「匿名」）和测试过的模型。「**预览**」展开全文，「**下载**」把它存成你自己的一份模板并直接选中（和你已有的模板重名时自动改成「名字（2）」）。你正在改的模板还没保存时，下载前会先问你要不要放弃改动。作者出了新版本，按钮会变成「**有新版本**」，可以选**覆盖本地那份**或**另存一份**。广场连不上时会先显示上次存下的离线副本。\r\n  - **📤 分享**：先在下拉里选中**你自己保存过的**模板（内置示例和没保存的改动不能分享，点了会提示原因），再填作者（可不填）、一句话说明、1–3 个标签、测试过的模型，点「**复制分享文本**」，把复制到的内容发到神谕 Discord 的模板分享频道就行。分享出去的模板是**公开的**，任何人都能拿去用。广场开放时，改进过已分享的模板可以勾上「这是对已分享模板的更新」并选中原来那条。\r\n  - 广场里的文字只当普通文字显示，下载来的模板不会执行任何代码，也不碰你的聊天、世界书和变量。\r\n\r\n> 💰 自动模式默认只发回复正文 + 目标，并带**禁词预筛 + 字数下限**——回复本就干净 / 太短时**根本不发起调用**，不会每条烧 token。\r\n\r\n自动改完会**应用为新 swipe** 并在侧聊留记录，带 **[用原文]**（划回原稿）/ **[看改动]**（逐字对比）。配置**按当前聊天保存**，还能存成具名**套餐**（如「硬核西幻」）一键复用。\r\n\r\n> 🔀 **v1.77.0 行为变更**：**切换聊天不再取消进行中的校正 / 模板处理**——已经买单的那一份结果会先暂存，等你**回到那个聊天时自动落地**（半小时内回来都算数，超时或刷新页面会丢；最多同时暂存 8 个聊天的结果）。以前切走就等于整轮作废、钱白花。🩺 自动诊断与 🎛 变量修改器仍照旧在切聊天时作废（它们写的是当前聊天的变量状态）。\r\n\r\n> 🎯 **自动识别（v1.17.16 起，v1.18.3 加「检测收据」）**：自动模式只改**正文**——正文在哪个包裹标签里（`<content>`、`<gametxt>`、`<正文>`…）会**自动识别并按聊天记住**，正文内外的状态栏 / 选项 / 面板 / 图生指令等结构块**不送模型、原样原位保留**；认不准的卡它会**问你一次**（面板「✋ 需要确认」点一下）。**常见格式开箱即用**；格式特别的卡打开「进阶设置」看**检测收据**（本条实际识别到的块），认漏的点一下固定进保留区——也欢迎把那条回复原文在 **Discord 私信 @Prince**，会加进测试集修复。**判定预览行**随时告诉你「这条回复会被怎么处理」；你**手填**的标签不会被自动覆盖；配乱了点「**恢复推荐设置**」一键还原（会一并清掉已确认的正文形态）。\r\n\r\n## 🎭 角色工坊模式（Character Builder）\r\n\r\n跟神谕聊几句就能把一个角色从零打磨成完整设定——写进世界书里的一条 **NPC** 条目，或者把**你自己扮演的角色**写成一份给 AI「读」的说明书（完善当前 Persona / 另存新 Persona）。和其它模式一样**不碰主聊天**；唯一的输出只在最后一步 **写入** 时才真正落盘，随时可**撤销**。\r\n\r\n> ✅ **用户角色（Persona）目标已回归（v1.76.0）**：角色卡是给 AI「演」的，用户信息是给 AI「读」的——所以用户角色走的是**专门的一套访谈与锻造模板**（行为翻译手册式：每一行要么是硬事实，要么是「TA 做什么＝什么意思」的翻译，台词只收对话记录里你真打过的原句），不套 NPC 那套。\r\n\r\n- **目标下拉**：三选一——**NPC 世界书条目** / **用户角色·抢话**（AI 也会替你的角色行动、说话，「AI 同时扮演 {{user}}」的玩法选它）/ **用户角色·不抢话**（AI 只回应你，绝不替你行动）。两种用户角色各有自己的章节 chip 和独立的访谈房间，切换目标就换房间、互不串档。选 NPC 时，是全新 NPC、改已有条目、还是剧情里出现过但还没写进书里的角色，由**访谈师**在聊天里问你确认。\r\n- **草稿包含**：一排可勾选的章节 chip，决定这次要写哪些内容——**勾选＝送进锻造工序，没勾的章节会从锻造提示词里物理删除**（访谈师不问、锻造不写、也不会「顺手」多写，所见即所得）。默认开：基本信息 / 外貌特征 / 背景经历 / 人际关系 / 性格画像 / 说话方式 / 目标动机 / 深层人格 / 防误读提示；默认关：弱点缺陷 / 能力技能（排在普通章节末尾），以及最后带**虚线边**的**进阶三件**：多副面孔 / 言行反差 / 点睛比喻（勾选前有一行「简单 / 喜剧调剂角色留空」提示）。桌面端鼠标停在 chip 上看说明；手机上点「草稿包含」旁的 **「？」** 看完整图例（顶部有进阶三件的取舍指引）。\r\n- **上下文**：世界书多选 + 条目选择器（同世界书模式的机制）——**角色类条目通常是绿灯**（关键词触发），要编辑或参考某个已有角色务必**先勾上它所在的那本书**，不然锻造读不到；上下文深度（数字 + 「全部」勾选）往上调到能看见该角色出场的位置为止（长聊天开「全部」比较吃 token）；「带上 📜 剧情概要」；「带上状态栏数据」（世界里有数值化角色设定时有用）；「**关键词触发世界书**」（默认关，v1.31.0）——开了会额外跑一次 ST 关键词扫描，把主聊天 / 访谈侧聊里**提到**的设定条目（蓝灯 + 命中绿灯）作为参考补充喂给访谈师和锻造，**已勾选的条目不会重复投喂**，你勾的书 / 条目仍是唯一权威。**默认（没在选条目器里手动勾过的那本书）只喂它当前【启用】的条目**——禁用条目在列表里显示成未勾选、也不会发出去；手动勾选之后发的就是你勾的那几条（含禁用），「全选」＝连禁用一起发（v1.82.0）。条目列表的汇总行还带**体积读数**（「约 X token」，过 10 万标红提醒，只提示不拦截）。\r\n- **锻造回复上限**：锻造调用的 max_tokens，留空 = 自动（下限 16384，v1.29.0 起；v1.23.0 起曾 12288，更早 8192 时全章节的重型锻造约半数会被「思考+成稿」截断）。还嫌不够时可再调高——但超过服务商的单次输出上限会被直接拒绝，报错就调回来。另注：巨型世界书吃的是**输入**上下文（受模型上下文窗口限制），要精简靠条目选择器和上下文深度，这个旋钮管不到输入侧。\r\n- **用自定义预设**：勾选后**访谈对话**走你在设置面板策展的酒馆预设（文本块保留、RP 标记去除）；**锻造调用不受影响**，始终使用内置锻造工序。\r\n- **锻造后自动精简**（v1.30.0，默认关）：锻造成功后自动跑一遍「✂️ 精简」。只在 NPC 草稿、且原稿明显冗长（长句密集）时才触发；守卫不过 = 原稿原样保留，一行注记说明原因。强输出模型（如 Claude）建议开。\r\n- **台词丰满**（v1.34.0，默认关）：锻造时把台词写成**当面说出口的完整人话**——保留角色个性与说话习惯，话少的角色照旧话少、但开口的句子完整不碎。嫌锻造稿台词干就开它；个性、条数、卡片结构不受影响。\r\n- **深度精简恒串行·流式**：「✂️✂️ 深度精简」的 3 份分节 + 手术单**一份接一份**地跑（不再有并行/串行开关），任何时刻只有一个请求在天上——不撞公益站的并发限流，流式的持续字节流也扛得住会掐长请求的代理。进度实时铺在气泡里。v1.35.4 起分节与手术单的内部思考同样加了**一遍成稿纪律**（台词保护原样焊死）：爱反复推敲的强推理模型不再把分节想到超时截断——此前偶发的「精简未采纳：第 N 份分节没有有效围栏」正是这么来的，实测该故障从 1/3 概率降到 0/3，整轮耗时约减半。\r\n- **✂️ 精简全稿 / ✂️✂️ 深度精简 / 原稿切换**（v1.30.0，草稿卡按钮）：把冗长的锻造稿拆短句、删跨节重复——台词、章节结构、状态行、画面与衍生的实体一律原样保留，整套守卫兜底，任何一道不过就自动回落原稿。成功后卡上出现**「原稿 ⇄ 精简稿」**切换钮（●标当前侧），**写入和修订都以当前显示的版本为准**；切回**原稿**侧时两个精简按钮仍在——想换一档重跑随时可以（重跑覆盖旧精简稿）；对精简稿提修订后，两个版本收敛为修订后那一份（切换钮收起）。\r\n\r\n> 💡 chip 就是这份设定的「体量旋钮」——全勾默认打出来的是**主角级**完整设定（约 2000 字）。**排在最后的进阶三件（多副面孔 / 言行反差 / 点睛比喻）默认关**，勾给**有内在层次**的角色；喜剧调剂 / 纯功能 / 简单直给的角色**留空就好**。是否需要由**你**决定——**勾了＝一定做，不勾＝一定不做**（不再由模型自己判断适不适合）；给一个简单角色勾上进阶件，锻造会照做、硬造出它本没有的复杂。打个酱油的次要 NPC，连**深层人格**也可以关掉，一盘清爽的调色盘就够了。\r\n\r\n描述完你想要的角色，访谈师只会追问**答得上来的客观信息**（外貌、年龄、性别、身份、性格梗概……），一次 2-3 个问题，你的描述 / 已勾的世界书 / 聊天记录里写明的东西不会重复问。信息够了会出一张**〈角色简报〉**摘要卡，点 **「🔨 生成」** 才真正开始锻造——之前不会有任何调用。\r\n\r\n> 💰 锻造是**一次较重的调用**：会读入你配置的全部上下文，先在世界书里找有没有**角色生成规则**（命名规矩、种族限制、数值模板……），找到就当**硬性约束**照办；打磨过程在内部完成，你只会看到成品，粗略估算输出量是普通回复的 2-3 倍。这次调用只在你点「生成」时才发生，绝不自动触发。v1.35.3 起锻造的内部思考加了**一遍成稿纪律**——爱反复推敲的强推理模型（如 Claude Opus 一类）不再把五道工序整个重想一遍，锻造明显更快更省（实测该类模型耗时/输出砍半），成品质量与结构不变。\r\n\r\n> ⚠ **Claude Fable 5 用户注意（v1.76.0 发版时实测）**：锻造工序要求模型把思考写进 `<thinking>` 标签，Fable 5 的安全层会把这条指令判成「提取模型推理」而**整条拒答**（NPC 与用户角色目标都中招，navy / routera 两条路一样，navy 上表现为「content filter」）——锻造会得到空回复。请给工坊换一个模型（Opus / Sonnet / DeepSeek / Gemini 均正常）；访谈不受影响。\r\n\r\n> ⏳ 🔨 锻造与 ✂️✂️ 深度精简都是**后台保活**调用（锻造 v1.35.2 起、深度精简 v1.36.0 起）：发出后切到别的模式**不会中断**它们——后台照常跑，回到工坊房间时流式气泡自动接上，完成后成稿按原始房间落盘归位（人不在场不弹打扰通知，回房自见）。生成期间发送键显示为 ⏹ 停止键，点它仍会中止；**切换聊天**或清空该房间的侧聊记录也会中止（结果属于旧聊天，不会写进新聊天）。\r\n\r\n草稿出现在**窗口顶部「角色工坊」面板底部的常驻卡片**里——锻造完成会自动把收起的面板展开（v1.19.2 起；之后想再看，点「角色工坊」标题展开即可）。刷新页面、切走再回来都还在，按聊天各自保存。锻造稿收尾的小滑手能自动救回（v1.19.2 起）：漏了闭合标签、闭合多打了几个 `>` 都不再白丢一稿；思考区块忘了闭合也不会把成稿吞成「(空回复)」。想改就直接说要改哪里——神谕会先**用普通文字引用原句、给出替换建议**征求你确认；全部确认、你说**「改完了」**之后才输出**唯一一个**补丁、**一次性逐字精确**地套进草稿，且**只含你确认过的修改**（不会重新整篇改写，也不会夹带没让它改的地方）。补丁锚定和世界书补丁同样皮实——跨「——」、引号风格不同、标点小差异都能命中。满意就点 **「写入」**；**「🔨 重新锻造」**整份推倒重来；**「放弃草稿」**直接清空。\r\n\r\n写入会在目标世界书里**新建一条**（或**改写**你选定的已有条目），并自动配 3-5 个触发关键词；用户角色目标则写进**当前 Persona 的描述**（完善当前角色）或**另存为一个新 Persona**（默认头像，可在 Persona 面板换），同样一键可撤销。\r\n\r\n> ⚠ **撤销只在这次会话里有效**——刷新页面、切换聊天、修订生效后（改稿套进草稿）、或点「重新锻造」都会让上一次写入的撤销失效。写入后尽早核对，不对就趁早撤销。\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 侧聊历史与运行概要\r\n\r\n- **侧聊历史按聊天持久化**：每个聊天各存自己的一份，关窗 / 刷新 / 切走再回来都不丢；只有点标题栏 🗑 **清空**才清掉当前聊天的。\r\n- **每模式独立侧聊房间（1.28.0）**：普通聊天 / 诊断 / 世界书 / 参谋 / 校正 五个模式**各存各的一份侧聊历史**，切模式即换成该模式自己的记录——普通聊天里的闲聊不会混进诊断，反之亦然；每份都按聊天持久化、跨刷新存活，非普通模式的记录顶部有一行「本模式独立保存」提示。进**参谋**时若普通聊天已有讨论，会出现一个一键「**导入普通聊天的讨论并整理成方案**」按钮，把刚才的闲聊搬进参谋房再帮你整理成方案卡（参谋始终会通读真正的主聊天剧情，这个按钮只是把侧聊里的讨论一并带上）。\r\n- **运行概要（📜，在「⋯ 更多」菜单）**：把剧情关键背景写成一段概要，存进当前聊天，之后在普通聊天与参谋模式下插在最近对话**正前方**喂给神谕——长 RP 里给它补全局背景。诊断模式不带；世界书模式勾「同时带上最近剧情对话」时一并带上（1.46.0 起）。\r\n\r\n## 对话操作\r\n\r\n鼠标移到任意消息上，气泡角落出现小按钮：**你的消息**可 ✎ 编辑（保存并重新生成）/ 🗑 删除；**神谕的回复**可 ↻ 重新生成 / 🗑 删除。删除前会弹确认框（1.22 起；删除提问时若其后紧跟神谕回复会提示一并删除；出错气泡直接删、不打扰）。**发送失败时**（如共用 key 被 `429` 挡回），出错气泡上会显示常驻的 **↻ 重试**，点一下即可重发、不必重打（手机尤其方便）。**Enter 发送还是换行，跟随酒馆「用户设置 → 按 Enter 发送」（1.85.1 起）**：默认「自动（PC）」＝电脑上 Enter 发送、Shift+Enter 换行，手机上 Enter 换行、点发送按钮发出；想在手机上也 Enter 直接发送就改成「已启用」，想电脑上也只用按钮发就改成「已禁用」。用中文输入法按回车选词 / 上屏不会误发。\r\n\r\n**📥 导出 / 📤 导入对话（1.60.0 导出、1.61.0 导入 + 换位）。** 聊得尽兴想留档？**神谕回复气泡下的操作行**（复制/删除那排）里有 **📥 导出** 和 **📤 导入** 两个小按钮：导出把当前页面的问答往返存成一个 **Markdown 文件**下载到本地（【我】/【神谕】逐轮排版，参谋模式的 `<StoryPlan>` 卡原文保留；系统记录不掺入；文件名带模式、聊天名和时间）；导入则把之前导出的文件**还原成可继续聊的对话**——接在当前页末尾、绝不覆盖已有内容（页面非空会先确认），导入的对话神谕也记得、能接着聊。空白页面上没有气泡时，页中会出现「📤 导入对话」入口。只在**普通聊天**和**剧情参谋**里可用。认不出的文件段会明说跳过了几段，绝不悄悄丢内容。\r\n\r\n## 进阶选项\r\n\r\n- **用补全预设作为系统提示词来源。** 除了直接写提示词，还可让神谕**沿用某个 Chat Completion 预设的结构**：首次选中会弹出**挑选清单**，逐块决定去留并可拖动排序（故事 / 世界 / 人格类默认保留，思维链 / 字数 / 文风等输出块默认去掉），保存后**冻结成快照**（之后改原预设不影响这份）。点 [↺ 重新挑选] 会按你**上次保存的勾选和顺序**打开，可以接着改；想拿原预设的最新内容从头挑，在清单里点「重置默认」。发送时**忠实复刻**主聊天的提示词结构（各插槽就地填入、保留每块的角色、宏实时解析且 `setvar` 会自愈不污染主聊天）。**选用预设时人格与下方系统提示词文本框都会停用。** 开了「应用剧情正则」时神谕会像主聊天一样渲染自己的回复（状态栏美化等正常显示）。\r\n- **说话人格。** 普通 / 泉こなた / 贝阿特丽丝 / 胡蝶忍 给神谕套一层说话腔调（选「普通」= 不叠加）。**选预设时默认关**以免冲突。参谋 / 世界书模式下人格只改语气，不影响方案区块格式或写入条目的正文。诊断模式不生效。\r\n- **自定义人格（1.39.0）。** 下拉旁的 ✎ 打开编辑器：起个名字、写一段「这个人格怎么说话」（性格、态度、口头禅——职责规则如「分析必须准确、知无不言」由神谕自带，不用写），保存后出现在下拉的「── 自定义 ──」组里，与内置人格一样在普通 / 参谋 / 世界书模式生效（诊断模式同样不生效）。只有一个粗略点子？点「✨ AI 帮我完善」让当前连接的模型把几个词扩写成完整描述（附示例对话），不满意可「↩ 撤销」。最多 20 个。\r\n- **自定义各模式提示词。** 设置里有个模式下拉，可查看 / 改写**诊断**、**世界书**与**剧情参谋**（单步方案，1.17.7 起）模式的内置提示词（未改时随更新自动改进，改了就冻结，[↺ 重置为默认] 还原）。弧线编译等长线提示词不开放。\r\n- **读取其它扩展的后台世界。** 勾「附带『世界引擎』后台世界状态」（默认开）后，神谕会在普通聊天与参谋模式读入**世界引擎 / World Engine** 维护的幕后世界状态（正在酝酿的事件、势力动向……），于是你能问「外面正在发生什么」。目前仅适配世界引擎；未识别到相关扩展时无开销。\r\n- **读取柏宝书的历史剧情摘要（1.33.0，1.46.0 扩展触达）。** 如果你在用**柏宝书（ST-BaiBai-Book）**记忆扩展：它会把窗口外的旧楼层隐藏、只给主模型留摘要——而神谕默认不读隐藏楼层，等于「只看得见最近几十楼」。勾「附带『柏宝书』历史剧情摘要」（默认关）后，神谕在普通聊天与参谋模式会把柏宝书的**被隐藏旧楼摘要**（带「昨天 / 三天前」相对时间标注）插在对话记录之前——问三百楼前的旧事也答得上来；**校正 / 工坊**勾「带上剧情概要」时也一并附带；**世界书模式**勾「同时带上最近剧情对话」时随之附带（此时运行概要也会一并带上）；**已注册的插件模式 / 二创**（如大纲版）经接口读取故事记录时也自动附带。与所有连接方式、预设路径都兼容。诊断模式有意不接（概要与摘要都不进诊断——审计以 stat_data 为准）。注意保持「读取隐藏楼层」关闭（否则原文与摘要重复喂两遍）；未安装柏宝书时勾了也无开销。\r\n- **读取小白X 的剧情总结记忆（1.50.0）。** 如果你在用 **LittleWhiteBox（小白X）** 的「剧情总结」：它把早期剧情压成记忆、只在主聊天生成时喂给主模型——神谕平时读不到。勾「附带『小白X』的剧情总结」（默认关）后，神谕会在主聊天生成时悄悄记下那份总结，之后在普通 / 参谋 / 世界书 / 校正 / 工坊里当背景一起看，于是问早期剧情也答得上来。重开酒馆也记得住（存在本聊天里）；刚装上立刻问、还没生成过时，也会现取一份垫上。诊断模式有意不接；未安装 / 未开启小白X 时勾了也无开销。\r\n- **机制块 / 思维链自动隐藏。** 普通 / 参谋模式会自动从显示和历史里剥掉回复内嵌的 `<UpdateVariable>` 增量块与泄漏的 `<think>` 思维链（诊断模式保留——读它们是其本职）。\r\n\r\n## 界面\r\n\r\n- 空对话时窗口中央有**示例问题 chip**，点一下即填入输入框（每种模式各一组）。\r\n- 全键盘可用 + 读屏支持，尊重系统「减少动态效果」；移动端触摸目标更大。\r\n- **各模式的配置栏**（诊断 / 世界书 / 校正 / 工坊 / **参谋**）都可整条折叠（手机默认折叠、限高半屏）；破坏性操作弹 ST 主题化的确认框。（参谋栏 1.20 起也能折。）\r\n- 消息操作按钮（复制 / 重生 / 编辑 / 删除）默认排在**气泡底部**、鼠标悬停显影（1.20 起）；切换模式时会**自动收起设置面板**。\r\n- **切换模式的中断确认（1.36.0）**：有回复正在生成时点别的模式按钮 / ⋯ 菜单「普通聊天」/ 工坊打造目标下拉，会先弹确认框——切换会**中止并丢弃**这条未完成的回复，确定才切、取消留在原地。锻造与深度精简是后台保活调用、切模式不中断，所以不会弹这个框。\r\n- 「界面」设置里的开关（1.20 起）：把 ⋯ 菜单的工具按钮**移到标题栏**（省一次点击，默认关、⋯ 菜单仍在；1.37.1 起窗口装不下时按钮**自动换行**到第二行——之前在手机上会把右上角 ✕ 挤出窗外、按不到）。（旧「开发者·控制台打印提示词」开关已于 1.37.2 移除——它是早年二创调试的遗留，与 ⋯ 菜单里的「调试提示词」面板完全重复。）\r\n- **点击窗外自动收起（1.48 起，默认关）**：「界面」设置里勾上后，点酒馆页面的其它地方（正文、输入框等）就把神谕窗**收起**。点窗内、方案浮条、📡 实时输出、酒馆的弹窗 / 提示条、魔杖菜单、🌙 与 ✂️ 快捷按钮都**不算窗外**；**划词选字、滚屏也不会**误触发（选段校正的划选流程照旧可用）。收起只是隐藏——模式、侧聊、方案统统保留，从魔杖或 🌙 再点开一切如旧。1.48.1 修复了**窗口配色选「深色 / 浅色」时点哪都不收**的问题；另外若浏览器装了 **uBlock Origin** 等拦截扩展且勾了也没反应，请为酒馆地址关闭拦截（实测它会拦掉这类点击监听）。\r\n- 退出子模式会回到**进来之前**的那个模式，而不是一律掉回普通聊天。\r\n- **移动 / 调整大小**：拖标题栏移动、拖右下角握把缩放（鼠标和触屏都支持）；位置与尺寸都记住，并自动限制在屏幕内。\r\n- **🖥 全屏阅读（1.51.0）**：点标题栏的全屏图标（在 ✕ 左侧），窗口**铺满屏幕**；再点一次或按 **Esc** 退出，回到悬浮窗口（位置 / 大小不变）。适合手机上长对话阅读。纯显示切换，刷新页面回到悬浮窗口。\r\n\r\n## 扩展开发接口（Hook API · 面向二创 / 插件作者）\r\n\r\n想给故事神谕**加一个自己的模式**、又不想每次它更新就重抄一份代码？从 **1.21.0** 起，故事神谕在页面上挂出一个**版本化的稳定接口** `window.StoryOracleAPI`（外加 `story-oracle-ready` 事件）。你的插件**只装一个自己的文件**、监听这个接口即可——不必打包故事神谕，主体更新（只要主版本号不变）也不会打断你。\r\n\r\n- **首选 `registerMode(spec)`**：声明一个模式（图标 / 标题 / 输入框占位 / 设置栏 / `onSend`）——DOM、渲染、模型调用全由主体负责，你只写「这个模式该怎么想」。\r\n- 还有：`addMessageAction()`（每条回复挂按钮）、`updateReply()`（改写并持久化一条回复）、`api.context.*`（角色卡 / 世界书 / 对话记录只读构建器，与内置模式同源）、逃生阀 `api.run()` + `api.appendReply()`（onSend 覆盖不到时才用）。用 `api.isCompatible(1)` 做版本闸；回复的原始模型输出存在 `.so-content` 的 `data-so-raw` 上，便于读自定义标签。\r\n- **只读引导快照 `api.guidance.getActive()`**（1.78 起）：返回当前聊天**已采纳的参谋引导**——`null` 或一份副本 `{ schemaVersion: 1, chatId, revision, kind: 'plan'|'seq'|'arc', directive, intensity }`（`directive` 就是注入主聊天的那段文本）。只在引导注册成功后发布；用户没勾「数据库联动」、聊天身份不符、当前无引导时为 `null`。面向「规划类」扩展（如 SP·数据库 的剧情推进）在**组装自己的提示词之前**读取——请把 `directive` 当**字面文本**原样加入，不要再过占位符 / 模板通道。不发事件、不接受写入；`api.version` 仍为 1，用 `typeof api.guidance?.getActive === 'function'` 探测能力即可。\r\n- **完全开放逃生阀 `api.unsafe.eval(code)`**（1.22 起）：在故事神谕**模块作用域内**求值——可直读 / 改写内部任意顶层函数与状态（含日后新增的），插件侧可完全自助、无需逐项对接。⚠ **非正式接口**：不入版本契约、无任何兼容承诺，主体更新后失效 / 变样由插件侧自行适配；首次调用会在控制台打一条提示，排查异常时请先停用相关插件再复测。日常仍**首选上面的正式接口**。\r\n- **可直接照抄的范例插件**：`data/default-user/extensions/so-example-plugin/`（不打包故事神谕，仅监听接口）。完整接口文档见仓库 `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-05-story-oracle-hook-api-design.md`。\r\n": "# Story Oracle (Story Oracle) - SillyTavern Extension\r\n\r\nA draggable side panel: Connect your custom **OpenAI Compatible** endpoint to ask LLM questions about *ongoing* plots.\r\nThe Q&A takes place in its **independent window and independent history** - **does not touch your main chat at all** and can be cleared at any time.\r\n\r\n**It can do six things for you** (top icon switching, mutually exclusive):\r\n\r\n- 💬 **Normal Chat** - Ask about the plot: \"Why did she do this?\" \"How much does she like her now?\"\r\n- 🩺 **Diagnosis** - Fix MVU status variable (when the value/status bar does not match).\r\n- 📖 **World Info** - Chat about World Info, or let it ** help you directly modify** World Info.\r\n- 🧭 **Plot Consultant** - Conceive the plot direction together, and can **quietly guide** the main chat (including multi-shot long-term \"arcs\" and pre-written \"sequences\").\r\n- ✨ **Correction** - Correct the \"AI flavor\" of the latest reply with one click (manually specified, or automatically for each post).\r\n- 🎭 **Character Workshop** - Just a few chats will polish a character from scratch to a complete setting, and write it into your character or World Info NPC entry.\r\n\r\n> **v1.89.0 (🩺 Diagnosis understands \"cards with variable rules\")**: Some character cards have strict rules for variables (the most common ones are cards with mvu_zod: a certain value must be a number, you can only choose from a few options, a certain folder is not allowed to add new items...). In the past, the diagnosis was written correctly, but if the card was quietly rejected, all you would see was \"It took a long time to diagnose and nothing has changed.\" Starting from this version: ① **Rehearse according to the rules of this card before writing** - Above the \"Apply Repair to Status\" button on the patch card, it will be written directly \"This repair contains N, which this card will not accept\", and why for each place (such as \"Protagonist › Stamina: must be a number\"), and only write the parts that can be passed when applying; ② If the model is written incorrectly, the diagnosis will **automatically rewrite it with the reason** (it takes one more call; uncheck \"Let the model automatically rewrite once when rejected\" in \"Diagnosis Settings\" to turn it off); ③ Newly added ** \"🩺 Check the archive: If there is an illegal value in the archive, every subsequent variable update of this card will fail (even the story-telling model written by itself) - the check will indicate in plain English which grid it is, what it is now, what the card requires, and there will be a button to open that grid directly in the 🎛 variable editor. It will automatically check the first time you perform a diagnosis in a chat, or when a repair does not change anything. The reading rules rely on the internal data of SillyTavern; if one day SillyTavern cannot read it after updating, the diagnosis will work quietly in the previous way without reporting an error. Another fix, bug: Opening a chat with only an opener (newly created or reopened) will no longer trigger automatic correction/auto-diagnosis/modifiers - before, every time it was opened, a round would be run on the opener (the modifier's \"per round +X\" would be added once each time it was opened).\r\n\r\n> **v1.88.0 (🎛 You can delete things in the variable editor + \"Reselect\" by selecting the preset block no longer looks like it has not been saved) **: ① In the **🎛 variable editor**, there is an extra **🗑** on the right side of each folder, field, and list in the tab - such as items that are no longer in the backpack/storage, click 🗑 to mark delete (the entire line of underlines fades, the button becomes **↩**, click ↩ Cancel), and then press \"**Apply**\" to actually delete it; if you delete it by mistake, click \"**Undo**\" on the \"🎛 Manual Edit\" record in the diagnostic side chat to replace the entire copy. The tab itself (the top-level category) cannot be deleted, and the individual items in the list still use ➖. A word of warning: For cards with a strict variable structure (schema), after deleting the \"must have\" fields specified by the card, the next reply may be added back by the card itself - that is the behavior of the card. ② **Select preset blocks**: When you click [Reselect] to open, what is now displayed is the **checks and order you last saved** (previously, the default checkboxes were always displayed, and it looked like they were not saved - in fact, the save was always valid, but it was not displayed; what's worse is that clicking save again will cover the default checkboxes). If you want to start over from the current default content, click \"Reset Default\".\r\n\r\n> **v1.87.0 Newly added (🧭Next shot suggestions - when guiding the sequence, help you think of what to say next)**: The community plug-in \"Next shot suggestions\" has been incorporated into the oracle body (original author **Cotton Doll**, thank you for the authorization). Check **Next Shot Suggestions** in the plot consultant's \"**Staff Settings**\", and then as long as the **sequence guidance** is in progress, a small card will appear below the latest reply in the main chat: click \"**Generate Suggestions**\", the oracle will read the guidance of the current shot, the character card and your character, the relevant World Info entries and the just-written text, and give 4~7 words that you can send next (3 (\"I\"), 1~3 characters present, and 0~1 time advance; storyboards/transition shots do not give \"I\"), **click on one to fill in the input box** - if there is already a word in the input box, add a new line after it, **will not be overwritten, nor will it be sent for you**. By default, it is only generated when you click the button; if you want to automatically generate it for each reply, you can turn it on in \"More Settings\" (each reply costs one more API call). Does not appear under single-step scenarios/arcs. Friends who have installed the independent version of the plug-in before, please disable it, otherwise there will be two cards under each reply.\r\n\r\n> **v1.86.0 Newly added (🌐 Template Square - download custom templates shared by others, and you can also share your own)**: The template row of the \"Custom\" panel in calibration mode has two more buttons: **🌐 Square** Open a public template library, press the label / Find keywords, click \"Preview\" to see the full text, click \"Download\" to save it into your template drop-down and select it; when the author updates, it will display \"There is a new version\", you can overwrite the local copy or save another copy. **📤 Share** Fill in the name, description, and tags of your current template and submit it to the author for review. Only if it passes the review will it appear in the square (the shared template is public and anyone can download and use it). The downloaded template is just a piece of ordinary text, just like what you wrote by hand. It will only be used when you select it. **(The square is currently closed, and one-click submission has been cancelled; 📤 Sharing is changed to copy the sharing text and send it to Discord, see the \"🌐 Template Square\" section below.) **\r\n\r\n> **v1.85.3 Improvement (⚡ Faster opening/switching of long conversation records)**: Some friends reported that \"opening the Oracle is very laggy\". After checking, I found that the longer the conversation record in the oracle window is, the more stuck it will be when loading chat, switching chats, and switching modes. In the past, every time I drew an old message, the browser had to re-layout the entire page. Now the entire batch of drawings is only scheduled once: the record of 200 round, redrawing has dropped from about 8.5 seconds to about 0.4 seconds (actual measurement on the computer, the difference on the mobile phone is even greater). In addition, old messages will no longer replay the fade-in animation every time the window is opened, only newly arrived messages will have it. The functionality and appearance remain unchanged, and no settings are required. (If the record is particularly long, the windowing itself will still be slower; further optimization is still being evaluated.)\r\n\r\n> **v1.85.2 Repair (🧭 The characters/places named in the plot consultant guide are not recognized by the World Info)**: A friend reported that when the plot consultant quietly guided the main chat, the keywords NPC and location mentioned in the guide did not light up the \"green light\" entry triggered by the keyword in the World Info - the model could not see that setting and could only make up one by itself. The reason is that this guide did not tell SillyTavern to \"scan me into the World Info keyword detection\" when registering before. Now the **character/location keywords mentioned in the plot consultant will trigger the green light entry in the World Info** (the same is true for single-shot plans, arc shots, and sequence shots, as well as the blind box mode of arcs); the prompt sentence for the drop shot sensor is still not included in the keyword scan. Its wording is too general, and scanning it in will easily trigger other entries by mistake.\r\n\r\n> **v1.85.1 Repair (⏎ The oracle input box on the mobile phone cannot change the line)**: Some friends reported that the message was sent as soon as they pressed Enter in the oracle input box on the mobile phone, and there was no way to segment it (the mobile phone keyboard does not have Shift+Enter). Now the oracle's input box **follows SillyTavern's own \"User Settings → Press Enter to send\"**, and is the same as SillyTavern owner's input box: by default \"Auto (PC)\", the computer will send Enter, and the mobile phone Enter will change the line (click the send button to send); if it is changed to \"Enabled\", Enter will be sent directly on the phone, and \"Disabled\" will only use the button to send everywhere. Using the Chinese input method and pressing Enter to select words/up the screen will not cause mis-sent.\r\n\r\n> **v1.84.1 Repair (✨ A whole copy of the HTML source code is spread out in the correction result card)**: Some friends reported that when using cards such as \"Corridor of Creation\" to correct the entire article, the **correction draft card** in the Oracle window is a large piece of `<!DOCTYPE html>…` with the source code and text buried in it (✂️ The selection correction has always been normal). The reason is that the \"beautification\" of this type of card is not an inline widget like the status bar, but an entire web page - which is rendered into an embedded page by SillyTavern assistant in the main chat. The oracle window does not have that set of renderers, so the source code can only be spread out as it is. Now when Oracle recognizes this kind of **entire webpage** beautification, the correction card will **change to plain text layout to display the main text**; the beautification itself is not missing at all - click **[Apply]** and then return to the main chat to still beautify. Inline beautification such as the status bar, weather header, and thought chain collapse are not affected and are still rendered in the card.\r\n\r\n> **v1.82.0 fix (🎭 Character Workshop · World Info entries only feed enabled + entry volume readings by default)**: Some friends reported that the workshop \"suddenly started reading the entire World Info\" - the prompt words skyrocketed, and the request was returned with 400 by the service provider. It turns out that the workshop's **entry selector will feed out every entry in that book if it has not been touched**, including the entries that you have disabled in the World Info (old version settings, abolished cases, backup rules). Now **unchecked books only feed its currently enabled entries**, and disabled entries are also displayed as **unchecked** in the list - what you see is what you get; if you really want to feed a disabled item (such as a disabled \"Character Generation Rule\"), manually check it and it will be sent. \"Select All\" will still be sent with the ban. By the way, the **volume reading** that already existed in the World Info mode has been moved over: the summary line of the entry list will now read \"about X token\", and if it exceeds 10, a red reminder will appear (**only prompt, never intercept and send**).\r\n\r\n> **v1.79.0 Newly added (✂️ Selection correction · Mobile \"click and select\" mode)**: When selecting on mobile phones, the cursor always runs around with multiple selections/less selections, and it also fights with other word delineation pop-ups - now the selection card is changed to \"click and select\" by default on **touch screen devices**: The full text is spread out according to sentences, **tap a sentence to select this sentence** (amber), and click elsewhere to change a sentence; if you want to select multiple sentences, press **\"Expand Selection\"** Click the other end to select the entire paragraph in the middle; to be precise to the word, press **\"Fine Adjustment\"**, and a **large character grid** of this sentence will be docked below (select one word each for \"Beginning\" and \"End\", as well as \"‹ One word / one word ›\" nudge, \"Complete / Cancel fine-tuning\"; during the fine-tuning period, the nail segment below and the \"How do you want to change\" input box will be temporarily closed. Press \"Finish\" or \"Cancel\" to return, and the written words will not be lost). After selection, it is still the same as before **📌 Pin this paragraph**, write requirements, and start correction - in click mode, the pinned paragraphs and the \"How do you want to change\" input box are **fixed in the operation bar** below the text, so there is no need to turn to the end of the text to find it; the mechanism has not changed a word (only the paragraphs you selected are sent according to the character offset, and the rest remain unchanged; the status bar and other structural blocks are also ordinary text in the click selection, you can select whatever you want, just like drag selection). The entire card will not generate system selections in the click mode, so the magnifying glass, \"copy\" bubble, and word expansion will not pop up; finger sliding is scrolling, and pressing and stopping during inertial scrolling does not count as clicks. There is a **\"Click | Drag to Select\"** switch in the upper right corner of the card. You can switch back to the old selection method at any time (switching will not lose the pinned segments and written requirements); this selection is only recorded in the **current browser** (it will not be synchronized with the account to other devices). Desktop browsers still default to \"drag and select\" and the behavior is exactly the same as before. There are two other small changes that are effective in both modes: ① If you have pinned a segment and select a segment that is not pinned yet, click \"Start Correction\", and you will be reminded to **pinning or clearing** first** (previously this segment would be quietly discarded) - for this reason, there is also an additional \"Clear\" next to the 📌 in the drag-and-select mode; ② If you encounter an inaccurate point, you can execute it in the browser console `localStorage['so.fixsel.debug']='1'` and then reopen the card. There will be a \"Debug Log\" box at the bottom of the card. Press and hold to select all and copy them to the author.\r\n\r\n> **v1.77.5 Improvement (🧭 Return of the exclusive settings for consultants)**: \"Plot Guidance Injection Depth\" and \"Falling Sensing\" are only related to plot consultants. In the past, they were mixed in the \"Context and World Info\" group of the main settings panel and were difficult to find. Now they have been moved into the \"**Advisor Settings**\" folding group of the Advisor mode (you can see it by switching to the 🧭 Advisor mode, in the same place as \"Apply my completion defaults\"); the originally filled values ​​will be used as they are without reset. There is an additional reminder in the injection depth line: **When the model does not listen to the guidance, lower the depth, as low as 0** - the smaller the number, the closer the guidance instruction is to the latest message, and the easier it is for the model to follow it.\r\n\r\n> **v1.77.4 fix (🔔 Drop shot sensor · Thought chain beautification disappears when used with presets such as \"Mingyue Qiuqing Myriad Stars\")**: Some friends reported that when sequence guidance was turned on, the folded thought block in the AI reply was gone, and the entire thought chain was spread out in the text together with `</thinking>`; single-shot guidance was fine. It was found that two things collided: the default set the last \"Qiu Qingzi ate the original thinking chain\" as a **player message** and placed it at the end of the entire prompt word (its function is to let the model continue writing `<thinking>`, and SillyTavern will fold this paragraph), and the oracle 1.75 The fitting injection will put the drop-shot agreement at the end of the last player message - right after the prompt. The prompt is no longer the \"last sentence\". The model changes to native thinking, and the folding of SillyTavern will not recognize this text. Now when the oracle sees the last player message ending with a `<|…|>` token, an opening tag (such as `<thinking>`), or a bare line \"Speaker:\", it will put the protocol at the beginning of that message, so that the default prompt is still the last sentence; in all other cases, the content sent out is the same byte-for-byte as before. By the way, this \"thinking block is not folded\" is a limitation of SillyTavern itself on the line where the ** model returns the original thinking** at the same time (it only leaves one type when the two types of thinking arrive at the same time). This version of Oracle only guarantees that it will no longer be triggered by itself.\r\n>\r\n> **v1.77.3 Repair (🩺 Diagnosis · The reason when \"no value has changed\" is more accurate)**: A friend reported that each round of automatic diagnosis left the same sentence - \"The patch was run, but no value changed\", followed by \"① SillyTavern Assistant version is older ② This card has schema verification (mvu_zod) turned on, and writes with inconsistent types will be **rejected in batches**\". I went back and checked the source code of the variable engine. There are two things wrong with this passage: **mvu_zod is checking item by item and discarding it item by item** (the one that does not comply is discarded, and the rest are written in as usual), and the general \"environmental issues\" throws out the failure that could have been explained clearly. This version does two things: ① **Judge according to the card's own structure definition** - the variable engine by default **does not allow** to add items to objects/lists that are not marked as \"expandable\", nor can it add or subtract text fields; these two categories will now be named one by one (\"This layer is an object/list that the card is not marked as extensible\" \"The current value of this item is neither a number nor a date\") and each will be given a next step that can be done, without mixing in that general prompt. ② **When you really can’t tell the reason, point to a way to find the answer** - the variable engine will pop up a prompt to indicate which command it is and why it was rejected, but the switch **is off by default**: SillyTavern → \"MVU Variable Framework\" panel → Notification → Check \"Notify when errors in variable initialization/update\", you can see it after running again (the card that hangs mvu_zod displays `[MVU zod] …`; also available in F12 console). Another reminder: If there is an illegal value in the archive of the card linked to mvu_zod, every subsequent update will be rejected - including the story-telling model written by itself - in that case, you must first change the value to the regulation in the 🎛 variable editor.\r\n>\r\n> **v1.77.2 fix (🩺 Automatic diagnosis · There is no status bar when MVU selects \"Additional model analysis\" but unchecks \"Enable automatic request\") **: Some friends reported that \"automatic diagnosis is turned on, but the original additional analysis of MVU does not turn on automatic request, and the status bar cannot be displayed.\" It was found that MVU did nothing in reply to the newly received AI under this configuration - neither copied the variables from the previous floor nor added the placeholder line in the status bar; the oracle read the first floor and read an **empty status**, and none of the deduced updates could be implemented, so there was no placeholder. Now the automatic diagnosis will first do this step for MVU: there is no variable in this floor but there is one in the earlier floor, so **copy the status of the latest floor**, run the update (if any) brought by this reply, fill in the placeholder, and then diagnose as usual - the status bar appears like the official update. **Leaves a three-and-a-half-second grace period for MVU** (it will sometimes slow down a beat before processing). It will handle it by itself without intervening; users who \"output with AI\" or turn on automatic requests are not affected at all.\r\n>\r\n> **v1.77.1 repair (🧩 The Oracle suffered amnesia when used with the \"Youzuki Memory\" (yuzuki-Memory) plug-in)**: A friend reported that when installing Yuzuki Memory, the diagnostic mode \"does not modify variables\" - asked it \"Status Bar Error\", but it asked you whether you are using Apple or Android like customer service. The reason is on Yuzuki's side: it will block every model request sent by the browser for sorting. As long as its own memory title appears in any message (such as \"【 Current World State Reference - Character File 】\" \"【 Preliminary Summary 】\"), the entire message will be deleted - while the Oracle puts the rules, variable status and plot records into one message, in the plot. AI replied to a title that I copied once, and the entire prompt word of the oracle was gone, and only your sentence was left in the model. Now when the oracle detects Yu Yue's presence, it will secretly insert an **invisible character** into the titles in the sent copy to separate them, and Yu Yue will not recognize them; the text seen by the model is the same, and your chat history, World Info, and variables will not change a word. Users who have not installed Youyue are not affected at all (the content sent out is the same byte by byte as before). Ordinary chat, World Info, staff, correction, and workshop all benefit the same - they would also quietly lose their memory under the same conditions before. Oracle will also use Youyue**'s own** cleaning function to double-check the sent copy before sending it every time: it will recognize it even if the title is changed in the future, and will automatically change to a wider splitting method to save the message, and remind it once in the browser console.\r\n\r\n> **v1.77.0 Newly added (📋 The third level of correction mode \"Custom\" - use your own template to process each new reply) **: The correction mode drop-down has an additional level \"**Custom**\" - write a template of your own (such as \"Translate the text into Japanese\"), and process each new reply according to it, and the result will still be as **New swipe** After landing, leave the original text on the left and swipe it back at any time; in a chat, you can either run corrections or run templates, choose one of the two, and there will be no superposition. In the template, just write what you want it to do, and the reserved tags for the output format and structure blocks are automatically attached by Oracle. \"**Inherit corrected text recognition**\" is turned on by default (only the plot text is processed, the status bar and variable blocks are retained as they are), and when turned off, the **entire** reply is given to the template and the output is replaced as is; this file also has its own reserved area/discard area and minimum number of words. You can also turn off automatic and click \"**Use template to process latest reply**\" to run it at any time.\r\n\r\n> **v1.77.0 Newly added (✂️ Each of the two buttons for segment correction has a switch)**: 【 correction settings → In manual 】, there are now ** upper and lower lines of check** - the upper line (from 1.44 onwards, the default is ** off**) determines whether to put an extra \"✂️\" above the ** chat input box** \"Selection correction\" shortcut button; the line below (default **on**, the behavior is the same as before) determines whether to put the ✂️ in the upper right corner of the latest AI reply - if you think the small scissors on the reply are annoying, cancel it. The one above the input box will not be affected. After canceling, the button will disappear **immediately** without refreshing the page.\r\n\r\n> **v1.76.0 New (🎭 Character Workshop · User Character (Persona) is back)**: The \"Creation Goal\" drop-down list of the Workshop has three new items: **NPC World Info Entry** (as usual), **User Character·Talk** (AI will also act and speak for your character), **User Role·No Talk** (AI Only respond to you, never act for you) - The last two items write the role you played in the interview as an instruction manual for AI to \"read\". You can **perfect the description of the current Persona**, or you can **save it as a new Persona**. Writing can still be revoked with one click; each of the two user roles has its own section check and its own interview room. This version also conveniently solves an old problem: in the past, the \"goal motivation\" would occasionally install an ambition that was not in the material, and then add a sentence that did not match the basis; now each line is copied first from the original sentence in the material, and then writes what it can support. Lines that cannot be copied from the original sentence are simply not written - **the whole forging still only has one model call**, and does not cost a penny more. ⚠ During the period of delisting, the building target was uniformly changed to NPC, and it will not be automatically switched back. If you want to write a user role, please select it again in the drop-down list.\r\n\r\n> **v1.74.2 Fix (🧭 Drop Sensing · Prompt no longer flashes by)**: Previously, the prompt \"This shot may have landed\" only had one reply - you didn't have time to click 【 to complete 】 to continue chatting, and the prompt for the next reply disappeared as soon as it arrived. Now the prompt will stay on until you click 【 to finish 】 processing it, or delete the reply swipe that triggered it in the first place.\r\n\r\n> **v1.74.1 Improvement (🧭 Drop Sensing · More eye-catching reminder)**: When detecting \"this beat may have landed\", the 【 completed 】 button will now **slowly flash** (the circle of breathing light in v1.73.0 is too subtle and easy to miss); if you fold the guide bar into the **compass small round button** in the corner of the screen, the compass will also flash slowly synchronously - expand it to see familiar prompts and evidence sentences. It's up to you to nod if you want to change the photo, and it will never be automatically advanced; friends who have \"Reduce Motion Effects\" turned on by the system will not be disturbed (no flashing). Incidentally fixed: When switching from a sequence to a single-step plan/arc, the drop shot prompt of the previous sequence may remain on the guide bar.\r\n>\r\n> **v1.74.0 Newly added (🩺 Automatic diagnosis · Automatic retry on failure) **: Automatic diagnosis will occasionally run in vain - the model replies nothing (rejection/truncation), replies a bunch but the format is so bad that it cannot be used, or the request itself is not sent (network/transit convulsion). In the past, you could only let this kind of round pass and wait for the next reply before you have another chance. Now there is a new \"**🔁 Auto-retry on failure**\" checkbox in the diagnostic settings (default is off): after turning it on, if this round does not run, it will **automatically retry**, and the number of times is filled in by yourself (default 2 times). You can also check **which failure situations** need to be retried - **blank reply** (no content returned by the model), **format error** (failed to understand/reject updates from the model), **call failure** (network error/timeout, etc.), three independent combinations. Each retry will **reread the current status** and send another request (rather than resending the old request as it is). The ongoing prompt will indicate how many times it has been retried, and it can still be interrupted by clicking on it. Each of the failed rounds will also leave an entry in the diagnostic record, with \"will automatically retry\" at the end. **Never retry** situations: diagnosis is successful, verification passes without modification, and various safe skips (you cut off the chat/the status has just been changed by someone else/you manually clicked interrupt)-these retries are meaningless or unsafe. ⚠ Each retry is a real model call, and you will spend money as usual; friends who are not stable in using transfer are recommended to only check \"Blank Reply\" and \"Call Failed\".\r\n>\r\n> **v1.73.0 Newly added (🧭 Sequence Guidance · Drop Sensing - this beat is finished, the oracle can tell it by himself) **: When using sequence guidance, you had to remember and click 【 to complete 】 for each beat before. Now during the sequence, the oracle will make the storyteller model **invisibly** report a line \"Where is this beat\" at the end of each reply (you can't see this line at all in the chat, it is only read by the oracle); when the model reports \"This beat has happened in the text\", and the original sentence it quotes can actually be read in the reply When you find ** in the complex, a prompt will appear on the plan bar \"**This beat may have landed - completed?**\" (hover to see the evidence sentence), 【 completed 】 button to start breathing - **It is still up to you to nod whether to change the beat**: Ignore it and it will remain the same, **will never advance automatically**. The entire detection is **zero model calls** (hitting a ride on the reply that was supposed to happen), and it doesn't cost a penny to replace the old one. A new \"**Down Shot Sensing (automatically prompts that the current shot may have been completed)**\" checkbox is added in the settings (on by default; when turned off, the behavior is exactly the same as the v1.72.0). ⚠ Two points to note: ① The model occasionally forgets to report (especially the first shot at the beginning of the sequence, which has no precedent in the context) - that is, there is no prompt, so you still manually click 【 to complete 】; ② If the regular rules that come with some cards eat this line of invisible reporting, the sensor will fail but it will not affect any other functions**. If you want to clear the display rules registered by it after uninstalling the extension, go to \"Extension → Regularity\" and delete the \"Story Oracle · Drop Shot Sensor Hidden Line\".\r\n\r\n> **v1.72.0 Newly added (🧭 Sequence guidance - Arrange the entire long-term plot that has been discussed into a \"shot list\", adopt it once and advance it shot by shot)**: In the past, after talking to the consultant about an entire long-term plot (such as \"Ten things you want to experience in the first year of the magic school\"), you would either break it down into ten single-step plans and adopt them one by one, or open an arc and spend a model call for each shot. Now the consultant will directly arrange this type of discussion into an orderly shot list: each shot has its own goal, starting signs and fitting points, **all spread out for you to see**, click 【 to start the sequence and guide 】 to adopt it at once. After that **only the current shot is leading the main chat at the same time**, if you think this shot is finished, click 【 to complete 】 to change to the next shot - **change the shot without adjusting the model and without spending a penny** (the content has already been written). The plan bar will display \"X / Y shot\" and a **shot list**: ✓ Completed / ▶ In progress / ○ To be broadcast / ⤫ Skipped, click on any row to see its complete content; **The shot to be broadcast can directly ✏️ change the content, or you can 【 skip 】**. If you want to make major changes (rearrange, add, delete, change direction), click 【💬 and ask the staff to change 】 - **The current photo is always guided, nothing will be demolished**, the window will automatically open, return to the staff room to continue chatting; after chatting, the staff will re-list the **remaining photos**, and using it will only replace the part from the current photo, **the history that has been played will not be moved**. If you don’t want the whole one, just give up 【 and 】 (I’ll ask first). ⚠ A chat can only have one guidance component at a time: using a sequence will replace the running single-step plan/arc, and vice versa (you will be asked before throwing things away).\r\n\r\n> **v1.71.1 Fix (🩺 Automatic diagnosis · Actual reports from two users)**: ① **After the diagnosis is written, the regular/beautification on the message will no longer be erased**. In the past, as soon as the automatic diagnosis was written (or the status bar was refreshed), the regular and in-card beautification interfaces would return to plain text. You had to refresh the browser or click \"Reprocess Variables\" in MVU to get back - the root cause is that we only broadcast one type of refresh event after re-rendering, and the beautification ecosystem generally listens to the other type (the one sent by SillyTavern Assistant himself every round); now both are sent. ② **The record of \"Can't understand the model's reply\" can now be viewed in its entirety**. The reply summary in the record only displays the first line 3; when it is truncated (at the end...), there will be an additional \"**View full reply**\" button on the record. Click to expand the model in place to reply to the original text, and then click to collapse. The button is valid within **this session**. After reloading, only the summary will be recorded (the same rule as the \"Undo\" button - the complete original text will not be written into the archive to avoid repeated failures and the chat file will expand). In addition: When the abstract is not truncated, the label now reads \"Full text of the model reply (the model only returned these)\" - in the past, it always read \"the beginning of the model reply\". Some users mistakenly thought that the reply was truncated by the record; in fact, most of the cases were that the model/transfer really only returned that little bit (common in the reply token that the thought chain has eaten up).\r\n\r\n> **v1.71.0 Newly added (🧭 The injection command of the arc can also be edited manually ✏️)**: Some friends reported that when the arc was guided to the next beat, they were not satisfied with the details of this beat, but **can't find anything to change** - \"Change the idea\" and the re-roll was still a bit worse. Now there is also **✏️** on the plan bar for arcs (both transparent and blind boxes are acceptable): Click to open the behind-the-scenes instructions that are actually injected into the main chat for the current shot. Write the details you want to add and the writing methods you want to ban directly. 【 saves 】 and it will take effect immediately and will not be lost after refreshing; 【 restores the default 】 can retrieve the automatically generated version at any time. When you get to the next shot, a new command will be compiled - if you don't like it, just click ✏️ and change it. The rules are exactly the same as for single-step program editing (intensity files can still be switched as long as the \"Rhythm:\" line remains as is). **Attention for blind box players**: Click ✏️ to directly see the behind-the-scenes instructions (including spoilers). If you want to preserve the blind box experience, don’t click it. Editing only changes the injected text, and the tasks shown to you and the \"✓ Goal Achieved\" judgment will not be affected.\r\n\r\n> **v1.69.0 fix (🩺 Automatic diagnosis · Recalculation will be done when the update does not take effect) **: The model that tells the story occasionally writes the variable update block **bad** - there is one missing `</JSONPatch>` closing tag, an extra space in the tag, an incorrectly formatted instruction mixed into several instructions, the whole block is a \"rename\" instruction that is not supported by the engine, or the path is written with one more layer. In these cases, none of the variable engine is executed: your values ​​​​and status bar just stay in place, looking like \"stuck\". In the past, automatic diagnosis would only ask \"whether there is an updated block in this reply\" - if there is, it will assume that it has taken effect and only perform verification; it will even clearly tell the diagnostic model that \"these changes have already been taken into account, don't recalculate again.\" So the diagnostic model honestly answered \"nothing to change\" every round, and the freeze caused by the storyteller model could never be repaired (a user's save in 2026 and 8 froze an entire plot in this way). Now the automatic diagnosis asks another question: \"Has the variable engine been executed this round?\" Three results and three methods - if it is actually executed, it will still only be verified (**never recalculate, the old problem of counting the same transaction twice has not been relaxed at all**); there is no update block in the text at all, and it is still added based on the plot deduction; **The block is there, but none of it is executed**, just re-deduce** all the updates in this round based on the plot**, and clearly tell the diagnostic model \"that block is not effective\". This one will never insert another update block into the message body (there is already a broken one on that floor, and adding another one will swallow up the status bar of most cards entirely), only write variables into it and refresh the status bar. **Fixed by the way**: If the card throws out the `<JSONPatch>` block without any outer packaging** (note that there is no underline), Oracle could not recognize it before, so he deduced the changes in this round again** - the money spent is deducted twice, and the favorability is increased twice (it is the same type of problem that v1.40.2 has been repaired, but the form is more subtle); now it can be recognized.\r\n\r\n> **v1.68.0 New/Fixed (🩺 Diagnosis · Name change and move can really be implemented + You can save it by writing one less tag) **: This version is based on the error list run out of **768 real tests** (6 real cards × 4 models × 8 type modification instructions). Four things are fixed one by one: ① ** \"Rename / \"Moving\" is no longer lost** - When the model encounters a request such as \"rename a field\", it is favorite to write an `move` instruction (this is indeed the most appropriate in the JSON specification). But **SillyTavern's variable update engine is not implemented at all `move`**: the command is recognized and then **silently discarded**. What you see is \"the run was completed but nothing changed\", and the Oracle used to blame \"The version of SillyTavern is too old\". Now Oracle will automatically split it into two steps before landing (first build it under the new name, then delete the old one, and move it as it is, including fields with descriptions like `[数值,\"说明\"]`) - **Only do it when you can confirm that \"the old one is indeed there, and the one above the new location is also there\". If you can't confirm it, let it go as it is, and **clearly say that this verb engine does not support** and let you re-diagnose it again. This is the number one cause of failure in this test (768 times out of 37 times). ② **The model can be saved by writing one less `</JSONPatch>`** - some models (especially the Gemini series) have all the instructions written correctly, but miss the last closing tag, so the entire block is corrected **no one can read**, and the oracle can only report \"the reply of not understanding the model\". Now, as long as the ** command itself is complete**, Oracle will fill in the missing tag, and the correction will be implemented as usual (if it is not filled in completely, or if it is filled in and it is not compliant, no word will be touched). ③ **The square brackets in the instruction list are broken, no longer lie about \"no changes needed\"** - the model occasionally forgets to wrap `[ ]` in the instruction list, or opens `[` and forgets to finish. In the past, the oracle could not analyze this situation, but would write in the record \"**The latest reply has been checked, no changes are needed this round**\" - those **instructions that were originally correct were quietly thrown away. Now this kind of damage will be tried to be repaired first (if it can be repaired, it will be implemented as usual). If it cannot be repaired, it will tell you truthfully \"JSON is ​​missing something like brackets and cannot be parsed - no value is written\" and ask you to re-diagnose, and will never pretend to \"no changes required\". ④ **Two update blocks appear in one reply → Reject directly and ask you to reroll** - In this case, the same change may be **performed twice**, and the status bar of most cards will be **swallowed entirely** (this is a known display mine). The oracle will not merge it for you, nor will it pick a piece to execute. Instead, it will explain the reasons clearly without writing a word, and ask you to click \"Diagnosis\" again.\r\n\r\n> **v1.67.0 New/Fixed (🩺 Diagnosis · If the patch is wrong, correct it on the spot, if it doesn’t take effect, explain why)**: Some users saw a contradictory sentence after clicking \"Apply\" - \"**The patch was run, but no value changed - not written**\", but the four items below said \"**Cannot judge from the status change (it may or may not have taken effect)**\". Since it is certain that not a word has been written, you should not say \"may have taken effect\". This version does two things: ① **Physical examination before landing and automatic correction** - Oracle will go through the patch according to MVU's own rules before handing it over to MVU **, and fix the frequently used writing methods of the model on the spot: the verb is written as `set` / `update` / `修改` (MVU only recognizes `replace` / `delta` / `insert` / `remove` / `move`), write an extra slash at the end of the path, the increment of `delta` is written as `\"+5\"` this kind of string, `[数值,\"说明\"]` fields are written back in pairs (MVU Only recognize the first cell), there is an extra space in the `<JSONPatch >` label (MVU cannot see this area at all), and v1.66.1 is already repairing \"the path is written with an extra layer of `stat_data`\". In addition, as long as an entry with an illegal format is mixed into the patch, MVU will discard the entire instruction together - now that entry will be removed separately, and the rest will be implemented as usual, and the status line will tell you how many have been removed. Each category will only be used when there is evidence (only after it is modified to match your current variables), otherwise not a word will be touched. ② **Please explain why if it does not take effect** - \"Not a single value has changed\", each command will give a **confirmed reason** (there is no / this value is originally in this path state / the verb MVU does not recognize / the value type does not match...) ** plus a sentence about what to do next**, and \"may have taken effect\" will no longer appear. If the patch itself is **completely compliant but still has zero changes**, it will directly point out two real possibilities: **SillyTavern Assistant (MagVarUpdate) version is old or not working properly**, or **this card has schema verification (mvu_zod) enabled, and writes with inconsistent types will be silently rejected** - and tell you how to check yourself (first see if the variables of this card change by themselves during normal chat).\r\n>\r\n> **v1.66.1 repair (🩺 Diagnosis · The patch can be implemented even if the \"root\" is written incorrectly)**: After a user clicks \"Apply\", he sees \"**Applied (0 of the 29 instructions are effective)**\", and each item below says \"The path does not exist\" - the reason is that the model writes an extra layer of `stat_data` (written as `/stat_data/World/Time`, and MVU recognized `/World/Time`), so none of them were hit. Now Oracle will check it before handing the patch to MVU: confirm that this path only has this extra layer written (remove it to match your current variables) and automatically correct it. By the way, another **false alarm** has been fixed: the change to an item in the **list** (such as the status of item 2 of \"Today's To Do\") was originally effective, but it was reported as \"unable to judge from the status change\", and now it is actually displayed as having taken effect.\r\n>\r\n> **v1.52.0 added (📖 World Info EJS template rendering, opt-in)**: If your World Info entry has \"Prompt Word Template\" (ST-Prompt-Template) expanded `<% %>` For templates (such as dynamic entries for switching characters according to favorability), Oracle used to read **template original text** - those templates were only executed when the main chat was generated, so Oracle \"could see it but not understand it\". Now check \"**Support reading EJS World Info entries**\" under \"Settings → World Info/Knowledge Base\". Oracle will run the template first when reading the World Info in **General Q&A/Plot Advisor/Manual Correction** and see the finished text that is exactly the same as the main chat** (variable values ​​and conditional branches are all true), and by the way, token will be saved. The \"Prompt Word Template\" extension needs to be installed; if it is not installed, it will be automatically read as it is, with zero side effects. ⚠ One thing to note: Entries containing \"**write** variables\" (setvar, etc.) will be **extra executed** and may affect the variables in the card - just turn off this item when encountering an exception (the default is off). Diagnosis / World Info Editing / Character Workshop / Arc / Plug-in Interface **Intentionally not execute** the template (each has its own reasons for processing according to the original text, for example, what is changed in the editing mode is the original text of the template itself).\r\n>\r\n> **v1.51.0 Newly added (🖥 Full screen reading)**: There is an additional **Full screen** icon (⛶) on the left side of the title bar ✕ - click it to spread the oracle window to the entire screen, and long conversations will no longer be squeezed into the small floating window; click again (the icon becomes shrunken) or press **Esc** to exit and return to the original floating window (**position/size remains intact**). It can be used on mobile phones and desktops; pure display switching, chat content remains unchanged, and the page is refreshed to return to the floating window.\r\n>\r\n> **v1.49.0 Newly added (📖 Added \"book title search\" to the World Info selection box)**: There is a search box above the **book selection list** of World Info 📖 and Character Workshop 🎭 - when there are many books (dozens or hundreds), you can directly enter the keywords in the book title to filter them out, without having to search in a long list (it is a pair with the filter box that already exists in the entry list). It **only narrows the display range** and does not change the books you have selected; clearing the search box will restore the entire column. If there is no match, it will prompt \"No matching World Info\".\r\n>\r\n> **v1.47.0 New (✨ The command text of the correction target is open to customization)**: A new item \"Calibration Target\" is added in the \"System Prompt Word\" drop-down list - after selecting it, a second drop-down appears below, including the five targets of automatic correction (Bagu/Dialogue/Settings/Magic/Details). You can view and rewrite their command texts one by one (leave blank = use the built-in version, which will be automatically improved with updates; \"↺Reset to Default\" will restore with one click). The rules are simple: **Send only after checking the target; send the entire copy as it is after customization** - The built-in version's mechanism of \"add the second paragraph only when there is a character card/previous text/World Info basis\" no longer applies to customization, you can send whatever you write (the square bracket title is automatically added by the program). Two points to note: ① Before the automatic correction is called, there is a money-saving pre-screening based on the meaning of the built-in target. After rewriting a certain target into something that has nothing to do with the original meaning, if there is no sign of recognition by the built-in detector in the reply, it will still be judged as \"no correction\" and skipped, and your custom text will have no chance to appear; ② Copying the built-in text as it is into the edit box and saving it does not mean \"no changes\" - saving it will make it customized, and the two-stage basis mechanism will become invalid. If you want to return to the smart file, please click Reset.\r\n>\r\n> **v1.46.0 New/Fixed (four things)**: ① 📱 **The input method will no longer automatically pop up when switching modes on touch screen devices** - Previously, every time the mode was switched (World Info/Advisor/Calibration/Workshop/ Diagnosis, both entering and exiting) the oracle will automatically put the cursor into the input box, and the soft keyboard pops up on the mobile phone to interrupt the operation; now touch screen devices do not automatically focus (the keyboard pops up naturally when you click on the input box), the desktop mouse has the same feel, and the horizontal screen mobile phone / tablet can also recognize it (judged by the pointer type, regardless of the screen width). ② 🧭 **Advisor Plan Block Fault Tolerance** - The model occasionally writes the plan block label incorrectly (for example, the closing label is written as `</story_plan>`) or when the plan is truncated and not finished. Previously, the plan was **visible but not clickable** (it was rendered, and the adoption card could not be displayed); now the label variant and truncated plan can produce the \"Start Boot\" card as usual. ③ 📖 **Bai Bao Shu summary has a wider reach** - After checking \"Attached with Bai Bao Shu historical plot summary\", **World Info mode** (when checking \"Also bring recent plot dialogue\", the running summary will also be brought along at this time) and **Registered plug-in mode/second creation** (such as the outline version, when reading the story record through the interface) can now also read the summary of the hidden old building; the diagnosis mode is intentionally not connected. ④ ✨ **Auto-correction prompt words are open for customization** - \"Auto-correction·Light correction\" and \"Auto-correction·Fine correction\" are added in the \"System prompt word\" drop-down list, which can be changed and reset like normal/diagnosis/World Info/advisor (leave blank = use the built-in version, which will be automatically improved with updates; after fine-tuning is customized, it will take effect on both \"emphasis\"). Note that when customizing, keep the output format requirements (blocks such as `<FixedReply>`), otherwise the correction results will not be parsed and applied.\r\n>\r\n> **v1.45.0 newly added (🎨 three levels of window color matching)**: ⚙ Settings → 【 interface 】 has added \"window color matching\" - **Dark** (default for new installations), **Light**, **Follow the pub theme** (old behavior). Dark/light colors are fixed colors and are not affected by the theme of SillyTavern; if your beautification theme is frosted glass style, causing the words in the oracle window to be obscured by the chat behind it, just switch to dark or light color (these two settings will be turned off together with the frosted glass, and the main chat will no longer seep in). The skin covers everything the Oracle draws - the main window, the floating plan bar, the real-time output window, and the four overlay cards. **Old users will keep \"Follow SillyTavern Theme\" after upgrading, and the appearance will not change**. If you want to change it, you can change it yourself.\r\n\r\n> **v1.44.0 Added (✂️ \"Selected Correction\" shortcut button above the input box - off by default)**: Add a new switch in 【 Correction Settings → Manual 】. When checked, there will be an additional \"✂️ Selected Correction\" in the row above the chat input box (the same row as the quick reply button). Select a section in the main chat text and click on it to directly open the window, switch to correction mode, and pre-select that section - eliminating the back and forth of \"open window → switch mode → find that section again\". Just click without crossing anything, which is equivalent to opening the selection card with one click. The appearance of the button follows your theme and is consistent with the quick reply button next to it; if the quick reply extension is not installed, a button strip of the same style will be built and removed when the switch is turned off.\r\n\r\n> **v1.43.1 Repair (🎭 Workshop: The entire draft revised in the chat will disappear out of thin air)**: When asking the interviewer to **rewrite** a character draft in the workshop (for example, \"Don't make minor repairs, give me a reset version\"), it will give you a complete draft instead of sentence by sentence. Change——In the past, Oracle could not handle drafts like this: the drafts were only printed in the chat, and the resident card at the top remained motionless. It stayed at \"Existing interview summary (the draft has not been generated yet)\", and it was silent** (the user book also reported). Now this kind of complete draft will be put into the resident card as usual (the workshop panel will be automatically expanded, just like clicking \"🔨 Generate\" to publish a draft, you can continue to modify and then \"write\"); if the draft it writes is not in complete format (for example, the machine-readable header line is missing), it will also be **clearly stated that it has been confiscated and given the reason**, and will no longer be silently thrown away - your original draft will not be washed away by this kind of semi-finished product.\r\n\r\n> **v1.43.0 New**: Diagnosis 🩺 can also \"Apply my completion defaults\". There is a new checkbox in the diagnostic settings. When checked, the diagnostic instructions will be superimposed on the completion presets you have curated (**Manual diagnosis and automatic diagnosis are effective**) - Like the World Info/Consultant/Workshop/Calibration, it is mainly used to break the limit when the model refuses to do variable auditing (the diagnosis reads the main chat text, and models with censorship when the content is sensitive will still be rejected). If you select **Built-in limit breaking** under Default, it will also follow this checkbox. It is off by default; the preset extra content will distract the model's attention and affect the diagnosis accuracy, so don't turn it on if you don't need it.\r\n\r\n> **v1.42.0 Added**: The main chat quick entry - a ✂️ button will appear in the button row of the latest message replied by AI - select a paragraph of text in the text and click it (if the \"right-click message menu\" class extension is installed, \"Selection Correction\" will automatically appear in the right-click menu), Oracle will automatically open the window, switch to correction mode, and pre-select the paragraph you selected in the selection card, and scroll it to your eyes. You can just click without making a selection = open the selection card with one click. If the text is rewritten by a translation extension, or the word in the status bar is selected, and the original text cannot be located, the card will open as usual and prompt you to re-select within the card (you will never make a wrong selection or change). If there is a reply being generated at that time, the \"Do you still want to switch\" button will pop up to confirm - click Cancel and everything will remain unchanged.\r\n\r\n> **v1.41.0 added (🩺 Write diagnostic corrections into the text - default off; 1.65.0 starts in the \"Diagnostic Settings\" column and removes the \"Experimental\" mark)**: Automatic diagnostic corrections have always been only written into the **real-time status** of MVU and do not move in the message body. So just click on MVU's \"Reprocess Variables\" (it will clear the variables on that floor and recalculate only the message text), and the correction of this diagnosis will be gone. User smallmj reported: He relied on this button to load Tomoehime's illustrations, so he fell into an endless loop of \"reprocessing → correction and loss → reapplying → the illustration is stuck again\". **In the \"Diagnostic Settings\" column** of the diagnostic mode, there is \"**Write diagnostic corrections into the text**\" (default off; 1.65.0 Move here from the \"Interface\" group, next to the automatic diagnosis checkbox): After checking it, the correction will be written as a small patch into the existing update block of this reply (not a new one - that will make the status bar of most cards swallowed up by the folding panel), so no matter how many times you click \"Reprocess Variables\", the corrected result will be calculated. What is written in is the **actually calculated result value** rather than \"how much is added and how much is subtracted\", so no matter how many times you recalculate, you will end up with the same number. **Note**: Automatic diagnosis and manual \"🩺 Diagnosis\" click \"Apply\" will be written into the text; **Please keep it closed unless necessary**. **Fixed by the way**: In the past, clicking \"Undo this repair\" only restored the variables, but kept the part written in the text. The next time \"Reprocess Variables\" will be calculated according to it = undo is equal to undoing (the path of deriving patch blocks has always been like this); now undo/reapply will be synchronized **with the text**.\r\n>\r\n> **v1.40.2 fix (🩺 automatic diagnosis counts the same change twice)**: If your card uses **not** the standard `<UpdateVariable>` tag of MVU, but your own writing method (such as `<update>` + `<json_patch>`), Oracle **couldn't recognize** it before - so every round it was misjudged as \"this reply has not been updated with variables\", and I deduced it again** according to the plot**, and stacked it with the main model: **The money spent will be deducted twice, and the favorability will be increased twice** (reported by user smallmj). Now the identification of the update block no longer requires a hard-coded tag, and the card's custom writing method can also be recognized; and the judgment has been changed to **I would rather just verify, not easily deduce** - as long as it is seen that there is an update in this reply (even if the format is not standard and we cannot extract it cleanly), it will only be verified and will never be recalculated. When there is really no update block, it will be deduced and added as usual (the usage of \"replacing MVU additional model analysis\" will not be affected). **Two things have been fixed by the way**: ① In the past, the update block of this type of card would be **missed** and mixed into the context of ordinary chat/plot consultant (incremental numbers would mislead the model into falsely reporting values); ② When **automatic correction** is turned on, the version of the card that is replaced by the correction draft **will lose** the update block of the card. In addition, the prompt words sent by automatic diagnosis can now be seen in the \"**Debug Prompt Words**\" panel.\r\n>\r\n> **v1.37.0 Newly added (✂️ Selection correction · Multi-segment pinning selection - modify several paragraphs at one time) **: Selection correction can now **pin multiple paragraphs at one time** and modify them separately. Select a paragraph in the full text that pops up, click **📌 to pin this paragraph** (up to 8 paragraphs), and write a sentence \"How to change this paragraph\" under each paragraph - **leave blank and use the overall requirements above**; the pinned paragraphs are marked **cold blue** in the original text, and the paragraph being selected is still amber. The number of segments will be **honestly quoted**: if it is not nailed or only one segment is nailed, it will still be the same as \"Start Calibration\". If 2 segment is nailed, the button will change to \"Start Multi-segment Calibration (N segment, N calls)\". After clicking it, **each segment will send one call** (up to 3 paths are parallel, and the rest are queued). After the modification, a **segment-by-segment list** will be given - each segment has **[see changes]** diff, and each ticks to decide whether to adopt it or not. The title reads \"Changed X segment / Retained Y segment / Failed Z segment\", and the failed segment also has **[Retry failed] Z section]** One-click resend (the original request will be used without re-grabbing the context). After confirmation, the code will be used to insert each paragraph accurately at one time according to the character offset (spelling from back to front, there will be no misalignment between paragraphs), and the original reply will still be left in the left swipe, without damaging the archive. **Not a single word of the text you pinned will be entered into the model**, and it cannot be changed mechanically. **When pinning only a section (or directly selecting a section without pinning), the behavior is exactly the same as the old version of section selection correction. **\r\n>\r\n> **v1.36.0 Newly added (⏳ Confirm before generating mid-cut mode + ✂️✂️ Deeply streamline background keep-alive)**: Two things, both of which fix \"cut mode cuts out the reply being generated\". ① **Interruption confirmation for switching modes** - If you click another mode button when a reply is being generated, this reply will be **directly terminated and discarded** (each mode has an independent side chat room, and the reply in progress will be invalidated if you switch away - this is a design behavior, but it is easy to be mistaken for bug). Now a confirmation box will pop up first \"There is still a reply being generated - switching now will abort it, and unfinished content will be discarded\". Confirm before switching, cancel and stay in place. ② **Deep streamlining and enjoying the same background keep-alive as forging** - \"✂️✂️ Deep streamlining\" is the same multi-minute re-call as forging. In the past, it was stopped by switching to a mode and wasted money; now it runs in the background as usual after switching away, and the streaming bubble is automatically connected when returning to the workshop. After completion, the finished draft is returned to the original room (so it will not trigger the confirmation box above). Two points remain unchanged: the send key during generation is the ⏹ stop key (clicking it will still abort the background call); **switching chat** will still abort all calls in progress (the result belongs to the old chat and will not be written to the new chat).\r\n>\r\n> **v1.34.1 fix (✨ The thinking chain is strengthened and only `</think>` is left, the thinking can be peeled off)**: Some defaults will pre-fill the `<think>` opening tag** in the message sent to the model** (some inference models will also omit the opening tag), so there is only ** one `</think>` left in the model reply Closed tag**, the entire previous paragraph of thought is spit out directly as the text - Oracle used to encounter this kind of \"only closed tag\" situation, only delete the label literal, and leave the entire paragraph of thought in the bubble** (especially common in ordinary chat/plot consultant, the thought will be fed back to the next round as context). Now **when the closing tag appears before the opening tag, the entire thought from the beginning to `</think>` will be stripped together with the content** (bubble display and side chat history are stripped off at both ends). Guardrails: If the known structural blocks (`<StoryPlan>` / correction draft / character draft, etc.) are arranged before the closing tag, they will not be moved - your plan or draft will never be deleted by mistake.\r\n>\r\n> **v1.34.0 Newly added (🎭 Character Workshop·Full Lines)**: Many friends reported that the forged character Kari has **dry lines** - the meaning is right and the character is right, but the sentences are as short as telegraphs. When using it, you always have to manually let the model \"write the lines more fully and naturally\". There is now an additional switch in the workshop settings \"**Line Fullness (forging lines are written in complete human language)**\" (default off): When checked, all lines in the forging script (demonstration sentences for speaking methods, various language materials for multiple faces, and dialogue in the screen) will be written. **Full human words spoken in person** - with the character's current tone and speaking habits, allowing for emotions and details; **A character who talks less will still talk less**, but the few words he speaks will tell the whole thing in one breath, rather than breaking it into a few words. The character personality, number of cards, and card structure remain completely unchanged. This additional instruction has been checked and verified on DeepSeek / Gemini / Claude (including special judgments such as \"will a taciturn character be written as a talkative\" and \"will the mouths of aggressive and silent characters mix\") - just turn it on if you feel the lines are dry, and keep it off if you like the minimalist telegraph tone.\r\n>\r\n> **v1.32.0 Newly added (🛡 Long context to prevent deviation + clear name can be ghostwritten)**: Fixed a type of measured problem - when the chat record is very long (especially obvious when the chat record is more than 20,000 or 30,000 words), in ** normal chat / If you send short words such as \"then what\" and \"continue\" to the plot consultant**, or send the in-game speech** (character lines, bracketed actions, posted text fragments) that you want to send to the main chat by mistake, the model will no longer discuss it and directly continue to write the text for you (in serious cases, it will use the first person to pretend to be your character and speak). Now these two modes will package the story records into **read-only quotation materials** and add an \"off-screen reminder\" afterwards: ambiguous short messages will be treated as discussions (for analysis or rhetorical confirmation), and on-screen speeches sent to the wrong window will be pointed out instead of continued. At the same time, a new rule is set: **When you explicitly ask it to ghostwrite** (help write lines/monologues, rewrite and polish a certain paragraph, write your next reply, ask the consultant to write a draft of the scene directly...), it will **do it** - deliver it in an off-screen tone, indicate it is a draft, write only the paragraph you named, and stop after writing. Diagnostics/World Info/Calibration/Workshop mode are not affected.\r\n>\r\n> **v1.31.0 Newly added (📖 Side chat can also trigger World Info green light entries)**: Previously, the **green light (keyword trigger) entry only looked at the main chat** - if you enter the trigger word in the oracle side chat, it will not activate it (\"The name is clearly entered, but the relevant settings are not included\" is the reason). Now **normal chat, plot consultant, and manual correction (when \"World Info\" is checked) side chat Q&A also participate in keyword matching**: The trigger words in the recent side chat messages between you and the oracle count, and the number window is consistent with the main chat (use **\"Scan Depth\"** in the ST World Info settings, and it will be invalid when sliding out of the window - the same memory length as the main chat). The main chat's own scanning window is not occupied, and the behavior of the blue light (resident) entry remains unchanged. **Character Workshop** is an optional switch \"**Keyword Trigger World Info**\" (default off): when turned on, the setting items mentioned in chats and interviews will be fed to interviewers and forgers as **reference supplement blocks** - the books/entries checked in your **selector are still the only authoritative**, and the supplementary blocks will only be added but not subtracted, and checked items will not be fed repeatedly. Diagnostic mode remains scan-only for main chat (selected/mixed contracts unchanged).\r\n>\r\n> **v1.30.0 Newly added (🎭 Character Workshop · ✂️ Simplification of forging draft)**: There are two more buttons on the forged NPC draft card - ** \"✂️ Simplify the entire draft\" ** (one call: split long sentences, delete cross-section repetitions, much easier to read) and ** \"✂️✂️ Deep Simplification\" ** (3 Parallel section editing + 1 deletion of surgical orders, performed by the device on a knife-by-surgery basis, with deeper deletions). Simplify **Never touch the original**: After success, the **\"Original ⇄ Simplified Draft\" switch** will appear on the card. Writing and subsequent revisions will be based on the version you are currently displaying; a set of guards (chapter header/lines/status line/screen·derivative entity/agreement sentence) will **automatically return to the original** and explain it truthfully if any one of them is included. There is also a **\"Automatic streamlining after forging\"** switch in the settings (default is off) - when it is turned on, it will only automatically add a draft when the NPC draft is obviously lengthy (long sentences are densely packed). The already refined draft will not be used in vain. It is recommended to turn it on for strong output models (such as Claude). The forged drafts of DeepSeek/Gemini are usually already refined, and it will not make much difference whether it is turned on or not.\r\n>\r\n> **v1.27.0 Newly added (✨ Correction · ✂️ Selection correction - mark a section and change only this section) **: Added \"Selection Correction\" to manual correction. Click **✂️ Section Correction** on \"Correction Settings\", and the full text of the current reply will pop up. You **use your mouse/finger to select** the paragraph you want to change, write a sentence \"How to change\", and **send only this paragraph** to the model for rewriting. After modification, **insert it back into its original position accurately** - not a word will be moved in the places you **have not scratched (status bar, panel, other paragraphs) (they do not enter the model at all, so they cannot be accidentally deleted from the mechanism) / Change flowers). It is particularly suitable for two situations: ① **Long chat/weak model** When the entire correction is easy to \"copy the original text without changing/deleting it randomly\" - only change a small section, the model is much more stable (this has been verified by real DeepSeek 44 experiments: delineation rewriting in 8 million token context **zero degradation**); ② **Small surgical changes** (\"Make this line of dialogue cooler\" \"Rewrite this line to be more concise\"). The rewritten manuscript will first show you the changes diff**; if the model is **basically not changed**, or **crosses the boundary and is changed elsewhere**, or the length is abnormal, there will also be a **clear warning** (I won’t stop you, click after you see it clearly). Confirm it is correct and then **Apply** - the original reply will always remain in the left swipe and can be swiped back at any time, **without destroying the archive**. Want to change several paragraphs that are spread out? Just mark it twice and change it once each time. The unmarked section in the middle will remain unchanged.\r\n\r\n> **v1.25.0 Improvement (✨ Correction · Three Robustness Fixes)**: ① **\"The model has basically not changed\" will be clearly stated** - When manual correction encounters a model that is almost unchanged (a common \"copy the original text without change\" such as DeepSeek in high context), a new line **Amber Reminder** is added above the correction draft \"The model has basically not changed (changed about N) Words)... It is recommended to reduce the size of the previous text or try again\", and no longer fool you with a seemingly normal \"Apply\" button (the Apply button is still there - in case what you want is to correct a typo); in the automatic mode, directly ** press \"No Correction\" and do not submit the manuscript**. ② **New \"Correction Recovery Upper Limit\" setting** - Rewriting of long floors (about 3000 characters or more) often \"always fails\" because the output is truncated by the 4096 token floor. Now you can set the upper limit higher in the \"Calibration Settings\" (such as 8192 / 12288), leave blank = automatic (effective for both manual + automatic; if it exceeds the single limit of the service provider, it will be rejected, and it will be adjusted back if an error is reported). ③ **Old users are migrated to the streamlined default at one time**: 1.24.0 changed the manual correction default (without the previous text / World Info / summary), but ** the old default saved in the old archive (`-1` All previous articles) will not be automatically updated** - now the first load will **one time** move the items that are still stuck at the old default to the streamlined default and **replay the instructions once**. If you want to fully load the previous text, just change the \"Number of previous articles loaded\" back to `-1`. Another internal analysis has been fixed: when the model **mentions** the `<FixedReply>` tag in thinking, it will no longer be mistaken for the beginning of the manuscript.\r\n\r\n> **v1.24.1 Adjustment (🎭 Character Workshop·Chapter panel further streamlined)**: **\"Weaknesses and Defects\" and \"Abilities and Skills\" are no longer checked by default and moved to the end of the chapter line** - The default draft focuses on the nine core items (basic information, appearance, background, interpersonal relationships, personality, speaking style, goals, deep personality, prevention of misunderstanding). When you want to write about shortcomings or skills, you can just check them. If you check them, you will definitely write them (what you see is what you get remains unchanged).\r\n>\r\n> **v1.24.0 Repair + Improvement (✨ Correction·Manual mode default streamlined context + structure block retention)**: Fixed the problem of manual correction \"deleting/changing **non-text content** such as status bar/panel/HTML/Tu Sheng tags\", and **changed the default** of manual mode: ① **Previous text/World Info/plot summary are no longer included by default** (only send this reply + Character card) - Weak models (DeepSeek / Gemini, etc.) often cannot tell which item to change under high context, and the previous content is mixed into the results; there is a line of reminders at the top of the settings panel, and you can check each item one by one when you really need it (alignment settings/previous situations). ② Manual correction now ** retains the structure blocks in the reply as they are by default ** (status bar, `[方括号]` mark, HTML / XML panel, options, drawing prompts, etc.) and will no longer be deleted by general commands such as \"make the description more vivid\"; **but it will be up to you when you name it and want to change it** - for example, \"change the blood volume in the status bar to 50\", it only changes that one part, leaving the rest unchanged. (The automatic mode has a complete set of structural protection and is not affected.) Actual measurement by DeepSeek + Gemini cold model: 100% of the structural blocks survived, and only that block was moved when naming the block.\r\n>\r\n> **v1.23.4 Adjustment (🎭 Character Workshop · Panel streamlined + Interviewer will ask about appearance)**: ① **The \"Behavior Logic\" chapter is removed from the panel** - Make the draft containing panel more focused (it will be automatically canceled in the old archive, and the rest of the draft will not be affected; its underlying process is still maintained in the best state according to the latest verification round, and can be restored at any time in the future if needed); ② **The interviewer upgraded \"Appearance Characteristics\" to a required question** - As long as you want to write about appearance this time, and you haven't given material that is \"recognizable to TA\", it will definitely ask you for it and remind you on the spot: If you don't give real materials, AI loves to put scars and calluses on everyone when writing about appearance - TA TA can only be recognized by the traces left on his body (the work he does all year round, the places he often stays, and the habits of taking care of himself). It doesn't matter if you can't answer it. Say \"Whatever\" and it will write down \"Leave it to Forging to deduce from the experience of TA\" and continue the conversation (it won't ask if appearance is not checked).\r\n>\r\n> **v1.23.3 Polishing (🎭 Character Workshop · Gemini compliance nine repairs)**: The last round of management \"cross-card review\", this round audited the factory demo cards generated by Gemini one by one, and changed the nine prompt words that are prone to \"unruly\" to skeletonized writing (the same applies to DeepSeek, all are verified by cold model batteries, and the writing card process is not degraded): ① **Each of the multiple faces has a name** - Each face starts with a two- or three-character subtitle of 〔_face 〕 (previously, all the faces of Gemini were nameless and were written directly from the trigger condition); ② The **derivative items of the character portrait have color group titles** (\"X Derivative 1:...\" style, you can tell which color group it belongs to at a glance), each item is collected in two to four sentences, no longer longer; ③ The contrast between words and deeds is changed to **\"Screen 1\" \"Screen 2\"** serial number segmentation, daily scenes account for the majority, and the battle confrontation can only be one and can only be the finale - no longer half the page is about fighting; ④ **Swords and armor are no longer written into the appearance as physical characteristics**, and body descriptions are given with causes (why they are trained like this); ⑤ The ending of the keynote metaphor is no longer a countdown question of \"How many more times can it be broken?\", and the content of other sections is no longer pasted, and the metaphor is no longer translated back into the vernacular; ⑥ The target motivation is fixedly written in two layers: \"The version that is spoken of / the version that really drives TA\"; ⑦ The background of background experience no longer repeats the same thing as the shaping; ⑧ The examples of behavioral logic return to daily trivial matters (what to do when you are at a loss, embarrassed, asking for help, no longer drawing a sword); ⑨ To prevent misreading, there are two permanent items: \"way of speaking\" and \"way of writing\". **Known limitations**: Gemini occasionally still assigns sword-wielding characters with common career marks such as \"callus on the tiger's mouth/thick knuckles\" - if it's too cliché, just say \"Revision: Change the appearance mark to one that grew out of TA's own experience\" in the draft.\r\n>\r\n> **v1.23.2 polishing (🎭 Character Workshop·Cross-card \"reread\" management)**: Six prompt word surgeries were performed on \"I have built several characters, and the same thing always appears in the card\" (each of them has been verified by cold models, and does not reduce the craftsmanship of writing cards): ① The moral bottom line is no longer \"That is TA's final definition of himself\" - the ending is changed to the character's own words; ② The accompanying entity entries no longer copy the example sentences, but are changed to each card's own expression; ③ The \"canteen cooking\" example scene in the contrast between words and deeds has been removed (the co-produced character will move it in its entirety); ④ The appearance characteristics guide \"the imprint grows from TA's life\" - the scar/earlobe gap no longer has one for each person; ⑤ The three colors of Gemini's personality are no longer literal colors (grey/gold/white → Real mechanical words); ⑥ The keynote metaphor is anchored in the character’s own world (the character in the wasteland is no longer equipped with a sea fog lighthouse). Another tip: **Forging occasionally \"produces no draft\"** (any context length has a probability of about 8%, because the model spends all the output budget on thinking) - **Just try again**, it is not a setting problem.\r\n>\r\n> **v1.23.0 major overhaul (🎭Character Workshop · Comprehensive reconstruction of the forging process)**: The forging prompt words are rewritten section by section according to the eight-chapter course of \"Card Writing Classroom\" - 15 Each chapter is equipped with a set of **fill-in-the-blank skeleton** (each of the three colors of the character palette 3-4 The scene derivation of the strip title, the seven pieces of deep personality, and the prevention of misunderstandings one by one (\"About TA's 〔 characteristics 〕\"...), DeepSeek / Gemini were optimized section by section by 8 editors and then merged and accepted. Changes that users can perceive: ① The texture of the generated cards is obviously a step above ** - no labels are attached to the actions, the scenes are included in the facts, and the kindness is hidden in the practices; ② **\"Lifestyle Habits\" chip is changed to \"Behavior Logic\"** (What TA will do in daily trivial matters - specific reactions when suffering a loss/embarrassment/asking for help; the checkbox of the old archive is not affected); ③ When the World Info has entry format regulations (such as 【 origin, 】【 current status, 】 at the beginning and end of the status line) ** Priority is given to the rules of the world **; ④ The automatic lower limit of the upper limit of forging recovery **8192 → 12288** (previously, about half of the heavy forging in the entire chapter was truncated); ⑤ persona When the target has checked \"Multiple Faces\", all the lines will be included in the corpus of each face (if it is not checked, it will still be at most three sentences).\r\n>\r\n> **v1.18.3 revision (✨ Calibration · Newbie friendly interface + streaming calibration) **: \"Calibration settings · Automatic\" rearrangement - by default only the **judgment line, two running switches, calibration target, intensity** (the original \"calibration prompt word\" drop-down is renamed \"strength\"; ✂️tightening switch **removed**, light calibration constant tightening), and the rest are folded into **\"Advanced Settings (generally do not need to be touched)\"**. Added **Detection Receipt** above the reserved area: list in real time the structural blocks of this reply that are actually recognized and automatically retained**. The blocks that are recognized as missing will be fixed into the reserved area by **clicking**; if the format is not recognized correctly, please send a private message to **Discord @Prince**, and it will be added to the test set for repair. The reminder box when switching to automatic has been completely rewritten (the promise is more practical: **common formats** will be automatically recognized, and if you are not sure, you will **ask you once**). **\"Correct the latest reply according to the target\" now streams the correction manuscript** (respect the \"streaming\" switch, and the stop button can interrupt it at any time).\r\n>\r\n> **v1.18.0 Supplement (✨ Correction · \"Overall Correction\" is turned on by default + unknown tags will also ask)**: On the segmentation engine, the default is changed to **\"Overall Correction\"**: The text is merged into **1 calls** (no longer multiple times paragraph by paragraph), and the structural blocks sandwiched between the text (Settlement Panel / Tu Sheng / Note...) Change to **position anchor** in the call, and put the code **back to its original position** after correction - saving calls and making the whole article more coherent; **the content will not be lost** when the model moves the anchor point very occasionally (take it to the end of the text, the record will explain it truthfully, and you can restore it by swiping left to \"use original text\"). If you want the safe mode of \"the position is 100% controlled by the code, and if a single segment fails, only that segment will be lost\", turn off the **\"Overall Correction\"** in the \"Calibration Settings\" to return to segmented calls one after another. Two other points: ① When the card contains text with an unseen tag (such as `<narrative_x>`), it will now be asked once \"The text seems to be packaged in <narrative_x> - click here to confirm\" (previously it would be silently skipped); ② `<action_info>` settlement panel is added to the list of known structures (the panel of the Destined Poetry battle card is **guaranteed** to remain intact from now on).\r\n>\r\n> **v1.18.0 Newly added (✨ Correction · \"Segment Correction\" - multiple paragraphs of text will be corrected, and structural blocks will never be sent to the model)**: The automatic correction engine has been upgraded. Now it first splits the reply into \"text fragments + structure blocks\", and sends a normal correction call to the text section by section. Status bar/options/comments/code blocks/`[IMG_GEN]` These structures are not entered into the model at all and are put back together in the code - so problems such as \"the structure is changed/moved to the end\" will not happen mechanically. Three direct improvements: ① **Multiple `<content>` blocks will now all be corrected** (previously only the first block was changed); ② `<item_info>`/`<details>` and other structural blocks buried in the text are automatically saved (no need to manually fill in the reserved area); ③ **Cards that do not have mixed tags, prose and structural blocks** (the category with the most problem reports) can also be corrected - for the first time, a **\"needs to confirm once\"** will pop up for the first time: click to confirm that \"the text is prose outside of tags\", and then each reply will be automatically corrected in sections, and click to chat to remember. Side chat records now **truthfully** write \"Corrected N paragraph M in the text\" + the reason for each paragraph not being corrected; if most of the text is not corrected, a ⚠️ warning will be given and it is recommended to try again. In addition, a number of anti-fools have been connected: scope labels are automatically cleaned when they are out of focus (full angle brackets are also recognized), a warning will be given if the reserved area is filled with an incorrect pointed/square bracket and can be corrected with one click, and a reminder will be given when automatic is turned on but there is no connection. **Known trade-offs** (v1 intentional): each paragraph is corrected independently, and repeated clichés across paragraphs are not deduplicated; a single reply can send up to 4 fragment calls (the largest paragraph is given priority, and the excess is recorded truthfully); inline style tags follow the text, and may occasionally be deleted by the model (can be retained by naming in the exclusion area). The clean monoblock `<content>` card and pure prose card still follow the original path, and the behavior remains unchanged byte by byte.\r\n>\r\n> **v1.17.22 Fix (✨ Correction · No longer rush to write with MVU \"Extra Model Update\", opt-in)**: If you turn on MVU's \"Extra Model Update\" (use another model to parse variables asynchronously), it will rush to write at the same time as the automatic correction after the same reply, which may mess up the data. Now there is a new switch in \"Calibration Settings\" ** \"⏳ Use with MVU additional model update\" ** - when checked, the automatic calibration ** starts immediately as usual ** (in parallel with MVU, almost no wait), only waits for MVU to finish writing the variables before ** generating a new reply draft, and then merges the variable blocks it has written. The two will no longer rush to write the same message. **Unchecked by default**: People who do not need additional model updates will not be affected at all.\r\n\r\n> **v1.17.21 Newly added (✨ Calibration·Fine Calibration adds \"Gemini type\" focus)**: The \"Focus\" drop-down of fine calibration has an additional item **Gemini type** - select it when running calibration with Gemini (`gemini-3.1-pro-preview`, etc.). (According to actual measurement, Gemini's temperament is similar to that of DeepSeek: it will clean up the lines that report parameters in a series like \"Magic is Physics\", while the Opus version of \"Strike\" will overdo the formal/solemn lines, so the **Gemini type currently directly uses the prompt words of the DeepSeek version**; if it is made into Gemini in the future Exclusive version, the \"Gemini type\" you choose does not need to be changed, it will be automatically upgraded) DeepSeek / Opus users will not be affected at all.\r\n\r\n> **v1.17.20 improvements (minor repairs)**: ① ✨ The gray `content` placeholder prompt in the \"Only correct the text in this tag\" input box in the correction settings** has been removed** - the gray line of text in the previous box looks like the value has been filled in, which easily makes people think \"cannot be deleted / has been set to content\" \"; In fact, leaving it blank is a valid setting** (= correcting the entire reply). Now after clearing it, it will be a real empty box, and there will no longer be misleading gray words. (The default value is still the truly deletable `content` text, but the gray phantom is gone.) ② The title of the reset item in the mobile phone magic wand menu is shortened from \"Oracle Window Return (Centered)\" to \"Window Return\"** - Some mobile phone users reported that it is too long; the center icon remains unchanged.\r\n\r\n> **v1.17.19 Improvement (Mobile)**: Now **the entire title bar can drag the window** - before, the title bar squeezed 8 buttons, and only the small gap between the buttons could be dragged, which was difficult to grasp on the mobile phone. Now on mobile phones, you can move the window by pressing and holding anywhere on the title bar (including buttons); tapping the button still has the original function (relying on \"whether there is dragging after pressing\" to distinguish tapping/dragging). (The desktop remains unchanged.)\r\n\r\n> **v1.17.17 Added (✨ Calibration·Auto mode \"Fine Calibration\" prompt word)**: The automatic mode of \"Calibration Settings\" has added **\"Calibration Prompt Word\"** drop-down - **Light Calibration** (current prompt, default, behavior is completely unchanged) / **Fine Calibration** (a more thorough **three-step** correction: Tighten → Go to dialogue AI cavity → Go to narrate AI cavity, tightening is included). When selecting \"Fine Calibration\", there will be another **\"Fine Calibration Focus\"**: Select according to the model you are using - **DeepSeek / domestic model** select \"DeepSeek type\", **Claude/Opus** select \"Opus type\". (The two versions have **opposite directions** in processing the lines of \"reporting parameters in series like reading instructions\": the DeepSeek version is more restrained, and the Opus version is more proactive in cleaning up such \"data packet cavities\"; choosing the wrong emphasis will cause over-correction, so select separately according to the model.) The default is \"light correction\", and **if you do not select fine correction, everything will remain the same**, with zero impact on existing users.\r\n\r\n> **v1.17.16 Newly added (✨ Calibration·Auto mode \"Auto-configuration + Fool-proof\")**: Auto-calibration will now **recognize the text label of your card** - the first reply will be sniffed in the background, whether it is `<gametxt>` or `<正文>`, it will be automatically cut, **press chat to remember**, you basically don’t have to match it by hand; mismatching will not cause trouble (the set tag is not in this reply → **Skip without moving**, never change the entire status bar/options/World Info). Added in \"Correction Settings\": **\"Scan the text label of this card\"** (fill in the scope with one click + check the structural blocks in the text and add them to the reserved area), **Judgment preview line** (switch to automatic to display \"How will this reply be processed at this moment\"), **\"Restore recommended settings\"** restore with one click. Two more corrections were made to bug: **cut chat** during correction will no longer write changes into other conversations; model replies that are **truncated** into half sentences will no longer be mistakenly applied as corrections. Tags you fill in by hand are never automatically overwritten.\r\n\r\n> **v1.17.15 Improvement (Mobile Phone)**: Fixed the old problem on mobile phones that \"window buttons are crowded at the top and cannot be reached/windows are dragged and lost and cannot be found\" - ① When opening for the first time, the window **centered** pops up, and the title bar is no longer pushed to the status bar / under the Liu Haihai; ② A new item **\"Oracle Window Return (Centered)\"** is added to the Magic Wand menu (exclusive for mobile phones), which can reset the window** to the center of the screen with one click + Default size** - Even if the window is dragged off the screen and the size is damaged, you can still save it at any time. (The desktop is not affected.)\r\n>\r\n> **v1.17.14 Fix**: ✨ After the calibration point \"Calibrate latest reply by target\", it can now be interrupted** - the send key will become the \"stop\" key, click it to stop immediately (previously, you could only wait for it to finish running/timeout).\r\n>\r\n> **v1.17.13 Fix**: ✨ **Manual Calibration** When encountering a model that does not spit out the standard `<FixedReply>`, it will no longer directly report \"Failed to parse the correction draft... Please check the connection/model\" - it will try to **save the correction draft back** from the reply (weak models / messy tags / thinking of full quota can be pocketed), and when it is really truncated, it will clearly tell you that it is \"truncated\". (Strict parsing in automatic mode is unchanged.)\r\n>\r\n> **v1.17.12 Fix**: ✨ **Auto-correction/Auto-diagnosis** The problem of occasionally \"changing to the previous reply instead of the one just received\" has been fixed - now firmly **pin the triggered message**; if the message is temporarily empty / pushed by the updated floor, it will be skipped cleanly and the old reply will never be changed by mistake.\r\n>\r\n> **v1.17.11 Improvement**: Switch to ✨ The reminder box when correcting \"Auto\" is rewritten as **Simple instructions for newbies**: Automatic correction** only changes the story text in `<content>` by default**, the status bar / options / World Info / picture / panel outside the text will be retained as they are, generally there is no need to set anything; the only thing to confirm is - if your card uses other tags to wrap the text (such as `<gametxt>`), change the column \"Only correct the text in this tag\" to that tag name.\r\n>\r\n> **v1.17.10 Fix**: ✨ The **\"View Changes\" of the correction \"Calibration by Target\" card no longer falsely reports** - it used to put you into the reserved area, but the blocks that were actually well preserved (such as `<branches>`, `<sceneinfo>`) were displayed as a large red deletion, making people mistakenly think that they were deleted (in fact, those blocks were not sent for correction at all, and were still there after application). Now \"View Changes\" compares the **actually applied results**: retained blocks are no longer marked in red, only the text that was actually changed and the blocks that were deleted because you did not retain them will be displayed.\r\n>\r\n> **v1.17.9 improvements**: ✨ Correction of \"exclusion area\" is stronger: ① supports **nested tags with the same name** (`<div>` set `<div>` will now retain the outermost layer in **the whole block** and will no longer be chopped); ② supports **square bracket blocks** (`[IMG_GEN]…[/IMG_GEN]` of Tusheng Card, etc., directly put them `[IMG_GEN]` can be written into the reserved area). With 1.17.8's \"Only correct the text in this tag\", the status bar/options/images/panel of the structured card can basically be maintained stably.\r\n>\r\n> **v1.17.8 New (Important)**: ✨ Correction added **\"Only correct the text within this tag\"** (default `content`). Structured cards (with status bar/option menu/World Info/`<htmlcontent>` map, etc.) wrap the main text in `<content>…</content>`. After turning it on, only the main text will be corrected, and all blocks outside the main text will remain intact and remain in place. This completely solves the problem of \"automatic correction deletes all things outside the main text/it is useless to put labels into the reserved area\". Just fill in **a** tag name (if the card uses other tags to wrap the text, change it to that one), leave it blank = correct the entire reply. If there is no such tag in the reply, the entire article will be automatically corrected (simple cards will not be affected).\r\n>\r\n> **v1.17.7 Added × 2**: ①【🧭 The system prompt word of plot counselor 】 can now also be set in 【 → View/modify in the system prompt word 】 (previously only diagnosis/World Info could be changed; only single-shot counselor commands were available, and the arc compiler did not move). ②Cut to 【✨ Correction → A one-time reminder will pop up when automatically 】: Automatic correction will rewrite the entire reply. If you want to keep paired tag blocks like `<sceneinfo>` and `<details>` as they are without being moved/deleted, please change its **start tag** (such as `<sceneinfo>`, the ending `</sceneinfo>` (no need to write) is added to the \"Exclusion Area·Reserved\". You can check \"Don't prompt again\".\r\n>\r\n> **v1.17.6 Fix**: 🩺 **Variable Diagnosis** After manual \"Apply/Undo\", the floor variable panel (status bar) will now **automatically refresh** to new data. There is no need to manually click \"Reread Initial Variables\" (automatic diagnosis will be refreshed in the first place, this time the manual method is added).\r\n>\r\n> **v1.17.5 Repair/Improvement (Mobile Phone)**: The **folded circular compass floating window** after closing the window during plot guidance - ① is made **translucent** when resting, and no longer blocks the text below (touch it / It will automatically return to clear when dragging); ②Now you can drag again** (previously it couldn't be dragged after it was folded into a small compass, because the whole pill is a button and is regarded as a \"click\" rather than a \"drag\" - tapping is still expanding, dragging is moving).\r\n>\r\n> **v1.17.4 New**: When the auto-correction/auto-diagnosis is running, the \"Automatic...\" prompt can now be interrupted with one click (used when the background runs for too long, or if you want to stop); the interruption occurs before writing, so this reply will not be changed.\r\n>\r\n> **v1.17.3 Fix**: ✨ The label block set to \"Keep\" during correction (such as `<details>` that lets AI be written in the middle of the text) will **remain in the original position** after the change and will no longer be moved to the end of the reply.\r\n>\r\n> **v1.17.2 Fix**: ✨ After correction is applied, the reply in the main chat will now **immediately switch to the correction draft** without having to \"click/swipe\" to display it (cards rendered with Xiaobai X / Translation Extension would previously stop at the old reply; cards rendered by SillyTavern are not affected).\r\n>\r\n> **v1.17.0 New**: ✨ Calibration mode, \"↻ Retry\" if sending failed, \"⋯ More\" menu in the top bar, World Info multi-selection + entry content preview, \"Only character-related World Info\", read hidden floors.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Install and open\r\n\r\nPut the entire `story-oracle/` folder into the third-party extension directory of SillyTavern and refresh the browser:\r\n\r\n- **Newer version ST**: `SillyTavern/data/<用户名>/extensions/story-oracle/` (default `default-user`)\r\n- **Older version ST**: `SillyTavern/public/scripts/extensions/third-party/story-oracle/`\r\n\r\nOpen the **Magic Wand Menu** (🪄 next to the input box) → **Story Oracle**. If you want to enter and exit faster, you can check \"Show shortcut buttons in the chat input field\" in the settings, and there will be an additional one-click switch 🌙 next to the input box.\r\n\r\n### 🔔 Update reminder (from 1.38)\r\n\r\nWhen opening the Oracle window, it will automatically check for a new version (check once every time after refreshing the page): it is found that there is an update on GitHub, the **⋯ / ⚙ button** of the title bar and the **\"Update\" group** at the top of the settings panel will light up **red dot**, and the group will display \"New version vX.Y.Z found\" and an **\"Update now\"** button - click it to use SillyTavern's own extended update mechanism to pull the new version. After success **5 Automatically refresh the page** in seconds to take effect (**Click the prompt to cancel the refresh**, you can also refresh it yourself later).\r\n\r\n- **Prerequisites for one-click update**: The extension is installed through SillyTavern \"Download Extension\" (fill in the GitHub address). If you manually copy the folder and install it, the one-click update will fail. Follow the prompts to update in \"Extension Management\", or go to GitHub to re-download and overwrite.\r\n- **Privacy**: The check only reads the **public version number file** on GitHub (if it cannot be opened, change the jsDelivr image and try again), **does not send any data**; if it fails, it will be silently skipped without disturbing you.\r\n- If you don't want it, just uncheck \"Automatically check for updates\" in the \"Update\" group (there will no longer be any online checks).\r\n\r\n## Settings\r\n\r\nTitle bar \"⋯ More\" menu → ⚙ **Settings**. Two connection methods:\r\n\r\n- **Direct connection (Direct, default)**: Fill in the endpoint URL (such as `https://your-proxy.com/v1`, `/chat/completions` will be automatically added), API key, and model. The key plain text exists in ST and settings.json (personal/self-built instances are okay).\r\n  - **Forwarded via SillyTavern backend (avoiding cross-domain CORS)** ✅: Check this option when reporting directly **CORS / failed to fetch** - **The above endpoint and key are still used**, but it is forwarded by SillyTavern server instead, bypassing the browser cross-domain, **No need to connect the configuration file**. After checking **\"Get Model\" is also sent through SillyTavern server** (from 1.18.1), pulling the model list will no longer cause cross-domain collisions.\r\n  - **Use the address as it is (no automatic filling of /v1)** (from 1.22): Used for transfer stations with special routes - the address is clearly filled in correctly but 404 / cannot pull the model, most likely it is automatically filled in `/v1`. After checking, request according to the address you filled in as it is (only `/chat/completions` is left in the completion, \"Get model\" hits `地址/models` in the same way), which is often used in conjunction with the forwarding switch above.\r\n  - **Connection Archive** (from 1.20, renamed from 1.40): At the bottom of the direct connection area, you can save the current **endpoint/key/model (from 1.22 with the \"Address as is\" switch)** as a named archive, and use \"Save/Load/Delete\" to switch to different service providers at any time with one click; a confirmation box will pop up before deletion. ⚠ The \"Archive\" here is different from the **Complete Default** in the \"System Prompt Words\" area below - before 1.40, it was called \"Connection Default\". Some users mistakenly thought it was a custom default area, so the name was changed.\r\n- **Connection configuration file (Profile)**: Select a saved ST connection configuration; the request will be forwarded through the ST backend and **will not be blocked by CORS**. ⚠ Note: If the configuration file **does not come with its own independent key**, ST will fall back to using the key of your **currently activated connection** - at this time, the configuration file selected by the oracle must be consistent with the connection currently being used by SillyTavern, otherwise **401 / 400** will occur (the key is sent to an endpoint that does not recognize it). If you want to completely avoid this pitfall, in most cases it will be easier to just use the above \"direct connection + forwarding through SillyTavern backend\".\r\n- **Additional Parameters** (from 1.70 onwards): The \"Additional Parameters\" button in the \"Connection\" area will pop up the same three boxes as the ST \"Customized (compatible with OpenAI)\" interface - **including main parameters** (additional parameters sent with each request, YAML or JSON Object), **exclude body parameters** (a list of parameter names to be excluded from the request), **include request headers** (additional request headers). The most common use: **Turn off the thought chain for DeepSeek type transfer** - otherwise the model will run a long series of thought chains before replying, and the token fee will be paid in vain. Just fill in the switch recognized by your service provider in \"Include main parameters\", for example:\r\n  ```yaml\r\n  enable_thinking: false\r\n  ```\r\n  (Each company writes it differently: some are `enable_thinking: false`, some are `thinking: {type: disabled}` or `reasoning_effort: none` - refer to your service provider's document. Official DeepSeek directly replaces the model with `deepseek-chat` There is no thought chain, no need to fill in the parameters) Leave the three boxes blank = everything is as usual. Validity range: **Direct connection mode** (including \"Forwarding via Tavern Backend\") is all valid; in **Connection Profile** mode, only the API configuration file with the type \"Customized (compatible with OpenAI)\" is valid. Official interfaces such as OpenAI / Claude / Gemini will ignore these parameters. Incorrect formatting will not be silently ignored - when sending, the error will be clearly reported to indicate which box it belongs to.\r\n\r\nCommonly used options: temperature, maximum token, **context depth** (how many recent messages to feed, `-1` = whole paragraph, `0` = no feeding), whether to bring character cards, system prompt words. Normal mode also has real-time variable status by default (stat_data), so \"How much favorability\" will be answered according to the real value; when MVU is turned off or the card is disabled, it will truthfully say that the value cannot be seen and not make it up. The sources of world information can be \"all activated World Infos\", \"**only character related (excluding global)**\", etc., and \"**Read hidden floors**\" can be turned on to let it read the floor of `/hide`. World Info also has a \"**Customization (manual selection of books and entries)**\" (1.81.0) - just like the World Info Butler, select multiple books to be sent, and then check the items one by one. Only the ones you checked will be sent (ignore keywords and enable/disable; only when \"Mixed Mode\" is turned on, the green light currently triggered in the selected book will be added), with filtering and only blue light / Only green light and other shortcut keys, select **press current chat memory**, when a book enters the range for the first time, pre-select a copy according to the current activation status; use it when the entire book has a blue light, relies on plug-ins to limit the flow, or oracles but the entire book is issued. Two notes: the default scans of the Diagnostic/Variable Editor also follow it, but they will still bring in the variable rule entries in addition; the corrected \"Bring the currently active World Info\" is not affected by it. Setting items are grouped by purpose and collapsible. By default, only \"Connections\" are expanded.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🔓 Built-in limit breaking (from 1.40)\r\n\r\nDoes the model always refuse, preach, or just write off what needs to be written? The **Completion Defaults** drop-down in settings now has an item:\r\n\r\n> **🔓 Built-in limit breaking · Original intention to break the limit 1.2 (from the first encounter with the boss) **\r\n\r\nSelect it to take effect. **Newly installed users and users who have never selected a preset will have it selected for you by default**; if you** have already selected it and selected it\r\nYour own default**, we will not touch your choice**.\r\n\r\n**It is \"covering\", not \"replacing\". ** The normal default path is to **overall replace** the oracle's own prompt words; the built-in limit breaking is different,\r\nIt wraps the limit-breaking block around the oracle's own prompt word - the oracle's analysis framework, off-screen guards, and structured formats for each mode are all used as usual.\r\nTherefore, the system prompt word text box below will not be disabled.\r\n\r\n**By default, it only works on 【 normal chat 】. ** It is up to you to decide whether you want to use other modes - go to the settings of each mode and check it\r\n**\"Complete the default by customization\"** (World Info/Plot Consultant/Character Workshop Interview/Correction Manual/Correction Automatic).\r\n**🩺 Never pick up diagnostic mode**: It only does mechanical variable repair, there is no such thing as \"rejection\", and its parser is the most sensitive.\r\n\r\n**Cancel at any time**: Just change back to \"—Custom—\" or your own default in the same drop-down list.\r\n\r\nAfter opening it, the plot consultant will obviously be more willing to take the initiative and say, \"I can help you write this paragraph.\"\r\n\r\n> The content of breaking the limit comes from \"The original intention to break the limit 1.2\" by **Meet the boss for the first time** (the built-in version is updated with the author 1.0 → 1.2). The author deleted it in 1.2\r\n> Natural language main prompt words, only retain the `<sys>` rule block and the end of the sentence, and the built-in version will follow suit. The thinking chain layer in the original default\r\n> (Think Override / Think Lock, 1.2 onwards Think Override is enabled by default) ** still does not include ** - it is related to the limit breaking function\r\n> Irrelevant, but it will allow the thought process to leak into the bubble and disrupt the structured output format of Diagnosis/World Info/Calibration/Workshop.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 💬 Normal chat\r\n\r\nDefault mode, just ask for the plot. The system prompt word is rebuilt every time it is sent, so the Oracle always sees the latest story status.\r\n\r\n## 🩺 Diagnostic mode (Diagnose)\r\n\r\nFix state variables for MVU (MagVarUpdate). Oracle reads the MVU rules of this card, the current `stat_data`, and the `<UpdateVariable>` in the latest reply, and provides a **conservative corrective patch** based on the plot; an **Apply fix to state** button appears below the bubble, which is applied through MVU's own pipeline and can be **undoed** with one click. The full audit output is relatively long, and the upper limit of token has been automatically raised to ≥4096.\r\n\r\n**Patch physical examination + automatic correction (from 1.67.0, automatically effective, no switch). ** When you click \"Apply\", the patch will first be checked according to MVU's own rules, and the common writing methods of the model will be fixed on the spot (verb synonyms → `replace`, extra slashes at the end of the path, `delta` written as `\"+5\"` string, `[数值,\"说明\"]` fields are written back in pairs, `<JSONPatch >` The spaces in the tags and the path with an extra layer of `stat_data` are removed), and the **format-irregular entries** that are mixed in are removed separately - if not removed, MVU will discard the entire instruction together**. Each category is only started when there is evidence (after modification, it will match your current variables); the number of modifications will be displayed in the status line. Manual \"🩺 diagnosis\" and automatic diagnosis follow the same assembly line.\r\n\r\n**We will tell you why when it does not take effect. ** If a value has not changed, each instruction will give a definite reason (the path does not exist / it is this value / the verb MVU does not recognize / the type of the value does not match / there are internal fields starting with an underscore / **This layer is that the card is not marked as an expandable object or list, and new items are not allowed** / **The item to be added or subtracted is not a number or a date**...) and a next step suggestion - the latter two categories are 1.77.3 is judged according to the card's own structural definition. If the patch itself is **fully compliant but still has zero changes**, it will tell you **where to look for the real reason**: SillyTavern → \"MVU Variable Framework\" panel → Notification → Check \"Notify when errors occur during variable initialization/update\", run it again, and `[MVU]` will pop up (the card with mvu_zod is `[MVU zod]`) The prompt will indicate which instruction it was and why it was rejected.\r\n\r\n**Automatic Diagnosis (AUTO) ⚠ Experimental. ** In the \"**Diagnosis Settings**\" column of the diagnosis mode, check \"**Automatically diagnose every new reply**\" to turn it on (from 1.65.0: the diagnosis button only turns on/off the diagnosis of this room, and whether it is automatic or not is exclusive to this check box; when checked for the first time, a one-time explanation will be played first, and it will be turned on only after confirmation). After turning it on, the diagnosis button turns red, and every new reply in the main chat will be automatically diagnosed in the background and **automatically applied** - the judgment is based on \"whether the **variable engine has been executed in this round**\" (from 1.69.0): if it is really executed, it will only be verified (cards with custom tags such as `<update>` are also recognized, v1.40.2 (starting); there is absolutely no update block in the text, so just add it based on the plot derivation; if the block is there, but one of the broken ones has not been executed, then re-derive the round based on the plot (this one only writes variables and does not leave the message text). Each round leaves a record in the side chat (changed records with \"undo\"; \"unable to understand the model's reply\" type of record, if the reply summary is truncated (at the end...), there will be a \"**View complete reply**\" button on the record, click on it to view the original text of the model reply - only valid within this session, starting from 1.71.1), and write the update back to the message and refresh the status bar. **If there is no MVU data on this floor at all** (MVU has selected \"Additional Model Analysis\" but not checked \"Enable Automatic Request\", it will do nothing for this floor), the automatic diagnosis will first copy the status of the previous floor, fill in the status bar placeholder and then diagnose (starting from 1.77.2; give MVU three and a half seconds first, and it will not intervene after it handles it by itself). **Leaving diagnostic mode will not turn it off** - the button remains red to indicate that it is still running in the background; to stop, return to diagnostic mode and uncheck it.\r\n\r\n**Automatically retry on failure (from 1.74.0, off by default). ** After checking \"**🔁 Automatically retry on failure**\" in the diagnostic settings, the automatic diagnosis will automatically retry if this round of failure is not completed: the number of times can be filled in (default 2, upper limit 99), and three types of failure situations can be checked respectively - **Blank reply** (the model returns no content), **Format error** (cannot understand / Rejection of updates given by the model includes situations where rejection is based on rules such as \"one reply to two update blocks\"), **call failure** (network error/timeout, etc.), three independent combinations. Each retry is a **complete round**: wait for MVU again, re-read the current status, regroup the prompt words, and then send the request again; the ongoing prompt indicates the number of retries and will be interrupted with one click. The diagnosis is successful, the verification is passed without any changes, and it is safe to skip (cut chat/status changed/manual interruption/new reply to cancel this round) **Never retry**. Only applies to automatic diagnosis; manually clicking \"🩺 Diagnosis\" will not be affected.\r\n\r\nIf you use the \"**Extra Model Analysis**\" of TavernHelper / MVU at the same time, then check \"**⏳ Compatible with MVU \"Extra Model Analysis**\"\" (off by default; people who don't use external analysis will not have to wait). The oracle will observe **4 seconds** after the reply lands: if no external parsing is detected, it will immediately continue with normal automatic diagnosis; once detected, it will wait for its **entire retry batch** to end, rather than being fooled by the short \"idle\" between retries. When the external parsing successfully writes the update block, automatic diagnosis is responsible for verification; when the external parsing fails, retries are exhausted, or no valid block is written, the automatic diagnosis is deduced according to the plot as usual. You can wait up to **10 minutes** for a single batch. If you still cannot confirm the completion, you can safely skip this round and never rush to write. If automatic correction is also turned on, it can be generated in parallel as usual, but the wait will be shared before swipe is updated, and the update block written after MVU will be aligned with the status bar placeholder and entered into the correction draft. Old oracle jobs are silently invalidated while the user waits for the next message; MVU's own external requests are not forcibly canceled.\r\n\r\n**Allow writing MVU in conjunction with other scripts (from 1.83.0, off by default). ** Some character cards come with \"post-turn\" scripts (world advancement, variable verification, etc.), which will rewrite the MVU variable after each reply, and some will also adjust the model themselves first; while automatic diagnosis first writes down the variables at that time, then asks the model, and then writes them back - as long as the variables are touched by others in the meantime, the entire round will be invalidated, and each round will be recorded as \"Skipped: MVU variable was changed during the automatic diagnosis run.\" After checking \"**🧩 Allow simultaneous writing of MVU** with other scripts\" in the diagnostic settings, the automatic diagnosis no longer gives up in the whole round: the corrections given by the model are viewed **one by one**, and those that fall on values ​​that have not been touched by others are written as usual (written on top of the latest current variables). Those that happen to hit the values ​​​​that have just been changed by others are **skipped and not written**, and which ones (paths) are named at the end of the record; they are still skipped when they all hit. Only the standard `<JSONPatch>` writing method is recognized, the patch of `_.set` writing method cannot be cut and will be skipped as usual. In addition, starting from 1.83.0, the round that passed the model verification and was given an **empty patch** will no longer be recorded as skipped because of \"variable changes\" - there is nothing to write in the first place, and the record simply says \"no changes required\". The \"Apply\" button after manually clicking \"🩺 Diagnosis\" is not affected by this check.\r\n\r\n> **v1.66.0 interface repair**: When there are too many diagnostic settings, the settings bar occupies at most half of the Oracle window, and the excess part is scrolled in the bar, and the chat area and input box are no longer pushed out of the window; the \"Diagnostic Settings\" at the top can still be folded.\r\n\r\n> ⚠ This is **the only function that automatically writes the MVU status**, so it is off by default and needs to be manually switched to red**. There will be a reminder when it is turned on for the first time. If you're not sure, just stop at manual \"🩺 Diagnosis\" - it will only issue a patch after you click on it.\r\n\r\n**Write corrections into the text (optional, off by default). ** By default, diagnostic corrections are only written into the **real-time status** of MVU and do not change the message text - so once you click **\"Reprocess Variables\"** of MVU** (it will clear the variables on that floor and recalculate only the text), the correction is gone. After checking \"**Write diagnostic corrections into text**\" in the \"**Diagnostic Settings**\" column of diagnostic mode, the diagnostic corrections (automatic and manual) will be written as a short patch into the existing update block of this reply. When the variables are reprocessed, the same result will still be calculated; when undoing, the section will also be removed. What is written is the **result value** (absolute value) rather than the increase or decrease, so repeated recalculation will not drift. **Both automatic and manual diagnosis are covered** - Manual \"🩺 Diagnosis\" and \"Apply\" will also be written into the text, and will be removed when undoing. Please keep it closed unless necessary.\r\n\r\n**Featured entries (optional). ** After checking \"Use Selected Entries\", you can **select** the entries to be fed to the diagnosis one by one like the World Info mode, and **ignore** the enabled/disabled status of ST - so the variable rule entries that are disabled (to keep the main chat clean) can also be fed to the diagnosis alone. With quick selection and filtering, **press current chat memory**.\r\n\r\n**🎛 Variable Editor (from 1.55.0). ** The **\"🎛 Variable Editor\"** button in the diagnostic settings will open a \"Game Modifier\" style panel: arrange all the current MVU variables in this chat into **pagination + collapsible tree** (the pagination follows the character card's own grouping structure). You can directly change whichever you want to change - number box (with a slider when you recognize the value range), text box, switch, the list can **add/delete items**, `[数值,\"描述\"]` For such fields with descriptions, only the values are changed and the descriptions are retained as they are. (1.89.0) On a card with variable rules, before writing the diagnosis, it will be rehearsed according to the rules, and only the parts that can pass will be written, and \"🩺 Check Archive\" will be provided to find out the non-compliant values ​​in the archive. Folders/fields/lists in tabs can also be deleted using **🗑 Delete** (1.88.0; mark first and click \"Apply\" to take effect, ↩ unmark and it can be undone after application; the tab itself cannot be deleted). Changes will be highlighted and counted. Click \"Apply\" once to write them uniformly (using MVU's own writing channel, **no model calls, no money, and never change chat messages**). The status bar will be refreshed immediately, and a \"🎛 Manual Edit\" record will be left in the diagnostic side chat with an **\"Undo\"** button. The search box can find field names across pages.\r\n\r\n- **「🔍 Analysis value rules」 (optional, one model call). ** Some cards have rules in the World Info that limit certain fields to only a few values ​​(for example, the mood can only be \"calm/happy/angry\" because it needs to be linked to the front-end rendering). Clicking this button will hand over the variable rules of this card to your model for analysis. The identified restricted fields will become **drop-down boxes** and the value ranges will be fed to the sliders; the results **click on the chat cache** (free later) and can be \"rescanned\". You can click **⏹ to interrupt** while scanning. There will inevitably be errors in recognition - there is a ✎ next to each drop-down box to switch back to free input.\r\n- **Scope of undo. ** The undo of each \"Manual Edit\" record restores the **entire state before that application**: If you apply other modifications later (or write automatic diagnosis), undoing the earlier one will roll back all subsequent changes. The undo button is valid within **this session**, and the record becomes read-only after reloading the page (consistent with the diagnostic record).\r\n- **Tips. ** A list with exactly 2 text items (such as only two items in a backpack) will be displayed as a \"numeric value + description\" pair by the MVU convention - only affecting the display method and not destroying the data. Starting from 1.56.0, there will be an additional **≡** button next to this type of field: click it to display it **as a list** (items can be added/delete), **⇄** to switch back, and select **Press Chat Memory**.\r\n- **Scan reply truncated? ** If your model is a \"thinking type\" (reasoning takes up a lot of output quota), the scan reply may not be completed; starting from 1.56.0, a clear prompt will be given that \"the reply is incomplete (may be truncated)\" - just change to a non-thinking type model or try again (starting from 1.57.0, the scan output limit is raised to 16384).\r\n- **⤢ Zoom editing (from 1.57.0). ** The text box is too small? There is **⤢** next to each text input box: click to open a large editing window (filling the editor panel), press \"OK\" to write back after making changes, and \"Cancel / ✕ / Click Mask\" to give up; pressing OK without making changes means doing nothing. Note: The field value itself is a single line - line breaks in large windows will be merged and explicitly prompted.\r\n- **The editor follows the plot (starting from 1.59.0). ** When the editor is open, if the plot progresses (new replies, automatic diagnosis and corrections, etc.), the panel will **automatically refresh to the latest values** - the values ​​you are changing will not be affected, and a prompt will appear \"Untouched values ​​have been synchronized\". When you are typing or have a magnified editing window open, it will wait quietly for you to finish before refreshing. In addition: If the status of a \"Manual Edit\" record changes again after clicking \"Undo\", it will **confirm with you** first (because it will also roll back the subsequent changes).\r\n\r\n**🎛 Modifiers (from 1.63.0). ** Do you want a variable to \"maintain itself\" without having to manually change it every time? There is a 🔒 button at the end of each editable field line in the variable editor - click it to freeze the field at its current value: after every new reply is processed (after correction/diagnosis is run), Oracle will quietly pull it back to the number you locked, even if the plot or diagnosis has changed it; click again to unfreeze it. In addition to freezing, fields can also be linked to **\"±X per round\"** (for example, money automatically +100 per round) and **\"upper and lower limits\"** (for example, physical strength is not less than 0 and not more than 100) - the three rules can be stacked on the same field at the same time. The fixed algorithm is **±X first, then upper and lower limits, and freeze overrides everything**. There is a special **\"🎛 Modifier\"** page at the end of the variable editor page, which lists all the rules in effect in this chat (click ✕ to delete), and you can use its form to add ±X / upper and lower limit rules to frozen fields (use 🔒 to freeze once before the fields will appear in the drop-down list of the form); the bottom of the page will display what has been changed by the \"last round\" modifier, making it easy to confirm that the rules are indeed in effect.\r\n\r\n- **Rules follow the chat, don't tell AI. ** The rules are saved according to **Current Chat** (changing chats will not affect each other), it is purely calculated by the code - no model calls are made, no money is spent, AI is ​​completely unaware of the existence of these rules (will not appear in any prompt words), so it will not be \"explained\" or bypassed by the plot. Also because it runs quietly, no prompts are played, and no side chat records are left - if you want to confirm whether it has taken effect, go to the 🎛 modifier page and look at the line \"Previous Round\".\r\n- **Will manual changes to the rules cause fights? ** No - if you manually change a frozen field in the variable editor and click \"Apply\", the **freeze target of that field will be automatically updated to the new value** you just wrote** (otherwise the next reply will pull back your manual changes); the ±X / upper and lower limit rules on the same field will not be affected and will remain the same. When this \"manual editing\" record is revoked/reapplied, the frozen target that was updated by the way will also be replaced with the value before/after the revocation - there will be no situation where \"you clicked Undo, and the next reply was quietly pulled back by the rules.\"\r\n- **⚠ will be washed away by \"reprocessing variables\". **MVU's **\"reprocessing variables\"** is to recalculate** `stat_data` from the beginning according to the message text - it does not know the existence of the modifier rule, and will overwrite the value just written in the rule after calculation. After using \"Reprocess Variables\", the modifier will automatically apply the rules again when there is a new reply. If you happen to be looking at the status bar on the middle floor, you may see that the numbers first fall back to what they were before the rules were applied. This is normal and not bug.\r\n- **Freezing only takes effect for \"editable single-value fields\". ** If a frozen field later becomes a list or group (for example, a list of two items is added by the plot, or the path of the rule originally points to an entire group of data), the modifier will safely skip this rule and will never replace the entire list/group with the frozen old value; 🎛 The \"Skip N item\" in the \"Previous Round\" line of the modifier page will reflect this situation. If you want to continue freezing, delete the rule and click 🔒 again after changing the field back to a single value.\r\n\r\n## 📖 World Info Mode (Lorebook)\r\n\r\n**Talk** about the World Info (what is written in it, which setting is it, whether there are any contradictions, how to expand it), or let it **change** the World Info directly. After entering, there is a toolbar below the title:\r\n\r\n- **Book selection**: The default is \"all currently activated World Infos\", you can also **check one or several books** (supports multiple selections).\r\n- **Item Selector**: The entire book is sent by default, and can be expanded and used to select only a few items to send to the Oracle (with shortcut keys such as filter + select all / blue light only / green light only, **👁 content preview** can display a one-line summary for each item).\r\n- **🪄 Smart Selection (from 1.54.0)**: The 🪄 button on the item selector toolbar - **Use human words to check the instructions** (\"Tick all green light items that talk about war lines\", \"Cancel all those involving emotional scenes\", \"Cancel the entire \"Book of So-and-so\"..., any combination of mechanical conditions and content semantics). AI reads a condensed catalog to make a plan; when he is not sure, he will do a **free keyword search** in the book, or call out the original text of individual items to read carefully (**two rounds at most**, each round is clearly stated in the window, and never spend more money silently). The result will first give you a **pre-check card**: what will be checked/cancelled, why each item, what words it searched for, and whether there are any fake uid it ​​compiled (will be eliminated and marked) - click 【 to apply 】 to really take effect, click 【 to restore 】 and return to the previous check with one click. It only checks and never changes the content of the book; the meaning of the check is exactly the same as manual checking (the entire book is still read when applying changes). It only affects the content sent to AI. When applying, the entire text will still be read, and any edits will take effect as usual. **(1.40.1 onwards) Your check boxes will be remembered according to the book title, and will still be there when refreshing and reopening**, you don’t need to re-check each time; if you check the entire book of a certain book, it will automatically return to the \"send the entire book\" state - so that new entries added to this book in the future will be automatically included, instead of being blocked by the old check boxes. If you want to send only the entire book, click \"Select All\". **(1.58.0 onwards) Live streaming**: If your \"streaming\" setting is turned on, 🪄 you will be in the window while working **reading while writing** AI's original text - what it is thinking about, searching for, and planning are all visible in real time (you won't be dragged back to the bottom when you scroll up while reading); the pre-check card will be issued as usual after writing. With streaming turned off, only the progress line is displayed as before.\r\n\r\nWhen requesting changes, the oracle will explain in Chinese what has been changed, and attach the `<LorebookEdit>` block (**delimited format** instead of JSON, long text will be written as it is in the `<<<content … content>>>` fence without escaping). Four operations: `create` new, `edit` covering the entire line, `patch` (default - \"the first few words || the last few words\" anchor only changes one paragraph), `delete`. Then the **Apply changes to World Info** button appears: write back through `saveWorldInfo` of ST, list the results one by one, and can be **undoed** with one click; the uid/anchor that cannot be found will be **safely skipped and explained**, and will never be written halfway. Anchor point matching is very sensitive to small differences (starting from v1.19.2): small differences in punctuation such as cross-Chinese dashes (——), different quotation marks (\"\"/『』/\"\"/\"), pauses ↔ commas, etc. can all be hit; if it still fails, the prompt will suggest using the anchor points at both ends of the \"start || end\" and try again. The text will be saved as it is, without macro replacement** (`{{user}}`, etc. will remain as they are, and the names will not be written into the book). New entries turn on \"Non-recursive\" by default.\r\n\r\n**Pre-check before application (from 1.53.0). ** When `<LorebookEdit>` is included in the reply, **item-by-item preflight lines** will first appear above the \"Apply changes to World Info\" button: the ones that can be applied are as usual; if the anchor is not found/hit multiple places, **are grayed out on the spot and state the reason**, and you don't need to click Apply to find out; in fact, the entry will automatically change the anchor in another checked book and indicate \"Reanchored to \"Book Title\"\"; when the target is a **resident** entry, there is ⚠ Tip (resident entries are usually your core settings, take a look before changing them). It is equipped with several smarter guards: when the same anchor point hits multiple places in the entry, it no longer silently changes the first one, but skips and prompts to write the anchor point more uniquely; when the patch has already taken effect, it directly informs \"no need to retry\" (no repeated empty attempts); `create` Hitting an entry with the same name automatically switches to editing that entry (no duplicate entries are created); new entries without keywords are automatically set to permanent (otherwise it will never be injected); long anchor points that span multiple paragraphs now hit the entire paragraph (the old version only hits the first paragraph, leaving a semi-replacement residue). In addition, every time the oracle answers, he will take the latest saved text snapshot and the last application result - \"Help me confirm if all the changes have been written in.\" This type of verification is based on the current archive, and no more guessing based on memory.\r\n\r\n**Volume reading (from 1.62.0). ** In addition to the number of items, the summary line of the item selector now also gives the approximate number of token that will be sent out this time** (`条目：全部（449） · 约 88 万 token`), which changes in real time as the check box is checked. **This number will turn red when it exceeds about 10 million token** - remind you that this shot is likely to exceed the context limit of the model and be rejected (World Info mode sends **the entire selected content**, which has nothing to do with SillyTavern's own \"World Info Activation Budget\", and disabled entries are also sent). Being red doesn't **stop you from sending**, it's just a reminder; if you want to lower the number, use the item selector or 🪄 smart selection to select a few items. Figures are estimates and therefore marked \"approximately\".\r\n\r\n> Injecting the entire book into token may be larger. If there are many entries, just use the entry selector to select a few.\r\n\r\n## 🧭 Plot Advisor Mode (Story Advisor) ⚠ Experimental\r\n\r\nTogether with the oracle, you can figure out how to proceed in the plot, and the main chat can be quietly guided with one click. The Oracle will read the dialogue and settings according to the **Context Depth** and **World Info** range you selected in the settings (**Plot Summary** is always read), and based on this, it will find dormant foreshadowing, unrealized clues, and the next step in the character arc, and list the feasible directions as **Plan Card** (`<StoryPlan>`: Goal + Starting Sign + Coherence Point). If you talk about your feelings in normal mode first, switch to 【🧭 and organize the discussion just now into a plan 】 button. **Markdown** (bold/title/list/table) in the reply will be rendered normally (from 1.18.2; from table 1.18.4), the original `<StoryPlan>` block will be displayed as a small block of equal width, and the adopted card will remain the same.\r\n\r\n在卡片上选**强度**（**只铺垫** / **自然推进** / **尽快引爆**）→【开始引导】，方案就作为一条幕后指令注入主聊天（ST 的 `setExtensionPrompt`，深度在「参谋设置」里调，1.77.5 起；模型不听引导就调低，最低 0）。之后**正常 RP 即可**——主线会逐步把剧情推向该方向，且**用户行动永远优先**（你偏离时它跟随）。采用后顶部出现**方案条**（关掉窗口会变成可拖动的「🧭 引导中」悬浮标签），可随时切强度、查看注入原文、或【完成】/【放弃】。方案存在**当前聊天**里，刷新 / 切换聊天都不丢、绝不串台。\r\n\r\n**✏️ Edit injected content (from 1.48). ** **✏️** on the plan bar (it was there when the preview was closed) can completely rewrite the behind-the-scenes instructions injected into the main chat - the details you want to add and the writing methods you want to ban can be directly written in, click 【 to save 】 and it will take effect immediately (refreshing the page is still there). When the \"**Rhythm:**\" line ** remains the same**, the three intensity files above it can be switched as usual (replace only that line, and the rest of the content you wrote will remain unchanged); once you **change or delete** that line, it will be regarded as \"the rhythm has been set by itself\", and the intensity file will be **grayed** (the explanation line will state the reason). If you want to retrieve the automatically generated text, click 【 in the editor to **restore the default** 】 (the current gear is retained). The intensity level is also temporarily grayed out during editing - changing gears will redraw the plan bar, flushing out unsaved words. Customization ** comes and goes with this plan **: 【 completes 】/【 and gives up 】/ will be cleared if you change another plan.\r\n\r\n**Story Arc (Long Lead) ⚠ Experimental. ** Upgrade the single-step plan to **Multi-shot long-term**: First define a **through-line** (what the entire arc is about), and then move it one beat after another. Each transition is made by a background call and the next beat is injected into the main chat until the through-line **really ends**. When creating a new game, fill in the form and select **mode** (**transparent** = you can see every instruction; **blind box** = only the goals given to the player are seen, and the behind-the-scenes intentions are hidden behind blurred spoilers), through lines, road signs, length, **difficulty** (peaceful / normal / harsh, the higher the stakes, the greater the stakes, but \"exit\" can always be reached before irreversible turning), red line. You can 【 exit 】 at any time and the main chat will be restored immediately.\r\n\r\n**1.71.0 also has an arc starting line ✏️**: What has been changed is the injection command of **the current beat**, and the usage is exactly the same as the editing of the single-step plan above (the \"Rhythm:\" line remains the same, the intensity file can be switched as usual, 【 returns to the default 】, the retrieve is automatically generated, the save takes effect immediately, and the refresh is not lost). 【 completed 】/【 and changed the idea. 】 now returns to automatic generation when programming a **new beat** - a new shot and a new command. If you are not satisfied, you can change it again. **Blind box arc** click ✏️ and you will directly **see the behind-the-scenes instructions (including spoilers)**. If you want to preserve the blind box experience, don't click on it; in addition, the editor only changes the injected text itself, and the goals shown to the player and the \"✓ Goal achieved\" judgment **are not affected**.\r\n\r\n> ⚠ The arc requires more models than the single-step solution with token (read the entire history + World Info in every shot), it is recommended to equip with **stronger models** (DeepSeek / Gemini Pro / Opus); streaming, timeout cancellation, 📡 real-time output are all built-in.\r\n\r\n**Sequence guidance (pre-write a whole long line, advance beat by beat) starting from 1.72. ** The single-step plan only guides one goal at a time, and the arc is \"set a general direction, and edit each beat now\"; **sequential guidance** is somewhere in between - you and the staff discuss the entire long-term plot (a school year, a volume, a journey) until it is finalized**, and the staff arranges it into an orderly beat list: each beat has exactly the same specifications as the single-step plan (goal + starting signs + points of convergence), **all laid out and visible, without any hidden content**. Click 【 on the card to start sequence guidance** 】 adopts the entire bar at one time; **regardless of intensity when applying**, the default is \"natural advancement\" beat by beat, and then press the beat adjustment on the plan bar.\r\n\r\nAfter adoption **Only the current beat is guiding the main chat at the same time**. After the performance, click 【**Complete**】 to change to the next beat - **Changing beats is a pure page turning: no model adjustment, no cost token** (the injection instructions for each beat have been written when adopting, and are generated by the same set of logic as the single-step solution, and the guidance quality is exactly the same). ** Starting from 1.75, the guidance command and status line will be merged into your own message before sending it** (you can't see it if you don't change the chat history; what you see in the prompt word viewer is still the way it was before fitting). In this way, whether you use the official DeepSeek, custom transfer, or Claude / Gemini, the model will see the same position - this is the reason for the problems of \"detonating as soon as possible but no response\" and \"drop shot sensor not ringing\" in long chats. The status line is written at the end of the reply. If the upper limit of your reply length (max tokens) is very tight and the model is cut off in the middle of writing, it will be the first to be lost - the drop sensor occasionally does not sound. Check this first. The header of the plan bar shows \"Beat X / Y\", the bar is the target of the current shot + three levels of intensity + ✏️, and the following is the **beat list**: ✓ Completed / ▶ In progress / ○ To be broadcast / ⤫ Skipped, click on any row to expand its target / starting sign / fitting point; ** Each row of the shot to be broadcast has ✏️ With 【 skipping 】** (change the injected content, or leave it unplayed), completed / skipped lines are read-only. ✏️ The rules are exactly the same as the single-step plan and arc (the intensity file can still be switched when the \"Rhythm:\" line remains as it is, 【 restores the default 】 retrieves the automatically generated version, saving takes effect immediately and is not lost after refreshing).\r\n\r\nIf you want to **make major changes** (rearrange, add or reduce shots, change direction), click 【**💬 and ask the staff to change **】: **click it and nothing will be removed** - the current photo often leads to the main chat, just automatically opens the window and returns to the staff room. The staff will first say \"You are currently shooting at X / Y...\" and then continue chatting. After chatting, it will re-list the **remaining shots** to a card for you, and use it = **only replace the part after the current shot**, and the completed/skipped history will not be moved at all (the ✏️ customizations on the replaced shots will also be invalidated - new content for new shots). No. 1: Before the filming started, I asked the staff to change it. The actual effect was to replace the entire line with a new one. If you don’t want the whole thing, just give up 【**】 (you will confirm it first, which will cause greater losses than the single-step solution).\r\n\r\n> ⚠ **Each chat can only have one guidance component at the same time**: Choose one of three options: single-step plan / arc / sequence. Using a sequence will replace the running plan or arc; conversely, if you use a single-step plan or create a new arc when there are still unfinished shots in the sequence, it will be played once for confirmation and then discarded. The status of the sequence (where each shot is performed, the injected text that you have changed) is stored in the current chat, and it will not be lost when refreshing/switching the chat, and the channels will never be lost.\r\n\r\n**🧭 Database linkage (experimental) starting from 1.78. ** This item is only required for those who have installed **SP·Database** and enabled its \"**plot advancement**\" at the same time. The plot advancement of the database will run its own \"planner\" before each sending, and write the plan of how to proceed next in your message - but that planner can't see the guidance of the staff, so they often talk about their own things, and the main model dictates what is written in your message, and the staff seems to have been \"rejected\". Check **Database Linkage (Experimental)** in the \"Advisor Settings\" of the staff bar, and the story oracle will take a look at the planner attached to the **current guide** before the database starts planning, then take it away as it is after planning: **The prompt words sent to the main model are the same byte-for-byte as when only the database is installed**, and your messages, chat records, and World Infos will not be changed word by word. It only takes action when your message is the latest one and is sent normally (not re-rolled/re-swiped/automatically triggered); it will not do anything if it is checked when the database is not installed (the check box will show whether the database has been detected).\r\n> Description: This is a transitional plan that relies on the sequence of events. We have also hooked up a read-only interface (see \"Extended Development Interface\" below), and have suggested to the database author that its planner directly read the staff guidance; once the other party is connected, this check is no longer needed. If the boot text contains the database's own placeholder writing like `$8` or `{{…}}`, the copy attached to the planner will be treated harmlessly (the boot read by the main model will not be affected).\r\n> Advanced (starting from 1.84, off by default): If you instead want the guide to stay in your message and be sent to the main model (heavier weight), there is a line at the top of `index.js` that reads `const ENABLE_DB_BRIDGE_KEEP = false;`, change it to `true` There will be an additional sub-checkbox on the rear staff bar \"Peel off the guide block before sending to the main model\". Uncheck it to keep it. Please know the price first: the guide will be **stored into the chat record** as the database is rewritten (and will be re-sent in each subsequent round as history), the guide posted in your message when sending will not be posted in the entire round due to repetition, and the hidden target of the blind box shooting will appear in your own message. Only recommended for those who are aware of the consequences (from community PR #1, author f1luct).\r\n\r\n**🧭 The next shot is recommended to be from 1.87 (only effective when the sequence boot is in progress). ** Sequence guidance pushes the plot forward beat by beat, but when it's your turn to speak, you may not immediately think of \"how to take this shot.\" Check the **Next shot suggestion** in the \"Advisor Settings\" of the staff bar. When the sequence is running, a small card will appear below the latest reply** in the main chat (writing the number of beats and the goal of this shot):\r\n- Click \"**Generate Suggestions**\" → Oracle sends a request and gives 4~7 candidates: **3 \"I\"** (your own actions/lines), **1~3 characters present** (written as \"Character name:...\", send it to let that character do this), **0~1 \"Time\"** (given only when changing scenes or skipping time). When there is still a change of location, time or relationship between this shot and the end of the text, one of the candidates will have \"the middle step\" written first; **Storyboard/Transition Shot** (the shot title contains \"Storyboard\", \"Transition\", \"Cut to\", \"Perspective Cut\", \"B Line\" and \"Branch Line\"). If the player is not in that scene, it will not be given to \"me\".\r\n- **Click an item = fill in the input box**: If the input box is empty, just put it in; if you have typed something, just follow it with a new line - ** will not overwrite your words, nor will it be sent for you**, just change it and send it again. \"Fill in the entire paragraph\" puts all candidates in rows; \"Regenerate\" changes a batch; you can click \"Stop\" during generation.\r\n- What it reads is: **The original text of the guidance command for this shot** (exactly the same as what the main model received, including the content you changed with ✏️), **Character card and your character** (following the \"with character card\" setting), **the \"green light\" entry in the World Info named by the text or guidance this time** (following the \"World Info\" range setting: off = without; \"custom\" = Only the items you checked will be displayed), and the reply you just finished writing (the last 4000 words will be intercepted by default). The Oracle's own connection is used; when \"Apply my completion defaults\" is checked in the consultant mode and the built-in limit break is selected, it is also applied.\r\n- The result is stored in **Current Chat**: it will still be there after refreshing the page; if you change to swipe, change the reply, or the session is completed/modified, the old candidate will be invalidated and you will return to \"Generate Suggestions\". It is not displayed when the player has already sent the next message (the latest one is your own message). **Only appears during sequence guidance** - Single-step plans, arcs, and no guidance do not have this card.\r\n- In \"**Next Shot Suggestions · More Settings**\": **Automatically generate each new reply** (default off; after turning it on, each reply will cost one more call to API, which will wait for the automatic correction/automatic diagnosis to run before generating), **The maximum number of words that can be intercepted from the latest reply fed to it** (100–20000, default 4000), **option writing method** (additional requirements attached to the request, the default is a common writing method; can be rewritten, \"↺ restore default\", \"✕ clear\" = not attached).\r\n> Source: Community plug-in \"Story Oracle · Next Shot Suggestions\" (author **Cotton Doll**, GitHub: yacovonebeswick-art), merged into the main body with the author's consent; when incorporated, the author's own player character (\"ordinary person\" tone, cold writing style, etc.) was changed to follow your own character and character card. Friends who have installed the **standalone version** plug-in before, please disable it in the extension management - if it is turned on at the same time, two cards will appear under each reply (Oracle will remind you in the settings prompt when it detects it).\r\n\r\n## ✨ Calibration mode (Reply Fixer)\r\n\r\nSpecialized in \"repairing\" **Latest reply from AI**: Clearing out AI's stereotyped clichés, mechanical dialogue, overly precise \"mathematical essay style\", writing magic into science, and procrastination. It can also enforce the character's knowledge boundaries/plot guardrails you set. **Changes will always be applied as a new swipe (reshape)** - the original reply will always be at the \"swipe left\" location; the `<UpdateVariable>` block in the reply will be restored as is, **never breaking the MVU values ​​or status bar**. If the beautification of this card is **an entire webpage** (rendered as an embedded page by SillyTavern Assistant in the main chat), the correction card will switch to **plain text formatting** to display the text, and the HTML source code will no longer be displayed; the beautification will remain the same, and you can see it in the main chat after clicking **[Apply]** (v1.84.1).\r\n\r\nThere is a drop-down at the top of the \"Calibration Settings\" panel, and you can switch to three sets of usage: manual / de-AI flavor / custom:\r\n\r\n- **🖐 Manual** - Directly in the input box **use human words to change what you want to change** (\"Write the spoken word in this dialogue\" \"Delete this sentence\"). Only the latest one is moved, and only the part you named is changed, and the rest is left unchanged - the status bar/panel/graphic markup and other **structural blocks in the reply are also left as they are by default** (unless you want to change the content in the name). **Default simplified context**: Only send this reply + character card, without the previous text/World Info/summary (it is easy to misunderstand the floors to be changed in a weak model with high context, and check them one by one in the panel when necessary). After the correction, you will be given a **correction card**, and then click **[Apply]** if you are satisfied (this will become swipe).\r\n- **🤖 Go to AI flavor** - Specializes in \"Knowing it is written by AI as soon as you read it\": **Check the long-term goals you want to clean up** (5 switches: AI stereotypes / clichés, mechanical dialogue, over-precision, **magic is written as science** (fantasy only, default off), description procrastination / Logbook - the remaining four items are enabled by default), select **Strength** (light calibration by default / fine calibration more thorough + select emphasis according to the model), you can then fill in the **character knowledge boundary/plot guardrail** constraints, set the **exclusion area** (retain = force to keep the automatically unrecognized blocks as they are; discard = delete directly, such as `<thinking>`) - these and the scope / package are collected in the **\"Advanced Settings\"** fold. Two triggers: click **[Remove the AI flavor to the latest reply according to the target]** to run once (**Streaming live broadcast** correction draft, the stop key can interrupt at any time), or check **[Automatically de-flavor the AI flavor for each new reply]** to run in the background (✨ icon dyed gold as a reminder).\r\n- **📋 Custom (v1.77.0)** - The third drop-down level: **Use your own template to process each new reply** (example: the text is automatically translated into Japanese). The template **just writes what needs to be done**, and the output format and retention tags are automatically attached by the oracle; \"each new reply\" in a chat must either run corrections or run a template, choose one of the two. \"**Inherit corrected text recognition**\" is checked: On = only the plot text is processed, status bar/variable blocks, etc. are retained as they are; Off = the entire reply is handed over to the template and the output is replaced as it is (the original text remains swipe 0) - **When both sides of the reserved area/discard area are left blank**, the entire reply is handed over to the template byte by byte as it is. If anything is filled in any area, pick it out according to the area before sending it. In the entire mode, Oracle will additionally require the model to retain all tags and structure blocks as they are, but whether it can be kept depends on the model. For cards with status bar/variable blocks, it is recommended to keep \"Inherit Recognition\" on (it hides the variable blocks, but the package label will still be given to the model when the structure is not recognized); this file has its own retention area/discard area; both sides of the same label should be filled in with retention processing. **Minimum number of words** (the call will not be initiated if the text is shorter than this) is set in the custom panel, **shares the same value with automatic** (the automatic panel has never had this box), change one side and change both sides. For long replies, remember to increase \"Advanced Settings → Correction Output Upper Limit\": For templates like Japan-China Mirror that will double the Character count, DeepSeek is about 1.4 per word, token, Claude is about 2.0, token - the floor of 4096 is at 2-3 A normal reply with a thousand words will be truncated (the truncation will be blocked and will not fall into swipe). 8 The Claude type for a thousand-word floor requires more than 15k. Example template: `把 <text_to_transform> 里的叙事正文逐句完整翻译成自然的日文；对白引号用「」；{{user}} 与 {{char}} 的名字按原文保留。`\r\n\r\n  **📦 Built-in examples (just in the template drop-down list)** - There are two built-in examples in the drop-down list (with \"**(Example)**\" after the name, listed in the \"Built-in Examples\" group at the bottom). You can use it by selecting it; if you make changes and click Save, it will be saved as your own, and the examples themselves will not change. The two versions are \"**More vivid dialogue + detached narration (example)**\" (change the dialogue to make it look like a living person speaking, clean up the clichés in the narration, and keep the characters/events/names unchanged) and \"**Beautify the layout·Dialogue bubbles (example)**\" (not change a single word, just arrange each line of dialogue into a small bubble, and add light separation). Both copies have been run on DeepSeek V4 Pro and Gemini 3.1 Pro for many rounds; **Two known boundaries**: ① When the dialogue template encounters a card that does not have the \"name:\" prefix and relies on narrative to explain who is speaking**, DeepSeek basically only does the \"narration flavor removal\" half, and the words in the quotation marks remain unchanged (Gemini (Do both halves); ② When the typesetting template encounters `“…”某某说，“…”`, which is an action sentence sandwiched between two quotation marks, DeepSeek will \"repair\" the comma in the middle into a period and delete \"so-and-so said,\" (Gemini is normal). These are all model habits, just change the model.\r\n\r\n  **How to write a template** (these two copies are written according to these items):\r\n\r\n  - Write \"**What will it look like after the change**\", don't write \"What to do first and then what to do\"; there is no need to write the output format, tags, and anchors - Oracle will add them by itself.\r\n  - Every sentence must match a **really going to go wrong**; don’t write if you haven’t had any problems before.\r\n  - Writing the things you want to keep in a **visible form** (\"Still start the line with the name plus a colon\" \"Still the comma period\") is more effective than writing the principle (\"Don't change it\").\r\n  - **Only give one skeleton** for one layout, don't give multiple ones; the skeleton itself should be readable in both light and dark themes (translucent gray, no text color).\r\n  - **Don't** paste example text or \"ideal output\" into the template, **Don't name the concepts** - the model will copy them into the text as is.\r\n  - Different models will fill in the blanks in different directions (some like to compress and lose proper names; some just \"fix\" punctuation); **If the template cannot be changed, just change the model or accept it**. Don't over-code each sentence - sentences written specifically for a certain company often make it more biased.\r\n  - For templates that only add tags and do not change words, the output is longer than the original text (the `style` attribute of the bubble is enough), otherwise the \"no processing\" gate will block the manuscript.\r\n  - 300–600 characters are sufficient; the two built-in examples are 451 characters and 593 characters.\r\n\r\n  **🌐 Template Square (v1.86.0)** - The button on the far right of the template row:\r\n\r\n  > **Currently 🌐 the square is temporarily closed** (the button is not displayed for the time being), and \"one-click submission\" has been cancelled. **📤 Sharing** is available as usual: copy the sharing text and send it to the template sharing channel of Oracle Discord.\r\n\r\n  - **🌐 Square** (paused): The templates shared by everyone and reviewed by the author are all here. On it, you can filter by **tag** and **search** by name/author/description; each entry contains the version number, author (no signature indicates \"anonymous\") and the tested model. \"**Preview**\" expands the full text, \"**Download**\" saves it as your own template and selects it directly (if it has the same name as your existing template, it will automatically be changed to \"Name (2)\"). If the template you are changing has not been saved, you will be asked if you want to abandon the changes before downloading. The author has released a new version, and the button will change to \"**There is a new version**\". You can choose to **overwrite the local copy** or **save another copy**. When the square cannot be connected, the last offline copy saved will be displayed first.\r\n  - **📤 Share**: First select **your own saved** template in the drop-down list (built-in examples and unsaved changes cannot be shared, a reason will be prompted when clicking), then fill in the author (optional), one-sentence description, 1–3 tags, tested models, click \"**Copy Share Text**\", and send the copied content to the template sharing channel of Oracle Discord. The templates shared are **public** and can be used by anyone. When the square is open, you can check \"This is an update to the shared template\" for the improved shared template and select the original one.\r\n  - The text in the square will only be displayed as ordinary text. The downloaded template will not execute any code, and will not touch your chat, World Info and variables.\r\n\r\n> 💰 The automatic mode defaults to only sending the reply text + target, and comes with **banned word pre-screening + lower word limit** - the reply is clean/too short and **does not initiate a call** at all, and will not burn token for each reply.\r\n\r\nAfter the modification is completed, it will be **applied as the new swipe** and leave a record in the side chat, with **[Use the original text]** (cross back to the original) / **[See changes]** (verb by word comparison). The configuration can be saved according to the current chat, and can also be saved as a named package (such as \"Hardcore Western Fantasy\") for reuse with one click.\r\n\r\n> 🔀 **v1.77.0 behavior change**: **Switching chats will no longer cancel the correction/template processing in progress** - the result that has been purchased will be temporarily saved first, and will be automatically landed when you **return to that chat** (returning within half an hour will count, and it will be lost if it times out or refreshes the page; the results of up to 8 chats can be temporarily saved at the same time). In the past, cutting away meant that the entire round was wasted and money was wasted. 🩺 Automatic diagnosis and 🎛 variable modifiers are still disabled when switching chats (they write the variable status of the current chat).\r\n\r\n> 🎯 **Automatic recognition (from v1.17.16, v1.18.3 plus \"detection receipt\")**: Automatic mode only changes the **text** - which package label the text is in (`<content>`, `<gametxt>`, `<正文>`...) will be **automatically recognized and remembered by chat**, the status bar inside and outside the text / options / panel / Structural blocks such as Tusheng instructions **do not send the model and keep them as they are**; if you are not sure about the card, it will **ask you once** (click \"✋ Require Confirmation\" on the panel). **Common formats are available out of the box**; for cards with special formats, open \"Advanced Settings\" to see the **Detection Receipt** (the blocks actually recognized in this article). If you admit the error, click and fix it into the reserved area - you are also welcome to send the original reply to **Discord private message @Prince**, and it will be added to the test set for repair. **Judgment preview line** will tell you \"how this reply will be processed\" at any time; your **hand-filled** tags will not be automatically overwritten; if the configuration is messed up, \"**Restore recommended settings**\" can be restored with one click (the confirmed text form will also be cleared).\r\n\r\n## 🎭 Character Workshop Mode (Character Builder)\r\n\r\nA few chats with the oracle can polish a character from scratch into a complete setting - write an **NPC** entry in the World Info, or write **your own character** into an instruction manual for AI to \"read\" (complete the current Persona / save the new Persona). Like other modes, **do not touch the main chat**; the only output is only actually placed in the last step of **writing** and can be **undone** at any time.\r\n\r\n> ✅ **User character (Persona) goal has returned (v1.76.0)**: The character card is for AI to \"act\", and the user information is for AI to \"read\" - so the user character follows a **special set of interview and forging templates** (behavior translation manual style: each line is either a hard fact or \"TA \"What to do = what does it mean\" translation, the lines only include the original sentences that you actually typed in the conversation record), not the same as NPC.\r\n\r\n- **Target drop-down**: Choose one of the three - **NPC World Info Entry** / **User Role·Talk** (AI will also act and speak for your character, choose it for \"AI plays {{user}} at the same time\") / **User Role·No Talk** (AI only responds to you, never acts for you). Each of the two user roles has its own chapter chip and an independent interview room. When switching targets, you can change rooms without interlocking with each other. When selecting NPC, whether it is a brand new NPC, a modification of an existing entry, or a character that has appeared in the plot but has not been written into the book, the **Interviewer** will ask you in the chat to confirm.\r\n- **The draft contains**: a row of checkable chapters chip to decide what content to write this time - **checked = sent to the forging process, unchecked chapters will be physically deleted from the forging prompts** (the interviewer will not ask, the forging will not write, and will not write more \"conveniently\", what you see is what you get). Default on: Basic information/Appearance characteristics/Background experience/Interpersonal relationships/Character portrait/Speech style/Target motivation/Deep personality/Anti-misreading tips; Default off: Weaknesses and flaws/Abilities and skills (arranged at the end of ordinary chapters), and the **Advanced three items** with **dashed line** at the end: multiple faces/contrast between words and deeds/key metaphors (there is a line of \"Simple/comedy adjustment roles left blank\" prompt before the check). On the desktop, hover the mouse over chip to read the description; on the mobile phone, click **\"?\"** next to \"Draft Includes\" to see the complete legend (there are three advanced selection guides at the top).\r\n- **Context**: World Info multi-selection + entry selector (same mechanism as World Info mode) - **Character entries are usually green light** (keyword trigger). To edit or refer to an existing character, you must **check the book it is in first**, otherwise Forging cannot read it; adjust the context depth (number + \"All\" check) until you can see the position where the character appears (it is more expensive to open \"All\" in long chat token); \"Bring 📜 Plot summary\"; \"Bring status bar data\" (useful when there are numerical character settings in the world); \"**Keyword trigger World Info**\" (default off, v1.31.0) - run an extra ST keyword scan after a meeting, and feed the setting items (blue light + hit green light) **mentioned** in the main chat/interview side chat as a reference to the interviewer and the forger, **checked items will not be fed repeatedly**, the book you checked / The entry remains the sole authority. **By default (the book that has not been manually checked in the item selector) only feeds it the current 【-enabled 】 entries** - disabled items are displayed as unchecked in the list and will not be sent out; after manual checking, only the few items you checked (including disabled ones) will be sent, \"select all\" = even disabled items will be sent (v1.82.0). The summary line of the entry list also contains **Volume Reading** (\"Approximately X token\", if it exceeds 10, a red reminder will appear, and it will only prompt but not intercept).\r\n- **Forging recovery upper limit**: Forging call max_tokens, leave blank = automatic (the lower limit is 16384, starting from v1.29.0; starting from v1.23.0, it was 12288, and earlier than 8192, about half of the heavy forging in the entire chapter will be truncated by \"Thinking + Drafting\"). If it is still not enough, you can increase it again - but if it exceeds the service provider's single output limit, it will be directly rejected, and if an error is reported, adjust it back. Another note: The giant World Info eats the **input** context (limited by the model context window). To streamline it, it depends on the item selector and context depth. This knob does not cover the input side.\r\n- **Use custom presets**: When checked **Interview Conversation** will use SillyTavern preset you curated in the settings panel (text block retained, RP mark removed); **Forging calls are not affected**, always use the built-in forging process.\r\n- **Automatic streamlining after forging** (v1.30.0, off by default): Automatically run \"✂️ streamlining\" after successful forging. Only triggered when NPC drafts and the manuscript is obviously lengthy (long sentences densely packed); guarded = keep the manuscript as is, with a one-line note explaining the reason. It is recommended to turn it on for strong output models (such as Claude).\r\n- **Full Lines** (v1.34.0, default off): When forging, write the lines as **complete human words spoken in person** - retaining the character's personality and speaking habits. Characters who talk less still talk less, but the sentences they speak are intact. If you feel like forging script lines are too dry, just open it; personality, number of items, and card structure will not be affected.\r\n- **Deep Simplification Constant Serial·Streaming**: \"✂️✂️ Deep Simplification\" 3 sections + surgical orders** are run one by one (no more parallel/serial switches). There is only one request in the sky at any time - it does not hit the concurrent current limit of the public welfare station, and the continuous byte stream of the streaming type can also withstand the proxy that will choke the request. Progress is displayed in bubbles in real time. The internal thinking of v1.35.4's sectioning and surgical orders also adds **one-pass drafting discipline** (the lines are welded as they are): the strong reasoning model that likes repeated deliberation no longer thinks of sections as timeout truncation - this is how the previous occasional \"simplification was not adopted: the N section does not have an effective fence\". The actual measurement probability of this fault has dropped from 1/3 to 0/3, the whole round time is about half.\r\n- **✂️ Simplify the entire draft / ✂️✂️ Deep streamline / Original switching** (v1.30.0, draft card button): Divide the lengthy forging draft into short sentences and delete cross-section repetitions - lines, chapter structure, status lines, images and derived entities are all retained as they are. The whole set of guards is in place, and any single step will automatically return to the original draft. After success, the **\"Original ⇄ Condensed Draft\"** switch button (●marked with the current side) appears on the card. **Writing and revision are subject to the currently displayed version**; when switching back to the **Original** side, the two Simplify buttons are still there - you can change to a different gear and rerun at any time (the rerun will overwrite the old condensed draft); after revising the condensed draft, the two versions will converge to the revised one (the switch button is closed).\r\n\r\n> 💡 chip is the \"volume knob\" of this setting - if it is fully checked, it will display the **protagonist level** complete setting (about 2000 characters) by default. **The last three advanced items (multiple faces/contrast between words and deeds/key metaphors) are off by default** and are checked for characters with **internal layers**; comedy adjustments/pure functions/simple and straightforward characters **just leave them blank**. It is up to you to decide whether it is necessary - checked = must be done, unchecked = must not be done** (it is no longer up to the model to judge whether it is suitable or not); if you check the advanced parts for a simple character, the forging will follow it and forge it out of the complexity it does not have. To make matters worse, NPC, even **Deep Personality** can be turned off, and a refreshing color palette is enough.\r\n\r\nAfter describing the character you want, the interviewer will only ask for objective information that can be answered (appearance, age, gender, identity, character summary...), 2-3 questions at a time, and the things written in your description / checked World Info / chat history will not be asked repeatedly. When you have enough information, a **<Character Brief>** summary card will appear. Click **\"🔨Generate\"** to actually start forging - there will be no calls before.\r\n\r\n> 💰 Forging is a **heavy call**: all the context of your configuration will be read in. First, look in the World Info for **character generation rules** (naming rules, racial restrictions, numerical templates...), and if you find it, follow it as **hard constraints**; the polishing process is completed internally, and you will only see the finished product. A rough estimate is that the output is 2-3 times that of a normal reply. This call only occurs when you click \"Generate\" and is never triggered automatically. The internal thinking of v1.35.3's forging has added the **one-pass drafting discipline** - strong inference models that love repeated deliberation (such as Claude Opus) no longer have to rethink the entire five processes. Forging is obviously faster and more economical (the actual measurement time and output of this type of model are cut in half), and the quality and structure of the finished product remain unchanged.\r\n\r\n> ⚠ **Claude Fable 5 user attention (actual measurement when v1.76.0 was released)**: The forging process requires the model to write thoughts into the `<thinking>` tag. The security layer of Fable 5 will judge this command as \"extract model inference\" and **refuse to answer the entire message** (NPC Like the user's character target, both navy / routera paths are the same, navy appears as \"content filter\") - Forging will get empty recovery. Please change the model to the workshop (Opus / Sonnet / DeepSeek / Gemini are all normal); the interview will not be affected.\r\n\r\n> ⏳ 🔨 Forging and ✂️✂️ Deep streamlining are both **background keep-alive** calls (from v1.35.2 onwards for forging, onwards from deep streamlining v1.36.0): switching to other modes after sending will not interrupt them - the background will run as usual, and the streaming bubble will be automatically connected when you return to the workshop room. After completion, the finished manuscript will be returned to the original room (no interruption notification will be played when you are not present, you will see it when you return to the room). During generation, the send key is displayed as the ⏹ stop key. Clicking it will still abort; **switching chat** or clearing the side chat history of the room will also abort (the result belongs to the old chat and will not be written into the new chat).\r\n\r\nThe draft appears in the resident card at the bottom of the \"Character Workshop\" panel at the top of the window - the closed panel will be automatically expanded when the forging is completed (from v1.19.2; if you want to see it again later, just click on the \"Character Workshop\" title to expand it). Even if you refresh the page, go away and come back, it will still be there. Press Chat to save each one. Little skaters who are finishing the draft can be saved automatically (starting from v1.19.2): if they miss the closing tag or close it with a few more `>`s, they will no longer lose the draft in vain; if they forget to close the thinking block, the finished draft will not be swallowed up as \"(empty reply)\". If you want to change, just say where you want to change - Oracle will first quote the original sentence in normal text and give replacement suggestions to ask for your confirmation; confirm everything and you say \"changed\" before outputting the only patch, which will be accurately inserted into the draft word for word at once, and will only contain the changes you have confirmed (it will not rewrite the entire article, nor will it include areas that were not changed by it). Patch anchoring is as solid as the World Info patch - crossing \"——\", different quote styles, and small differences in punctuation can all hit. If you are satisfied, click **\"Write\"**; **\"🔨 Re-forge\"** to completely overturn it; **\"Abandon Draft\"** to clear it directly.\r\n\r\nWriting will create a new entry in the target World Info (or overwrite an existing entry you selected), and automatically assign 3-5 trigger keywords; the user character target will be written into the description of the current Persona (to improve the current character) or save as a new Persona (default avatar, which can be changed in the Persona panel), which can also be revoked with one click.\r\n\r\n> ⚠ **Undo is only valid in this session** - Refreshing the page, switching chats, after revisions take effect (revisions are included in drafts), or clicking \"Reforge\" will invalidate the last undo written. Check it as soon as possible after writing it, and cancel it as soon as possible if it is not correct.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Side chat history and operation summary\r\n\r\n- **Side chat history is persisted by chat**: Each chat saves its own copy, and it will not be lost when you close the window/refresh/cut away and come back; only click the title bar 🗑 **Clear** to clear the current chat.\r\n- **Independent side chat room for each mode (1.28.0)**: normal chat/diagnosis/World Info/advisor/correction Five modes **Each saves a copy of the side chat history**, switching modes will be replaced by the mode's own records - the chat in the normal chat will not be mixed into the diagnosis, and vice versa; each copy is persisted as a chat and survives across refreshes. There is a line \"This mode is saved independently\" at the top of the records in non-normal modes. When entering **Staff**, if there are already discussions in the normal chat, a one-click \"**Import discussions in normal chat and organize them into plans**\" button will appear, which will move the chat just now into the staff room and organize it into plan cards for you (the staff will always read through the real main chat plot, this button just brings the discussions in the side chat along with it).\r\n- **Run Summary (📜, in the \"⋯ More\" menu)**: Write the key background of the plot as a summary, save it in the current chat, and then insert it into the recent conversation **directly in front** of the normal chat and consultant mode and feed it to the oracle - long RP to supplement the global background. It is not included in the diagnostic mode; it is also included in the World Info mode when \"Also bring the latest plot dialogue\" is checked (from 1.46.0).\r\n\r\n## Dialog operations\r\n\r\nMove the mouse over any message, and a small button will appear in the corner of the bubble: **Your message** can be ✎ edited (save and regenerated) / 🗑 deleted; **Oracle's reply** can be ↻ regenerated / 🗑 deleted. A confirmation box will pop up before deletion (starting from 1.22; when deleting a question, if it is followed by an oracle reply, you will be prompted to delete it together; if there is an error bubble, delete it directly without disturbing). **When the sending fails** (for example, the shared key is blocked by `429`), a permanent **↻Retry** will be displayed on the error bubble. You can resend with one click without having to type again (especially convenient for mobile phones). **Whether Enter is sent or line wrapped, follow the pub's \"User Settings → Press Enter to send\" (from 1.85.1)**: Default \"Auto (PC)\" = Enter sent on the computer, Shift+Enter line wrapped, Enter on the mobile phone Wrap a new line and click the send button to send; if you want to send Enter directly on your mobile phone, change it to \"enabled\"; if you want to send it on a computer using just the button, change it to \"disabled\".Pressing Enter to confirm an IME composition does not accidentally send the message.\r\n\r\n**📥 Export / 📤 Import dialogue (1.60.0 export, 1.61.0 import + transpose). **Have a great time chatting and want to save some files? **The operation row under the Oracle reply bubble** (copy/delete row) has two small buttons: **📥 Export** and **📤 Import**: Export saves the Q&A on the current page as a **Markdown file** and downloads it locally (【, I 】/【, Oracle 】, round-by-round typesetting, `<StoryPlan>` in staff mode The original text of the card is retained; system records are not incorporated; the file name contains the mode, chat name and time); importing will restore the previously exported file** to a conversation that can continue to be chatted** - connected to the end of the current page and will never overwrite the existing content (the page will be confirmed first if it is not empty). The imported dialogue oracle will also be remembered and the chat can continue. When there are no bubbles on the blank page, the \"📤 Import Conversation\" entrance will appear on the page. Only available in **Normal Chat** and **Plot Advisor**. Unrecognized file sections will clearly indicate how many sections have been skipped, and the content will never be lost quietly.\r\n\r\n## Advanced options\r\n\r\n- **Use the completion default as the source of system prompt words. ** In addition to writing prompt words directly, you can also let the oracle ** follow a certain Chat Completion preset structure**: a ** selection list** will pop up when you select it for the first time. You can decide whether to keep it block by block and drag and sort (story/world/personality categories are retained by default, and output blocks such as chain of thought/number of words/style of writing are removed by default). After saving, **freeze into a snapshot** (changing the original default will not affect this). Clicking [↺Reselect] will open according to your last saved check and order, and you can continue to change it; if you want to pick the latest content from the original default, click \"Reset Default\" in the list. **Faithfully reproduce** the prompt word structure of the main chat when sending (each slot is filled in place, the role of each block is retained, macros are parsed in real time, and `setvar` will heal itself and not pollute the main chat). **When the default is selected, the personality and the system prompt text box below will be disabled. ** When \"Apply Plot Rules\" is turned on, Oracle will render its own replies like the main chat (normal display such as status bar beautification).\r\n- **Speaking personality. ** Ordinary / Izumi Nana / Beatrice / Butterfly Ninja Give the Oracle a speaking tone (select \"Normal\" = no superposition). **Off by default when selecting preset** to avoid conflicts. In the Staff/World Info mode, only the tone of the personality is changed, and it does not affect the format of the plan block or the text of the written entry. Diagnostic mode is not in effect.\r\n- **Customized personality (1.39.0). ** Next to the drop-down ✎ Open the editor: give a name and write a paragraph \"How does this personality speak\" (personality, attitude, mantra - responsibility rules such as \"Analysis must be accurate, know everything\" are provided by the oracle, no need to write), save it and appear in the \"── Custom ──\" group of the drop-down, and it will take effect in the normal / staff / World Info mode like the built-in personality (the diagnosis mode also does not take effect). Just a rough idea? Click \"✨ AI Help me improve\" to let the currently connected model expand a few words into a complete description (with sample dialogue attached). If you are not satisfied, you can \"↩ Undo\". Maximum 20.\r\n- **Customize the prompt words for each mode. ** There is a mode drop-down in the settings to view/overwrite the built-in prompt words for the **Diagnosis**, **World Info** and **Plot Advisor** (single-step solution, starting from 1.17.7) modes (it will automatically improve with updates if it is not changed, freeze if it is changed, [↺ reset to default] to restore). The prompt words for arc compilation and isolong lines are not open.\r\n- **Read the background world of other extensions. ** After checking \"Comes with \"World Engine\" background world state\" (on by default), Oracle will read the behind-the-scenes world state maintained by **World Engine / World Engine** in normal chat and consultant modes (events brewing, power trends...), so you can ask \"what is happening outside.\" Currently it only adapts to the world engine; there is no overhead when the relevant extension is not recognized.\r\n- **Read the historical plot summary of BaiBai Book (1.33.0, 1.46.0 extended access). ** If you are using **BaiBai Book (ST-BaiBai-Book)** memory expansion: it will hide the old floors outside the window and leave only a summary for the main model - and Oracle does not read hidden floors by default, which is equivalent to \"only the last few dozen floors are visible\". After checking \"Included with \"Historical Plot Summary of \"Bai Bao Shu\"\"\" (default off), Oracle will insert the **Hidden Old Building Summary** (with \"Yesterday/Three Days Ago\" relative time annotation) of Bai Bao Shu before the conversation record in normal chat and consultant modes - you can also answer questions about old things in front of the 300th floor; **Correction / Workshop ** will also be included when \"Bring plot summary\" is checked; **World Info Mode** will be included when \"Also bring recent plot dialogue\" is checked (the running summary will also be brought along at this time); **Registered plug-in mode/second creation** (such as the outline version) will also be automatically included when reading story records through the interface. Compatible with all connection methods and preset paths. The diagnostic mode is intentionally not accepted (neither summary nor summary enters the diagnosis - the audit is subject to stat_data). Be careful to keep \"Read Hidden Floors\" turned off (otherwise the original text and summary will be fed twice); there is no overhead if it is checked when BaiBai Book is not installed.\r\n- **Read the plot summary memory of Xiaobai X (1.50.0). ** If you are using the \"plot summary\" of **LittleWhiteBox (Xiaobai X)**: It suppresses the early plot into memory and only feeds it to the main model when the main chat is generated - the oracle cannot be read at ordinary times. After checking \"Comes with plot summary of \"Xiaobai X\"\" (default off), Oracle will secretly write down the summary when the main chat is generated, and then watch it together in the background of General / Staff / World Info / Correction / Workshop, so you can answer questions about the early plot. Remember to reopen SillyTavern (store it in this chat); ask as soon as you install it, and if it has not yet been generated, you will get a copy and put it on the table. Diagnostic mode is intentionally not connected; there is no overhead if it is checked when Xiaobai X is not installed/opened.\r\n- **Mechanism block/thought chain is automatically hidden. **Normal/Advisor mode automatically strips reply embedded `<UpdateVariable>` delta blocks and leaked `<think>` thought chains from display and history (diagnostic mode retains them - reading them is its job).\r\n\r\n## Interface\r\n\r\n- When the dialogue is empty, there is **Example question chip** in the center of the window. Click to fill in the input box (one set for each mode).\r\n- Full keyboard available + screen reading support, respecting the system's \"reduce dynamic effects\"; the touch target on the mobile terminal is larger.\r\n- **The configuration bar** of each mode (Diagnosis / World Info / Calibration / Workshop / **Advisor**) can be folded entirely (default folding on mobile phones, limited to half screen height); destructive operations pop up the ST themed confirmation box. (Staff column can also be discounted starting from 1.20.)\r\n- Message operation buttons (Copy/Rebirth/Edit/Delete) are arranged by default at the bottom of the bubble and displayed on mouse hover (from 1.20 onwards); the settings panel will be **automatically collapsed** when switching modes.\r\n- **Interruption confirmation of switching mode (1.36.0)**: When there is a reply being generated, click the other mode button / ⋯ menu \"General Chat\" / Workshop creation target drop-down, a confirmation box will pop up first - the switch will **abort and discard** this unfinished reply, cut it after confirmation, cancel it and leave it in place. Forging and deep streamlining are background keepalive calls and mode switching without interruption, so this box will not pop up.\r\n- Switch in the \"Interface\" settings (from 1.20 onwards): Move the ⋯ menu tool button ** to the title bar ** (save one click, default is off, ⋯ menu is still there; 1.37.1, when the window does not fit, the button **automatically wraps** to the second line - previously on the mobile phone, the upper right corner ✕ would be squeezed out of the window and could not be pressed). (The old \"Developer·Console Print Prompt Word\" switch has been removed in 1.37.2 - it is a legacy of the early second-generation debugging, and is completely duplicated with the \"Debug Prompt Word\" panel in the ⋯ menu.)\r\n- **Automatically close the window when you click on it (1.48 onwards, off by default)**: After checking it in the \"Interface\" settings, click anywhere else on SillyTavern page (text, input box, etc.) to close the oracle window**. Clicking inside the window, plan floating bar, 📡 real-time output, pop-up window/prompt bar in SillyTavern, magic wand menu, 🌙 and ✂️ shortcut buttons are not counted outside the window; **word selection and scrolling will not be accidentally triggered (the selection process for segment correction is still available). Collapse only hides - modes, side chats, and plans are all retained, and everything remains the same when opened again with the wand or 🌙. 1.48.1 has fixed the issue where the **window color selection \"Dark/Light\" is not accepted when clicking anywhere**; in addition, if the browser is installed with **uBlock Origin** and other interception extensions and there is no response when checked, please turn off interception for the pub address (actually tested it will block this type of click monitoring).\r\n- Exiting the sub-mode will return you to the mode you were in before entering, rather than returning to normal chat.\r\n- **Move/Resize**: Drag the title bar to move, drag the lower right corner grip to zoom (both mouse and touch screen support); the position and size are remembered and automatically limited to the screen.\r\n- **🖥 Full-screen reading (1.51.0)**: Click the full-screen icon in the title bar (on the left side of ✕), and the window will **fill the screen**; click again or press **Esc** to exit and return to the floating window (position/size remains unchanged). Suitable for reading long conversations on mobile phones. Pure display switching, refresh the page and return to the floating window.\r\n\r\n## Extended development interface (Hook API · For second-time entrepreneurs/plug-in authors)\r\n\r\nWant to add your own mode to Story Oracle, but don’t want to copy the code every time it is updated? Starting from **1.21.0**, Story Oracle hangs out a **versioned stable interface** `window.StoryOracleAPI` (plus the `story-oracle-ready` event) on the page. Your plug-in only needs to install its own file and listen to this interface - there is no need to package the story oracle, and the main update (as long as the main version number remains unchanged) will not interrupt you.\r\n\r\n- **Preferred `registerMode(spec)`**: Declare a mode (icon/title/input box placeholder/setting bar/`onSend`) - DOM, rendering and model calling are all the responsibility of the main body, you only write \"what to think about this mode\".\r\n- There are also: `addMessageAction()` (hang button for each reply), `updateReply()` (rewrite and persist a reply), `api.context.*` (character card / World Info / dialogue record read-only builder, same source as the built-in mode), escape valve `api.run()` + `api.appendReply()` (used when onSend cannot be covered). Use `api.isCompatible(1)` as the version gate; the restored original model output is stored in `.so-content` of `data-so-raw`, making it easy to read custom tags.\r\n- **Read-only boot snapshot `api.guidance.getActive()`** (since 1.78): Returns the current chat **Adopted staff boot** - `null` or a copy `{ schemaVersion: 1, chatId, revision, kind: 'plan'|'seq'|'arc', directive, intensity }` (`directive` is the text injected into the main chat). It will only be released after the boot registration is successful; if the user does not check \"Database Linkage\", the chat identity does not match, and there is currently no boot, it will be `null`. For \"planning\" extensions (such as the plot advancement of SP·Database), please read `directive` before assembling your own prompt words - please add `directive` as **literal text** and do not go through the placeholder/template channel. No event is sent, no writing is accepted; `api.version` is still 1, just use `typeof api.guidance?.getActive === 'function'` detection capability.\r\n- **Completely open escape valve `api.unsafe.eval(code)`** (from 1.22): Evaluation within the scope of the Story Oracle** module - any internal top-level functions and states (including those added in the future) can be directly read/rewritten, and the plug-in side can be completely self-service without the need for item-by-item docking. ⚠ **Informal interface**: Not included in the version contract, without any compatibility commitments. After the main body is updated, it will become invalid/changed by the plug-in side. A prompt will be displayed on the console when calling for the first time. When troubleshooting anomalies, please disable the relevant plug-ins before retesting. The above formal interface is still preferred for daily use.\r\n- **Example plug-in that can be copied directly**: `data/default-user/extensions/so-example-plugin/` (story oracle is not packaged, only the listening interface). For complete interface documentation, see the repository `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-05-story-oracle-hook-api-design.md`.\r\n"
+}
